{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011y9NzxhfJcBbThGiSjtinx","type":"tool_result","content":"FRONTIER (expansive depth)\nCurrent node: F-1-001 at depth 1 of 3, scope .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs, .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/overlay-engine-follow-up.test.cjs, .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/overlay-engine-strict-writes.test.cjs. Review dimension for this node: correctness.\nSet this iteration record's \"focus\" to \"Frontier node F-1-001: correctness\" and add \"frontierNodeId\":\"F-1-001\" to it, so the run can tell which node this iteration worked.\nYou may append up to 6 `frontier_proposal` rows to this iteration's delta with \"parentId\":\"F-1-001\", one per sub-target your evidence opened inside this node. Each row needs \"question\" (what to review), \"scope\" (paths inside the review target) and \"evidence\". The admission step prunes duplicates, anything outside the review target, anything past the depth or fan-out caps, and any budget above one the parent recorded. Never write review/frontier-nodes.jsonl or a coverage surface yourself.    6707 .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs\n    2116 .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/overlay-engine-follow-up.test.cjs\n     986 .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/overlay-engine-strict-writes.test.cjs\n    9809 total\n3aab896957e fix(doctor): roll back failed relayouts and refuse sibling folders outside git\n063daaee2c1 merge(doctor): bring in the sibling overlay folder and the framework/root layout\n5913aebc267 feat(doctor): lay overlay sources out under framework/ and root/\n8254108ad7e fix(doctor): pin the battery's private server to loopback\nbe87565aafa refactor(opencode-plugins): rename the plugin builder to definePlugin\nd2d2e839456 feat(doctor): let the overlay engine use a sibling overlay folder\na793f3ad733 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into worktrees/477-opencode-v1-removal\naf87a2aa13a docs(cli-opencode): describe OpenCode 2 as the only supported version\nba9720f2f08 refactor(cli-opencode): drop OpenCode 1 support from dispatch, loop and plugin code\n62e9beb3e25 fix(doctor): read a hub's canaries, commands and guards from its own repository\n8437023303e test(commands): cover the AGENTS.md backup path outside the source repo\n562c0ae0fa2 feat(commands): let a marked-section overlay land before a named line\n42://   node overlay-engine.cjs apply --relayout [--root <tree>]\n49://     folder stays for --rollback), 2 on a refusal before any write or an error.\n50://   node overlay-engine.cjs repin --rollback <run-id> [--root <tree>] [--json]\n95:const RELAYOUT_RUNS_FOLDER = 'relayout-runs';\n98:const REPIN_VALUE_FLAGS = ['upstream', 'to', 'stage', 'rollback'];\n106:  '       node overlay-engine.cjs apply [--capture <path> | --adopt <path> | --relayout] [--root <tree>]',\n110:  '       node overlay-engine.cjs repin --rollback <run-id> [--root <tree>] [--json]',\n3689:  // Relayout refuses a move into root/skilled, so each line, and the count of the\n3695:      : `run ${ENGINE_COMMAND} apply --relayout`;\n3703:      ? `; run ${ENGINE_COMMAND} apply --relayout`\n3706:        : `; run ${ENGINE_COMMAND} apply --relayout for ${movable}, and change the destination or remove the ` +\n4224://   3. Every failure after the backup names the run that --rollback restores.\n4580:function rollbackCommand(ctx, runId) {\n4582:  return `rollback: ${ENGINE_COMMAND} repin --rollback ${runId}${root}`;\n4586:// by the backup or the rollback: its bytes live at the link's target, and the\n4615: * the regenerate steps write afterwards, so a rollback also restores those.\n4624:function writeBackup(ctx, manifest, analysis, touched, runDir, meta) {\n4630:  // path can collide with them and a rollback restores them against that folder.\n4678:  // Only the tree records the folders a missing path would need: a rollback\n5163:      const backup = writeBackup(ctx, manifest, analysis, touched, runDir, {\n5176:    if (!job.isStage && !isClean) console.log(rollbackCommand(ctx, runId));\n5323:function rollbackUnderLock(ctx, runDir, backup) {\n5397:function rollbackRun(ctx, runId) {\n5406:  return withLock(ctx, 'overlay-engine repin rollback', () => rollbackUnderLock(ctx, runDir, backup));\n5410: * Run a re-pin or a rollback, collecting every printed line for the report.\n5413: * @param {{upstream?: string, to?: string, stage?: string|null, rollback?: string|null, isJson?: boolean}} options\n5419:    mode: options.rollback ? 'rollback' : (options.stage ? 'stage' : 'live'),\n5420:    runId: options.rollback || null,\n5440:    code = options.rollback ? rollbackRun(ctx, options.rollback) : repinRun(ctx, options, report);\n6190:function planRelayout(ctx, groups) {\n6293:function relayoutLinkTargets(ctx, moves, manifest) {\n6311: * Build the whole manifest text a relayout writes, without writing it. Every\n6317: * @param {object[]} linkEdits Changes from relayoutLinkTargets.\n6320:function planRelayoutManifest(ctx, fieldEdits, linkEdits) {\n6361: * Write the manifest text a relayout planned, once every copy has moved.\n6363: * @param {string|null} text Text from planRelayoutManifest.\n6365:function writeRelayoutManifest(ctx, text) {\n6371: * Point every live link whose target a relayout moved at the new path.\n6378: *   relayoutLinkTargets.\n6380: *   a rollback re-points a link even when writing the new one failed.\n6382:function retargetRelayoutLink(ctx, change, retargeted) {\n6403:function missingRelayoutParents(root, filePath) {\n6413: * Undo every step a failed relayout completed, newest first. A step that cannot\n6420:function rollbackRelayout(ctx, done) {\n6455:function relayoutUnderLock(ctx, manifest) {\n6461:  const plan = planRelayout(ctx, groups);\n6478:  const linkEdits = relayoutLinkTargets(ctx, plan.moves, manifest);\n6484:    manifestText = planRelayoutManifest(ctx, fieldEdits, linkEdits);\n6517:      done.createdDirs.push(...missingRelayoutParents(ctx.overlayRoot, move.to.absolute));\n6524:    writeRelayoutManifest(ctx, manifestText);\n6528:      retargetRelayoutLink(ctx, change, done.links);\n6531:    const cause = `error: relayout failed while ${step}: ${error.message}`;\n6532:    const restoreFailure = rollbackRelayout(ctx, done);\n6542:      // The rollback already put every copy back, so only the leftover backup\n6552:  // Emptied folders are pruned only once nothing can fail, so a rollback never\n6566:function commandRelayout(ctx) {\n6567:  return withLock(ctx, 'overlay-engine relayout', () => relayoutUnderLock(ctx, loadManifest(ctx)));\n6581:    command: null, root: null, isJson: false, isAudit: false, isRelayout: false, capture: null, guard: null, adopt: null,\n6582:    upstream: null, to: null, stage: null, rollback: null,\n6609:    if (value === '--relayout') {\n6610:      options.isRelayout = true;\n6623:  if (options.isRelayout && (options.command !== 'apply' || options.capture !== null || options.adopt !== null)) return null;\n6627:  if (options.rollback !== null) return repinFlags.length === 1 ? options : null;\n6657:    if (options.command === 'apply' && options.isRelayout) return commandRelayout(ctx);\n6689:  commandRelayout,","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"faa6b93c-ce84-436d-8875-372fa8efb878","uuid":"59880800-9965-42bd-a8ac-4db4d7134218","timestamp":"2026-11-20T16:35:56.292Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"FRONTIER (expansive depth)\nCurrent node: F-1-001 at depth 1 of 3, scope .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs, .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/overlay-engine-follow-up.test.cjs, .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/overlay-engine-strict-writes.test.cjs. Review dimension for this node: correctness.\nSet this iteration record's \"focus\" to \"Frontier node F-1-001: correctness\" and add \"frontierNodeId\":\"F-1-001\" to it, so the run can tell which node this iteration worked.\nYou may append up to 6 `frontier_proposal` rows to this iteration'