{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChEWRMzDmZUFvtYSHmeo2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017WMbJhaY1ed4igqGm3SAg8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled; Y=.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml; sed -n 1928,1966p $Y; sed -n 1178,1200p $Y; sed -n 1605,1614p $Y","description":"Read admit, convergence, activate steps"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3356,"cache_read_input_tokens":132500,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3356},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"faa6b93c-ce84-436d-8875-372fa8efb878","uuid":"80106864-3c56-45ae-9af1-9ced5dbc76f7","timestamp":"2026-11-20T16:37:59.350Z","request_id":"req_011ChEWRMaAu298iBNHgsYSc","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_017WMbJhaY1ed4igqGm3SAg8":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled; Y=.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml; sed -n 1928,1966p $Y; sed -n 1178,1200p $Y; sed -n 1605,1614p $Y","description":"Read admit, convergence, activate steps"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017WMbJhaY1ed4igqGm3SAg8","type":"tool_result","content":"      step_frontier_admit:\n        action: \"Admit this iteration's review frontier_proposal rows as sub-target nodes before the reducer runs\"\n        enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive'\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        instructions: |\n          The review leaf only proposes; this step decides. Before the command, write a\n          JSON array of strings to {artifact_dir}/frontier-known-texts.json holding every\n          frontier node question already in registry.frontier.nodes and every ruled-out\n          candidate rationale, so a proposal that repeats settled work is pruned as a\n          duplicate. An absent registry gives an empty array. The helper runs the six\n          admission checks in order and writes only node-store rows: a review run queues\n          its nodes from that store alone, with no separate question queue to append.\n        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs admit --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --iteration \"{current_iteration}\" --input \"{state_paths.delta_pattern with NNN = current_iteration}\" --known-texts \"{artifact_dir}/frontier-known-texts.json\"'\n        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n        outputs:\n          - frontier_admit_json: \"The JSON line the command prints: admitted node ids and pruned {nodeId, reason} rows\"\n        on_failure: \"Log the stderr line as a config_warning bookkeeping event and continue to step_reduce_review_state; a failed admission leaves the frontier as it was and never blocks the iteration.\"\n\n      step_reduce_review_state:\n        action: \"Run reducer to refresh the canonical findings registry before dashboard generation\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n        command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors\"\n        read:\n          - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n        write:\n          - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.dashboard}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n        failure_modes:\n          malformed_delta: \"skip + warn\"\n          missing_iteration_file: \"no-op + error\"\n          schema_mismatch: \"reject + conflict event\"\n        guarantee: \"Idempotent for identical inputs\"\n        note: \"Reducer outputs findingsRegistry, dashboardMetrics, and strategyUpdates. Re-running the same inputs must be idempotent.\"\n\n      step_graph_upsert:\n      step_check_convergence:\n        action: \"Branch on the stop decision that convergence.cjs computed in step_graph_convergence\"\n        algorithm: |\n          The whole stop decision is computed by convergence.cjs from the review config, the state log, the findings registry and the coverage graph. This step performs no arithmetic and never recomputes or overrides the result.\n          The ratio signals leave out every iteration that is not evidence-bearing (thought, error, timeout), and stuck_count is loop_counters_json.stuckCount.\n          The script applies this fixed order, first match wins:\n          1. if iteration_count >= max_iterations: STOP (maxIterationsReached). This terminal cap is evaluated before every veto, the claim-adjudication veto included; failed legal-stop gates are recorded in stop_decision.blockedBy as synthesis evidence.\n          1a. After 3 consecutive failed iterations (status error or timeout), halt the loop and enter synthesis with stop reason error and partial findings.\n          2. if stuck_count >= config.stuckThreshold: STUCK_RECOVERY\n          3. if convergence_mode == \"off\": skip convergence stop candidates and continue.\n          3a. if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: the vote is telemetry only and the decision is CONTINUE.\n          4. a STOP candidate exists when every dimension is clean (all_dimensions_clean) or the weighted vote passes (composite_converged). The vote cutoffs follow the configured convergenceThreshold. When neither forms and depth_mode == \"expansive\", a run whose frontier holds at least one answered node and none still open or active forms a hard candidate (frontier_drained); a frontier closed with nothing answered forms none. A default run never forms it, and the legal-stop gates below still decide it.\n          4a. if iteration_count < min_iterations: CONTINUE (minIterationsNotReached). min_iterations is config.minIterations, else antiConvergence.minIterations, capped at max_iterations; like research, the floor runs on a candidate before the legal-stop gates.\n          4b. if depth_mode == \"expansive\" and the frontier still holds an open or active node: CONTINUE (frontierOpen). It vetoes every review candidate, all_dimensions_clean included, and never creates a stop.\n          5. the nine legal-stop gates run on a candidate: convergenceGate, dimensionCoverageGate, p0ResolutionGate, evidenceDensityGate, hotspotSaturationGate, claimAdjudicationGate, fixCompletenessReplayGate, candidateCoverageGate, graphlessFallbackGate. Any failed gate gives BLOCKED (blockedStop).\n          6. the graph decision settles the candidate: STOP_ALLOWED keeps STOP, STOP_BLOCKED gives BLOCKED, CONTINUE or a missing graph decision gives CONTINUE.\n          Bind the outputs from stop_decision, where G is stop_decision.gates and I is stop_decision.inputs.review:\n            decision = stop_decision.decision\n            stopReason = stop_decision.stopReason\n            reason = stop_decision.stopReason when it is not null, else stop_decision.reasonDetail\n            reason_detail = stop_decision.reasonDetail\n            weighted_stop_score = stop_decision.weightedStopScore\n            stop_blocked = (stop_decision.decision == \"BLOCKED\")\n      step_frontier_activate:\n        description: \"Mark the active frontier node before the iteration dispatches\"\n        enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive' AND active_frontier_node is non-empty\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        note: \"Marking the node active at this iteration lets the reducer attribute the iteration to the node even when the leaf rewords its focus, so the node's own coverage keeps moving instead of the iteration sliding back onto the global dimension queue.\"\n        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs close --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --node-id \"{active_frontier_node}\" --status active --iteration \"{current_iteration}\"'\n        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n        on_failure: \"Log the stderr line as a config_warning bookkeeping event and continue; the leaf's frontierNodeId and focus marker still attribute the iteration.\"\n\n      step_dispatch_iteration:","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"faa6b93c-ce84-436d-8875-372fa8efb878","uuid":"e3a6bc40-d62e-4703-af82-19de67c6ed63","timestamp":"2026-11-20T16:38:01.853Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"      step_frontier_admit:\n        action: \"Admit this iteration's review frontier_proposal rows as sub-target nodes before the reducer runs\"\n        enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive'\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        instructions: |\n          The review leaf only proposes; this step decides. Before the command, write a\n          JSON array of strings to {artifact_dir}/frontier-known-texts.json holding every\n          frontier node question already in registry.frontier.nodes and every ruled-out\n          candidate rationale, so a proposal that repeats settled work is pruned as a\n          duplicate. An absent registry gives an empty array. The helper runs the six\n          admission checks in order and writes only node-store rows: a review run queues\n          its nodes from that store alone, with no separate question queue to append.\n        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs admit --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --iteration \"{current_iteration}\" --input \"{state_paths.delta_pattern with NNN = current_iteration}\" --known-texts \"{artifact_dir}/frontier-known-texts.json\"'\n        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n        outputs:\n          - frontier_admit_json: \"The JSON line the command prints: admitted node ids and pruned {nodeId, reason} rows\"\n        on_failure: \"Log the stderr line as a config_warning bookkeeping event and continue to step_reduce_review_state; a failed admission leaves the frontier as it was and never blocks the iteration.\"\n\n      step_reduce_review_state:\n        action: \"Run reducer to refresh the canonical findings registry before dashboard generation\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n        command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors\"\n        read:\n          - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n        write:\n          - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.dashboard}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n        failure_modes:\n          malformed_delta: \"skip + warn\"\n          missing_iteration_file: \"no-op + error\"\n          schema_mismatch: \"reject + conflict event\"\n        guarantee: \"Idempotent for identical inputs\"\n        note: \"Reducer outputs findingsRegistry, dashboardMetrics, and strategyUpdates. Re-running the same inputs must be idempotent.\"\n\n      step_graph_upsert:\n      step_check_convergence:\n        action: \"Branch on the stop decision that convergence.cjs computed in step_graph_convergence\"\n        algorithm: |\n          The whole stop decision is computed by convergence.cjs from the review config, the state log, the findings registry and the coverage graph. This step performs no arithmetic and never recomputes or overrides the result.\n          The ratio signals leave out every iteration that is not evidence-bearing (thought, error, timeout), and stuck_count is loop_counters_json.stuckCount.\n          The script applies this fixed order, first match wins:\n          1. if iteration_count >= max_iterations: STOP (maxIterationsReached). This terminal cap is evaluated before every veto, the claim-adjudication veto included; failed legal-stop gates are recorded in stop_decision.blockedBy as synthesis evidence.\n          1a. After 3 consecutive failed iterations (status error or timeout), halt the loop and enter synthesis with stop reason error and partial findings.\n          2. if stuck_count >= config.stuckThreshold: STUCK_RECOVERY\n          3. if convergence_mode == \"off\": skip convergence stop candidates and continue.\n          3a. if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: the vote is telemetry only and the decision is CONTINUE.\n          4. a STOP candidate exists when every dimension is clean (all_dimensions_clean) or the weighted vote passes (composite_converged). The vote cutoffs follow the configured convergenceThreshold. When neither forms and depth_mode == \"expansive\", a run whose frontier holds at least one answered node and none still open or active forms a hard candidate (frontier_drained); a frontier closed with nothing answered forms none. A default run never forms it, and the legal-stop gates below still decide it.\n          4a. if iteration_count < min_iterations: CONTINUE (minIterationsNotReached). min_iterations is config.minIterations, else antiConvergence.minIterations, capped at max_iterations; like research, the floor runs on a candidate before the legal-stop gates.\n          4b. if depth_mode == \"expansive\" and the frontier still holds an open or active node: CONTINUE (frontierOpen). It vetoes every review candidate, all_dimensions_clean included, and never creates a stop.\n          5. the nine legal-stop gates run on a candidate: convergenceGate, dimensionCoverageGate, p0ResolutionGate, evidenceDensityGate, hotspotSaturationGate, claimAdjudicationGate, fixCompletenessReplayGate, candidateCoverageGate, graphlessFallbackGate. Any failed gate gives BLOCKED (blockedStop).\n          6. the graph decision settles the candidate: STOP_ALLOWED keeps STOP, STOP_BLOCKED gives BLOCKED, CONTINUE or a missing graph decision gives CONTINUE.\n          Bind the outputs from stop_decision, where G is stop_decision.gates and I is stop_decision.inputs.review:\n            decision = stop_decision.decision\n            stopReason = stop_decision.stopReason\n            reason = stop_decision.stopReason when it is not null, else stop_decision.reasonDetail\n            reason_detail = stop_decision.reasonDetail\n            weighted_stop_score = stop_decision.weightedStopScore\n            stop_blocked = (stop_decision.decision == \"BLOCKED\")\n      step_frontier_activate:\n        description: \"Mark the active frontier node before the iteration dispatches\"\n        enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive' AND active_frontier_node is non-empty\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        note: \"Marking the node active at this iteration lets the reducer attribute the iteration to the node even when the leaf rewords its focus, so the node's own coverage keeps moving instead of the iteration sliding back onto the global dimension queue.\"\n        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs close --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --node-id \"{active_frontier_node}\" --status active --iteration \"{current_iteration}\"'\n        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n        on_failure: \"Log the stderr line as a config_warning bookkeeping event and continue; the leaf's frontierNodeId and focus marker still attribute the iteration.\"\n\n      step_dispatch_iteration:","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017WMbJhaY1ed4igqGm3SAg8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
