{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fi3NKUvCxJ3KanHJyxSoyv","type":"tool_result","content":"      counts: stateCounts(analysis.records),\n      destinations: outOfSync.map((record) => ({\n        state: record.state,\n        key: record.key,\n        kind: record.layout ? 'layout-link' : (record.removal ? 'remove-root' : 'overlay'),\n        overlay: record.layout ? null : record.plan.entry.id,\n        source: record.source ? ctx.overlayLabel + '/' + record.source : null,\n        fix: fixFor(ctx, record),\n      })),\n      staleRootFiles: stale,\n      offLayout,\n      notes,\n      check,\n    };\n    if (audit) report.audit = audit;\n    console.log(JSON.stringify(report, null, 2));\n    return isInSync ? EXIT_OK : EXIT_CONFLICT;\n  }\n\n  for (const record of outOfSync) console.log(problemLine(ctx, record));\n  console.log(stateSummary(analysis.records));\n  for (const problem of check.problems) console.log(`MISS     ${problem}`);\n  // A re-pin never copies a root file, so an upstream move to an owned one is\n  // outstanding work no destination line can report, and this comparison is the\n  // only place status sees it between re-pins.\n  for (const entry of stale) {\n    console.log(`STALE    root-file ${entry.path}: upstream changed it since overlay ${entry.overlay} was pinned; ` +\n      'rebase the overlay, then update its pinnedSha256');\n  }\n  // Relayout refuses a move into root/skilled, so each line, and the count of the\n  // moves past the cap, names the fix the operator can make instead of a run\n  // that would stop.\n  for (const move of offLayout.slice(0, LAYOUT_SHOWN)) {\n    const remedy = isUnderRootSkilled(move.to)\n      ? 'change the destination or remove the entry'\n      : `run ${ENGINE_COMMAND} apply --relayout`;\n    console.log(`LAYOUT   ${move.overlay}: ${move.field} ${move.from} belongs at ${move.to}; ${remedy}`);\n  }\n  if (offLayout.length > LAYOUT_SHOWN) {\n    const hidden = offLayout.slice(LAYOUT_SHOWN);\n    const blocked = hidden.filter((move) => isUnderRootSkilled(move.to)).length;\n    const movable = hidden.length - blocked;\n    const remedy = blocked === 0\n      ? `; run ${ENGINE_COMMAND} apply --relayout`\n      : movable === 0\n        ? ' under root/skilled; change the destination or remove the entry'\n        : `; run ${ENGINE_COMMAND} apply --relayout for ${movable}, and change the destination or remove the ` +\n          `entry for the ${blocked} under root/skilled`;\n    console.log(`LAYOUT   … ${hidden.length} more${remedy}`);\n  }\n  for (const note of notes) console.log(`NOTE     ${note}`);\n  if (audit) {\n    for (const finding of audit.findings) console.log(`AUDIT    ${finding.kind} ${finding.path}`);\n    if (!audit.isAvailable) console.log('AUDIT    skipped: no upstream checkout at the pin');\n    console.log(`audit=${audit.findings.length}`);\n  }\n17:| `--capture` given with `--adopt` or `--relayout`, or `--adopt` given with `--relayout` | `--capture saves a live edit, --adopt adds a new entry and --relayout moves overlay sources. Give one of them.` then `Try: /doctor:overlay apply [--root <dir>] [--capture <path> | --adopt <path> | --relayout]` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"conflicting_arguments\"` |\n26:| `apply` | `--root <dir>`, `--capture <path>`, `--adopt <path>` and `--relayout` |\n34:| `apply` | `/doctor:overlay apply [--root <dir>] [--capture <path> | --adopt <path> | --relayout]` |\n87:LAYOUT   [overlay]: [field] [from] belongs at [to]; run [the engine command] apply --relayout\n88:LAYOUT   [overlay]: [field] [from] belongs at [to]; change the destination or remove the entry\n96:The second remedy, `change the destination or remove the entry`, is printed when [to] sits under root/skilled, which relayout refuses because that folder holds no copy.\n118:| `LAYOUT` | An overlay source sits off the layout path its destination maps to, such as a copy kept under `<overlay folder>/skilled/skills/...` that belongs under `<overlay folder>/framework/skills/...` | The copy still applies, so the tree is not broken and nothing is lost. `/doctor:overlay apply --relayout` moves it to its layout path and points the manifest there: a `.skilled/X` destination maps to `framework/X`, and any other destination `X` maps to `root/` plus `X` with its leading dots dropped. Status prints at most 20 of these lines, then one overflow line, in one of three forms, where N is the hidden lines, M the ones relayout can move and B the ones under root/skilled: `LAYOUT   … N more; run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs apply --relayout` when none is under root/skilled, `LAYOUT   … N more under root/skilled; change the destination or remove the entry` when all are, and `LAYOUT   … N more; run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs apply --relayout for M, and change the destination or remove the entry for the B under root/skilled` when they mix. A LAYOUT line whose [to] sits under root/skilled names `change the destination or remove the entry` instead of the relayout, because relayout refuses a move under root/skilled. `status --json` keeps every move in its `offLayout` array | does not fail the status |\n276:The engine has no plan mode for `apply --relayout`, so the plan is the `offLayout` list that `status --json` prints for the same run, one row per move, because the text report stops after 20 `LAYOUT` lines. Each item names the overlay, the manifest field, the path the copy sits at now and the path it belongs at. Every move stays inside the overlay folder: a copy for a `.skilled/` destination lands at its `framework/` path, a copy for any other destination lands at its `root/` path, and the destination the overlay writes is untouched.\n279:OVERLAY RELAYOUT PLAN\n283:Backup: [overlay folder]/relayout-runs/[stamp]/, holding every copy the run moves and the manifest, written before the first move\n292:| An empty `offLayout` list, so no `LAYOUT` line | The nothing-to-move result. Every source already sits on its layout path | `STATUS=OK` |\n293:| At least one `offLayout` item, and nothing else outstanding | The relayout plan and the relayout question | asks |\n294:| Any `live-edited`, `both-changed`, `upstream-moved` or `cannot-apply` line | Each such line with its fix, beside the `LAYOUT` lines. The apply that follows the move would be refused until it is settled | `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"needs_resolution\"` |\n295:| A `MISS` line or a `STALE` line, and no line above | The relayout plan and the relayout question, with each such line shown beside the `LAYOUT` lines. The engine moves the sources and still exits 0, so the run goes on and ends on that line | asks |\n460:Backup: [overlay folder]/relayout-runs/[stamp]/\n462:Re-read: [the status report's RESULT line, its LAYOUT lines, and any moved copy still listed in the offLayout list of status --json]\n520:Declined: [the apply | the capture of the path | the adoption of the path | the relayout of the overlay folder | the re-pin to the commit | the rollback of the run]\n542:| A relayout, exit 0 with `skipped` lines | The copies the run reported moved. A skipped file was never copied into the backup: one that is a source on its own stayed where it was, and one inside a moved folder went with that folder |\n563:| A `LAYOUT` line in a status report | Run `/doctor:overlay apply --relayout`, which moves each off-layout source and then applies. The copy still applies while it sits off its layout path |\n565:| A relayout printed `skipped` for a path | The backup did not copy that file because the read rule protects it. A source on its own stayed where it was, so move it by hand to the path its `offLayout` item named. One inside a moved folder already sits on that path, and only the backup lacks it |\n566:| A relayout refused because the target exists | The overlay folder holds both the old copy and the path it belongs at. Keep one of them, then rerun |\n595:| The status report shows a `LAYOUT` line | `/doctor:overlay apply --relayout` | The source moves onto its layout path, the manifest names that path, and the apply in the same run puts the destinations on it |\n596:| A relayout just ran | `/doctor:overlay status` | The re-read confirms the tree is in sync |\n601:| An apply, a capture, an adopt or a relayout just ran | `/doctor:overlay status` | The re-read confirms the tree is in sync |\ndoctor-overlay-apply.yaml\ndoctor-overlay-presentation.txt\ndoctor-overlay-repin.yaml\ndoctor-overlay-status.yaml","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"faa6b93c-ce84-436d-8875-372fa8efb878","uuid":"20a51142-4f60-4fec-95dd-9bc10bdb0679","timestamp":"2026-11-20T16:39:13.289Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"      counts: stateCounts(analysis.records),\n      destinations: outOfSync.map((record) => ({\n        state: record.state,\n        key: record.key,\n        kind: record.layout ? 'layout-link' : (record.removal ? 'remove-root' : 'overlay'),\n        overlay: record.layout ? null : record.plan.entry.id,\n        source: record.source ? ctx.overlayLabel + '/' + record.source : null,\n        fix: fixFor(ctx, record),\n      })),\n      staleRootFiles: stale,\n      offLayout,\n      notes,\n      check,\n    };\n    if (audit) report.audit = audit;\n    console.log(JSON.stringify(report, null, 2));\n    return isInSync ? EXIT_OK : EXIT_CONFLICT;\n  }\n\n  for (const record of outOfSync) console.log(problemLine(ctx, record));\n  console.log(stateSummary(analysis.records));\n  for (const problem of check.problems) console.log(`MISS     ${problem}`);\n  // A re-pin never copies a root file, so an upstream move to an owned one is\n  // outstanding work no destination line can report, and this comparison is the\n  // only place status sees it between re-pins.\n  for (const entry of stale) {\n    console.log(`STALE    root-file ${entry.path}: upstream changed it since overlay ${entry.overlay} was pinned; ` +\n      'rebase the overlay, then update its pinnedSha256');\n  }\n  // Relayout refuses a move into root/skilled, so each line, and the count of the\n  // moves past the cap, names the fix the operator can make instead of a run\n  // that would stop.\n  for (const move of offLayout.slice(0, LAYOUT_SHOWN)) {\n    const remedy = isUnderRootSkilled(move.to)\n      ? 'change the destination or remove the entry'\n      : `run ${ENGINE_COMMAND} apply --relayout`;\n    console.log(`LAYOUT   ${move.overlay}: ${move.field} ${move.from} belongs at ${move.to}; ${remedy}`);\n  }\n  if (offLayout.length > LAYOUT_SHOWN) {\n    const hidden = offLayout.slice(LAYOUT_SHOWN);\n    const blocked = hidden.filter((move) => isUnderRootSkilled(move.to)).length;\n    const movable = hidden.length - blocked;\n    const remedy = blocked === 0\n      ? `; run ${ENGINE_COMMAND} apply --relayout`\n      : movable === 0\n        ? ' under root/skilled; change the destination or remove the entry'\n        : `; run ${ENGINE_COMMAND} apply --relayout for ${movable}, and change the destination or remove the ` +\n          `entry for the ${blocked} under root/skilled`;\n    console.log(`LAYOUT   … ${hidden.length} more${remedy}`);\n  }\n  for (const note of notes) console.log(`NOTE     ${note}`);\n  if (audit) {\n    for (const finding of audit.findings) console.log(`AUDIT    ${finding.kind} ${finding.path}`);\n    if (!audit.isAvailable) console.log('AUDIT    skipped: no upstream checkout at the pin');\n    console.log(`audit=${audit.findings.length}`);\n  }\n17:| `--capture` given with `--adopt` or `--relayout`, or `--adopt` given with `--relayout` | `--capture saves a live edit, --adopt adds a new entry and --relayout moves overlay sources. Give one of them.` then `Try: /doctor:overlay apply [--root <dir>] [--capture <path> | --adopt <path> | --relayout]` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"conflicting_arguments\"` |\n26:| `apply` | `--root <dir>`, `--capture <path>`, `--adopt <path>` and `--relayout` |\n34:| `apply` | `/doctor:overlay apply [--root <dir>] [--capture <path> | --adopt <path> | --relayout]` |\n87:LAYOUT   [overlay]: [field] [from] belongs at [to]; run [the engine command] apply --relayout\n88:LAYOUT   [overlay]: [field] [from] belongs at [to]; change the destination or remove the entry\n96:The second remedy, `change the destination or remove the entry`, is printed when [to] sits under root/skilled, which relayout refuses because that folder holds no copy.\n118:| `LAYOUT` | An overlay source sits off the layout path its destination maps to, such as a copy kept under `<overlay folder>/skilled/skills/...` that belongs under `<overlay folder>/framework/skills/...` | The copy still applies, so the tree is not broken and nothing is lost. `/doctor:overlay apply --relayout` moves it to its layout path and points the manifest there: a `.skilled/X` destination maps to `framework/X`, and any other destination `X` maps to `root/` plus `X` with its leading dots dropped. Status prints at most 20 of these lines, then one overflow line, in one of three forms, where N is the hidden lines, M the ones relayout can move and B the ones under root/skilled: `LAYOUT   … N more; run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs apply --relayout` when none is under root/skilled, `LAYOUT   … N more under root/skilled; change the destination or remove the entry` when all are, and `LAYOUT   … N more; run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs apply --relayout for M, and change the destination or remove the entry for the B under root/skilled` when they mix. A LAYOUT line whose [to] sits under root/skilled names `change the destination or remove the entry` instead of the relayout, because relayout refuses a move under root/skilled. `status --json` keeps every move in its `offLayout` array | does not fail the status |\n276:The engine has no plan mode for `apply --relayout`, so the plan is the `offLayout` list that `status --json` prints for the same run, one row per move, because the text report stops after 20 `LAYOUT` lines. Each item names the overlay, the manifest field, the path the copy sits at now and the path it belongs at. Every move stays inside the overlay folder: a copy for a `.skilled/` destination lands at its `framework/` path, a copy for any other destination lands at its `root/` path, and the destination the overlay writes is untouched.\n279:OVERLAY RELAYOUT PLAN\n283:Backup: [overlay folder]/relayout-runs/[stamp]/, holding every copy the run moves and the manifest, written before the first move\n292:| An empty `offLayout` list, so no `LAYOUT` line | The nothing-to-move result. Every source already sits on its layout path | `STATUS=OK` |\n293:| At least one `offLayout` item, and nothing else outstanding | The relayout plan and the relayout question | asks |\n294:| Any `live-edited`, `both-changed`, `upstream-moved` or `cannot-apply` line | Each such line with its fix, beside the `LAYOUT` lines. The apply that follows the move would be refused until it is settled | `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"needs_resolution\"` |\n295:| A `MISS` line or a `STALE` line, and no line above | The relayout plan and the relayout question, with each such line shown beside the `LAYOUT` lines. The engine moves the sources and still exits 0, so the run goes on and ends on that line | asks |\n460:Backup: [overlay folder]/relayout-runs/[stamp]/\n462:Re-read: [the status report's RESULT line, its LAYOUT lines, and any moved copy still listed in the offLayout list of status --json]\n520:Declined: [the apply | the capture of the path | the adoption of the path | the relayout of the overlay folder | the re-pin to the commit | the rollback of the run]\n542:| A relayout, exit 0 with `skipped` lines | The copies the run reported moved. A skipped file was never copied into the backup: one that is a source on its own stayed where it was, and one inside a moved folder went with that folder |\n563:| A `LAYOUT` line in a status report | Run `/doctor:overlay apply --relayout`, which moves each off-layout source and then applies. The copy still applies while it sits off its layout path |\n565:| A relayout printed `skipped` for a path | The backup did not copy that file because the read rule protects it. A source on its own stayed where it was, so move it by hand to the path its `offLayout` item named. One inside a moved folder already sits on that path, and only the backup lacks it |\n566:| A relayout refused because the target exists | The overlay folder holds both the old copy and the path it belongs at. Keep one of them, then rerun |\n595:| The status report shows a `LAYOUT` line | `/doctor:overlay apply --relayout` | The source moves onto its layout path, the manifest names that path, and the apply in the same run puts the destinations on it |\n596:| A relayout just ran | `/doctor:overlay status` | The re-read confirms the tree is in sync |\n601:| An apply, a capture, an adopt or a relayout just ran | `/doctor:overlay status` | The re-read confirms the tree is in sync |\ndoctor-overlay-apply.yaml\ndoctor-overlay-presentation.txt\ndoctor-overlay-repin.yaml\ndoctor-overlay-status.yaml","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/opus-medium/frontier-nodes.jsonl","hunks":[{"oldStart":3,"oldLines":3,"newStart":3,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"nodeId\":\"F-1-005\",\"parentId\":\"root\",\"depth\":1,\"scope\":[\"barter/ai-speckit/.gitignore\",\"barter/ai-speckit/overlays/README.md\",\"barter/ai-speckit/overlays/tests\",\"barter/ai-speckit/overlays/framework/repo-rules\",\"barter/ai-speckit/overlays/overlay-manifest.json\",\"barter/ai-speckit/overlays/sync-state.json\"],\"question\":\"Barter hygiene: is overlays/relayout-runs/ ignored and documented (prior R3-P2-001), is the barter-overlays fixture renamed (R3-P2-002), does any live barter-overlays or dot-dropped layout reference remain in either repo outside spec history and changelogs, and do the barter-overlay-first rule and overlays/README.md match the hooks? Read-only nested repo.\",\"status\":\"open\",\"reason\":null,\"iteration\":0,\"dedupeKey\":\"barter hygiene is overlays relayout runs ignored and documented prior r3 p2 001 is the barter overlays fixture renamed r3 p2 002 does any live barter overlays or dot dropped layout reference remain in either repo outside spec history and changelogs and do the barter overlay first rule and overlays readme md match the hooks read only nested repo\"}"," {\"nodeId\":\"F-1-007\",\"parentId\":\"root\",\"depth\":1,\"scope\":[\"specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout\"],\"question\":\"Are the remediation records traceable: do phases 006-review-remediation, 007-barter-review-fixes and 008-push-and-repin (spec, tasks, acceptance criteria, implementation summaries) and the ai-speckit record (e63bd038a5d) match the code and the test runs they cite, are prior R4-P2-001 (005 acceptance-criteria.md:66) and R6-P2-001 (002 spec.md:109) corrected, and is any completion claim, including the push and the blocked merge of main with origin, made without evidence?\",\"status\":\"open\",\"reason\":null,\"iteration\":0,\"dedupeKey\":\"are the remediation records traceable do phases 006 review remediation 007 barter review fixes and 008 push and repin spec tasks acceptance criteria implementation summaries and the ai speckit record e63bd038a5d match the code and the test runs they cite are prior r4 p2 001 005 acceptance criteria md 66 and r6 p2 001 002 spec md 109 corrected and is any completion claim including the push and the blocked merge of main with origin made without evidence\"}"," {\"nodeId\":\"F-1-001\",\"parentId\":\"root\",\"depth\":1,\"scope\":[\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs\",\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/overlay-engine-follow-up.test.cjs\",\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/overlay-engine-strict-writes.test.cjs\"],\"question\":\"Follow-up on the relayout rollback: does apply --relayout now restore every moved copy and leave no half-moved overlay folder when a rename or writeRelayoutManifest fails mid-run (prior R1-P1-001)? Is the rollback itself correct when a restore rename fails, is the writeBackup split sound, and does the new mid-loop failure test fail without the fix?\",\"status\":\"active\",\"reason\":null,\"iteration\":1,\"dedupeKey\":\"follow up on the relayout rollback does apply relayout now restore every moved copy and leave no half moved overlay folder when a rename or writerelayoutmanifest fails mid run prior r1 p1 001 is the rollback itself correct when a restore rename fails is the writebackup split sound and does the new mid loop failure test fail without the fix\"}","+{\"nodeId\":\"F-1-003\",\"parentId\":\"root\",\"depth\":1,\"scope\":[\".skilled/commands/doctor/assets\",\".skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/references/overlays.md\"],\"question\":\"Do the doctor docs now match the engine: both LAYOUT remedies in doctor-overlay-presentation.txt (prior R8-P2-001), the relayout failure contract in references/overlays.md, and the apply workflow's guidance on reading a failed relayout in doctor-overlay-apply.yaml? Does any doc claim behavior the code does not have?\",\"status\":\"active\",\"reason\":null,\"iteration\":2,\"dedupeKey\":\"do the doctor docs now match the engine both layout remedies in doctor overlay presentation txt prior r8 p2 001 the relayout failure contract in references overlays md and the apply workflow s guidance on reading a failed relayout in doctor overlay apply yaml does any doc claim behavior the code does not have\"}"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/opus-medium/frontier-nodes.jsonl"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Fi3NKUvCxJ3KanHJyxSoyv","permission_decision":{"decision":"a