{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T1G8qNAMj19iYu7zYhmm3Z","type":"tool_result","content":"5:purpose: Show the engine's status report as the plan, ask once, then run the engine's apply, capture, adopt or relayout only after that yes, and re-read the tree through status\n6:action: Read the engine -> run status -> show the plan -> explicit yes -> run apply, apply --capture <path>, apply --adopt <path> or apply --relayout then apply -> re-read through status\n34:    - \"with --relayout, the overlay sources the manifest keeps off their layout paths, moved inside the overlay folder to their layout paths, framework/<X> for a destination under .skilled/<X> and root/ plus the destination with its leading dots dropped for any other, the layout links that reach them, the source, fragment and base fields of <overlay folder>/overlay-manifest.json, and the backup\n38:    - \"a relayout target path that already exists, or a copy the engine cannot place safely, which the engine refuses rather than overwrite\"\n41:  invariant: \"Nothing is written until the operator has read this run's status report, and with --relayout the relayout plan built from the offLayout list of its status --json, and answered yes to it. The engine takes its own lock and classifies every destination again before the first write. While any destination is live-edited, both-changed or upstream-moved it writes nothing and exits 1. A n\n59:  adopt_path: \"The vendored file or folder given with --adopt <path> (default none). It sits under .skilled, under a runtime folder the manifest's repin block names, or is a root file named in repin.rootFiles. The engine resolves it against the tree root or the working directory. Never given together with --capture or --relayout.\"\n60:  relayout: \"The --relayout flag when the operator gave it (default none). It moves each overlay source kept off its layout path onto that path and then applies. Never given together with --capture or --adopt.\"\n70:      - \"Read the engine's interface before driving it: node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs --help prints its usage block and exits 0. status is read-only. apply applies every overlay under the engine's lock. apply --capture <path> moves one live edit into its overlay source. apply --adopt <path> copies one unowned vendored path into the overlay folder, appends its manifest\n77:      - \"Exit 2 means a precondition failed, such as a missing overlay manifest or an invalid .skilled-overlays.json. Quote the engine's message, name the accepted invocation (/doctor:overlay apply [--root <dir>] [--capture <path> | --adopt <path> | --relayout]), and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n78:      - \"Without capture_path, adopt_path or relayout: exit 0 with RESULT: PASSED means the tree is in sync. Render the unchanged result, ask nothing, write nothing and go to phase 6 with STATUS=OK.\"\n79:      - \"Without capture_path, adopt_path or relayout: a live-edited line stops the run before the question, because a plain apply refuses while one is there. Show each such line with /doctor:overlay apply --capture <path> for it and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n80:      - \"Without capture_path, adopt_path or relayout: a both-changed, upstream-moved or cannot-apply line stops the run before the question, because a person resolves it. Show each such line with the engine's fix and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n81:      - \"Without capture_path, adopt_path or relayout: a MISS line that says refusing to inspect a protected path means that entry is blocked and apply would write nothing; show it with the fix from the presentation contract's refusing to inspect a protected path row and end with STATUS=FAIL. Otherwise, exit 1 with no destination line and only MISS lines means no destination is behind, so an ap\n82:      - \"Without capture_path, adopt_path or relayout: a STALE line does not stop the run, and an apply never clears it, because an apply rewrites destinations and never the pinnedSha256 that comparison reads. Carry the line into the plan, which shows it, says the apply leaves it in place and names the fix: rebase that overlay on the new upstream file, then set its pinnedSha256. A report whose \n85:      - \"With relayout, keep every LAYOUT line as well, then run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs status --json with the same --root and take the plan from its offLayout list, which holds every move, including any past the twenty LAYOUT lines the text report shows and its one overflow line: the overlay id, the manifest field, the path the copy sits at now and the path it\n86:      - \"With relayout, an empty offLayout list in status --json means every source already sits on its layout path, so render the nothing-to-move result, ask nothing, write nothing and go to phase 6 with STATUS=OK.\"\n87:      - \"With relayout, a live-edited, both-changed, upstream-moved or cannot-apply line stops the run before the question, because the apply that follows the move would be refused until it is settled. Show each such line with its fix beside the LAYOUT lines and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written. A MISS line or a STALE line does not stop the run: the engine moves the sources with either\n92:      - \"Without capture_path, adopt_path or relayout, render the apply plan from the presentation contract: one line per overlay-edited line the report printed, each MISS line, each STALE line with the note that an apply does not clear it and the fix for it, each NOTE line, the regenerate and verify steps that follow, and the lock the engine holds. Then ask the apply question once.\"\n95:      - \"With relayout, render the relayout plan from the presentation contract: one line per offLayout item in status --json, the backup folder the run leaves, the manifest fields and layout links it rewrites, and the apply that follows in the same run. Then ask the relayout question once.\"\n102:      - \"Without capture_path, adopt_path or relayout, run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs apply, adding --root \\\"{root}\\\" when the plan ran with it. Run it only after the apply yes.\"\n105:      - \"With relayout, run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs apply --relayout, adding --root \\\"{root}\\\" when the plan ran with it, then run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs apply with the same --root, because the move leaves the destinations on the old copies until that apply writes them. Run both only after the relayout yes.\"\n111:      - \"A relayout that exits 0 prints its backup line, one moved line per copy, the moved count and the apply line it names. The run then applies, and every line both calls printed is kept.\"\n112:      - \"A relayout that rewrote a layout link prints one relinked line for it, in the form relinked <link path> -> <new target>. The manifest records that target in the same run, so the link and the manifest name one copy. Report each relinked line in Changed beside the moved lines.\"\n113:      - \"A skipped line inside an exit 0 relayout means the backup did not copy that file because the read rule protects it. A source on its own stayed where it was while the run moved the others, so report its path in Changed as not moved. A file inside a moved folder went with that folder, and only the backup lacks it. Report each skipped path and carry on with the apply.\"\n114:      - \"Exit 2 from apply --relayout with refuse lines means nothing was written: a target already exists, a copy the manifest names is missing, one copy is claimed by two destinations, two copies belong at one path, two copies sit one inside the other, or the overlay lock is held. Quote the lines and end with STATUS=FAIL. Never retry the relayout here.\"\n115:      - \"Exit 2 from apply --relayout with a refuse line that names a field or a link the run can no longer rewrite means the manifest changed under it or holds two entries for one copy. Quote the line and end with STATUS=FAIL. That refusal comes before the first move, so nothing was written.\"\n116:      - \"Exit 2 from apply --relayout with an error: relayout failed while line means a move, the manifest write or a relink failed part way. Any moved or relinked line printed before it was undone, so report none of them in Changed. When the line ends back as they were, every copy, the manifest and the links are as they were before the run: quote the line and end with STATUS=FAIL. When it say\n117:      - \"Exit 1 from the apply a relayout run makes means the sources moved. With no MISS generated line after the changed count, the destinations were not written, so report the moved lines in Changed and end with STATUS=FAIL. Exit 1 with MISS generated lines after the changed count means the destinations were written and recorded while a generator check still fails, so report the moved lines\n124:      - \"After a successful apply, capture, adopt or relayout result, resolve the advisor workspace root to {root} when supplied or \\\"$PWD\\\" otherwise, then make one read-only `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root <workspace root> --include-semantic-health true --format json --timeout-ms 1500 --warm-only` call. Report skills and command vectors as current/total, \n126:      - \"A re-read after a relayout runs status --json as well, with the same --root, and checks each copy the run reported moved against its offLayout list. A moved copy still listed there, or still shown on a LAYOUT line, is a failure, and its line or offLayout item is quoted as printed.\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"faa6b93c-ce84-436d-8875-372fa8efb878","uuid":"3bd80d6b-2165-48b2-943b-add9f9d1126a","timestamp":"2026-11-20T16:39:31.524Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"5:purpose: Show the engine's status report as the plan, ask once, then run the engine's apply, capture, ado