{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChEWgZskgzBgqRrpGf4DD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01713fS9kwYdn74zjQffige8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/barter/ai-speckit; cat -n overlays/framework/repo-rules/barter-overlay-first.md | sed -n 1,80p; grep -n \"relayout-runs\\|repin-runs\\|overlayDir\\|\\.\\./overlays\\|pre-commit\\|fail\" overlays/README.md | head -30; cd ..","description":"Read overlay-first rule and README"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1887,"cache_read_input_tokens":180221,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1887},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"faa6b93c-ce84-436d-8875-372fa8efb878","uuid":"39b4c5af-22ae-46f5-b8f2-9b63815a14e9","timestamp":"2026-11-20T16:41:24.960Z","request_id":"req_011ChEWgZd89NTszH4fdfM7G","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01713fS9kwYdn74zjQffige8":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/barter/ai-speckit; cat -n overlays/framework/repo-rules/barter-overlay-first.md | sed -n 1,80p; grep -n \"relayout-runs\\|repin-runs\\|overlayDir\\|\\.\\./overlays\\|pre-commit\\|fail\" overlays/README.md | head -30; cd ..","description":"Read overlay-first rule and README"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01713fS9kwYdn74zjQffige8","type":"tool_result","content":"     1\t---\n     2\ttitle: \"Rule: Barter overlay first\"\n     3\tdescription: \"A file that overlays/ owns changes in overlays/ first and reaches the live tree only through the overlay engine's apply, never by editing the live copy.\"\n     4\ttrigger_phrases:\n     5\t  - \"edit the vendored file\"\n     6\t  - \"hand-edit .skilled\"\n     7\t  - \"the overlay already owns that file\"\n     8\t  - \"the guard refused my edit\"\n     9\t  - \"status says live-edited\"\n    10\t  - \"both-changed or upstream-moved\"\n    11\t  - \"status says cannot-apply\"\n    12\t  - \"where do I make this change\"\n    13\t  - \"a re-pin would wipe it anyway\"\n    14\t  - \"create a new skill\"\n    15\t  - \"add a new command or agent\"\n    16\t  - \"overlay-engine apply --adopt\"\n    17\timportance_tier: important\n    18\tcontextType: reference\n    19\tversion: 1.1.1.0\n    20\t---\n    21\t\n    22\t# Rule: Barter overlay first\n    23\t\n    24\t> Routed from [`REPO RULES.md`](../../REPO%20RULES.md). Load it before editing any path that `overlays/overlay-manifest.json` lists as a destination, and before resolving an overlay engine refusal.\n    25\t> Expands `AGENTS.md`, never overrides it. Where they appear to disagree, `AGENTS.md` wins and this file is wrong. Say so.\n    26\t\n    27\t## 0. 📖 OVERVIEW\n    28\t\n    29\tThis rule explains how to identify overlay-owned paths and where their changes are made.\n    30\t\n    31\t---\n    32\t\n    33\t## Fires when\n    34\t\n    35\t- Editing a file that `overlays/overlay-manifest.json` names as a destination.\n    36\t- Hand-editing a vendored file under `.skilled` or a runtime folder.\n    37\t- Creating a new skill, mode, command, agent, hook, rule or any other new file under `.skilled` or a runtime folder.\n    38\t- Resolving an engine refusal: `apply` blocked, `status` reporting a live edit, or `pre-commit` reporting an unowned staged change.\n    39\t- Hand-editing a vendored file in a linked project, where `.skilled` is the same shared tree.\n    40\t- Capturing the hand edit into its overlay file with `apply --capture <path>`.\n    41\t\n    42\t## The rule\n    43\t\n    44\t**A Barter-owned file changes in `overlays/` first and reaches the live tree only through `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs apply`, or `/doctor:overlay apply`.** A path is Barter-owned only when the manifest owns it. Settle any path with `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs --guard <path>`, run from `skilled/`. It names the overlay file for an owned path and, because the manifest sets `\"strictWrites\": true`, refuses an unowned vendored path too. The edit hooks run the same check.\n    45\t\n    46\tThe live copy is output. Editing it is editing the printout.\n    47\t\n    48\t- **Wrong: open `.skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md` and change a line.** The guard refuses the write and names `../overlays/framework/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md`, the overlay file's path from `skilled/`, as the file to change.\n    49\t\n    50\t**A new Barter file starts in `overlays/` too.** Upstream has no copy of it, so a re-pin neither carries it nor warns that it is missing. Only a manifest entry keeps it. Write the new skill, command, agent or other file under `overlays/` at its source path: `framework/` plus the rest of the path for a destination under `.skilled/`, and `root/` plus the destination with its leading dots dropped for any other, so `.opencode/plugins/x.js` is written as `root/opencode/plugins/x.js`. A source under `root/skilled/` is refused. Then run `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs apply --adopt <destination>` from `skilled/`. The engine adds the manifest entry and applies it.\n    51\t\n    52\t- **Wrong: write `.skilled/skills/sk-new/SKILL.md` directly.** The guard refuses creating it and names `../overlays/framework/skills/sk-new/SKILL.md` as the file to write, and `--adopt .skilled/skills/sk-new` as the step after it.\n    53\t- A new file inside a folder an overlay already owns, such as a new reference in a Barter `sk-code` mode, needs no adopt. Write it in that overlay folder and run `apply`.\n    54\t- A new agent, command or skill under a runtime folder such as `.claude/agents/` is a mirror. Create the canonical file under `.skilled/` through `overlays/`, then regenerate the runtime mirrors.\n    55\t\n    56\t**Every write under `.skilled` or a runtime folder is checked, not only new files.** The guard decides each one:\n    57\t\n    58\t- An owned path is edited in its overlay file.\n    59\t- An upstream file no overlay owns is adopted first: `--adopt <path>` copies it into `overlays/`, at its source path under `framework/` or `root/`, and pins the upstream bytes it came from, so the next re-pin reports `upstream-moved` instead of overwriting the change. Then edit the overlay file.\n    60\t- A generated path, matched by a glob under `generated` in `overlay-manifest.json`, is never edited by hand. Change what it is generated from and rerun the generator. `overlays/README.md` names the generator behind each glob.\n    61\t- Build output, runtime state and anything else git ignores is not checked.\n    62\t\n    63\tThe write hooks see only an agent's write tools. A shell edit, a script or a person reaches the tree without them, so the commit gate checks every staged vendored path as well. The engine's `pre-commit` check, which the commit hook runs after `status`, refuses a staged path that no overlay owns, that is not generated and that differs from the pinned upstream copy, and names `--adopt` as the fix. A commit that moves the pin is a re-pin and passes.\n    64\t\n    65\t---\n    66\t\n    67\t## 1. WHY THE LIVE TREE IS OUTPUT\n    68\t\n    69\t`skilled/` holds one upstream pin, imported by `git archive`. A new pin replaces every vendored file at once, with no merge base, so a hand edit made there has no path through the next copy. `overlays/` is the other half of that arrangement: every deliberate Barter divergence lives there as its only canonical copy, and the overlay engine puts it back.\n    70\t\n    71\tThat makes the applied copy disposable and the overlay copy permanent. Edit the permanent one.\n    72\t\n    73\tA hand edit in the tree is not the smaller change. It is a change that survives until the next re-pin and then disappears, along with the reasoning behind it and any chance of noticing that it went.\n    74\t\n    75\t---\n    76\t\n    77\t## 2. HOW A CHANGE REACHES THE TREE\n    78\t\n    79\tWrite the overlay file, then apply it:\n    80\t\n8:This folder holds Barter's overlay sources, the manifest that maps each one to its destination, and the state the overlay engine records. It sits at `ai-speckit/overlays/`, beside the vendored tree `ai-speckit/skilled/`, whose `.skilled-overlays.json` names it as `../overlays`.\n40:node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs pre-commit              # exit 1 when a staged vendored change has no overlay\n47:The commit hook, `root/opencode/scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit`, runs `status` and then `pre-commit`. Each\n90:build for a newer Node, so `npm ci` under a newer default fails with\n124:     verify step fails after the live run and names each dropped item: carry it\n132:     DESTINATIONS=$(node -e 'const m = require(\"../overlays/overlay-manifest.json\");\n152:   The engine backs up every path it touches to `repin-runs/<run-id>/`, copies,\n155:   byte. Then `status` and `pre-commit` must both exit 0.\n190:   holds `git-hooks/pre-commit`, and `.opencode/plugins/lib/v2-bridge.js` must exist.\n201:   then remove the clone. A row that fails only on the new pin is a regression.\n214:     <(cd ../overlays/framework/skills/sk-git/sk-git-skilled && find references assets -type f | sort)\n234:| `.opencode/scripts/` | Upstream ships a link to `../.skilled/scripts` here, but Barter keeps a real folder. The Barter repository's `core.hooksPath` points at its `git-hooks/`. Its live `pre-commit` is unchanged; the canonical copy at `overlays/root/opencode/scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit` adds a refusal when the engine's `status` or `pre-commit` fails. A `file` overlay entry installs that copy. Five more `file` entries install a hand-over file each for `commit-msg`, `prepare-commit-msg`, `pre-push`, `post-merge` and `post-rewrite`: every one passes the call on to the Skilled hook of the same name under `.skilled/scripts/git-hooks/`, and refuses when that hook is missing. The folder is excluded from re-pins, so these entries are written into the manifest by hand rather than adopted. `tar` refuses to replace a non-empty folder with a link and exits 1; the exclude in step 2 keeps the exit clean. |\n376:stops working when it is absent, and `status` fails by name when one is\n458:  repin-runs/                    local re-pin backups, not committed\n459:  relayout-runs/                 local relayout backups, not committed","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"faa6b93c-ce84-436d-8875-372fa8efb878","uuid":"13da334e-d956-4d80-ab36-59b0f634c286","timestamp":"2026-11-20T16:41:25.509Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"     1\t---\n     2\ttitle: \"Rule: Barter overlay first\"\n     3\tdescription: \"A file that overlays/ owns changes in overlays/ first and reaches the live tree only through the overlay engine's apply, never by editing the live copy.\"\n     4\ttrigger_phrases:\n     5\t  - \"edit the vendored file\"\n     6\t  - \"hand-edit .skilled\"\n     7\t  - \"the overlay already owns that file\"\n     8\t  - \"the guard refused my edit\"\n     9\t  - \"status says live-edited\"\n    10\t  - \"both-changed or upstream-moved\"\n    11\t  - \"status says cannot-apply\"\n    12\t  - \"where do I make this change\"\n    13\t  - \"a re-pin would wipe it anyway\"\n    14\t  - \"create a new skill\"\n    15\t  - \"add a new command or agent\"\n    16\t  - \"overlay-engine apply --adopt\"\n    17\timportance_tier: important\n    18\tcontextType: reference\n    19\tversion: 1.1.1.0\n    20\t---\n    21\t\n    22\t# Rule: Barter overlay first\n    23\t\n    24\t> Routed from [`REPO RULES.md`](../../REPO%20RULES.md). Load it before editing any path that `overlays/overlay-manifest.json` lists as a destination, and before resolving an overlay engine refusal.\n    25\t> Expands `AGENTS.md`, never overrides it. Where they appear to disagree, `AGENTS.md` wins and this file is wrong. Say so.\n    26\t\n    27\t## 0. 📖 OVERVIEW\n    28\t\n    29\tThis rule explains how to identify overlay-owned paths and where their changes are made.\n    30\t\n    31\t---\n    32\t\n    33\t## Fires when\n    34\t\n    35\t- Editing a file that `overlays/overlay-manifest.json` names as a destination.\n    36\t- Hand-editing a vendored file under `.skilled` or a runtime folder.\n    37\t- Creating a new skill, mode, command, agent, hook, rule or any other new file under `.skilled` or a runtime folder.\n    38\t- Resolving an engine refusal: `apply` blocked, `status` reporting a live edit, or `pre-commit` reporting an unowned staged change.\n    39\t- Hand-editing a vendored file in a linked project, where `.skilled` is the same shared tree.\n    40\t- Capturing the hand edit into its overlay file with `apply --capture <path>`.\n    41\t\n    42\t## The rule\n    43\t\n    44\t**A Barter-owned file changes in `overlays/` first and reaches the live tree only through `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs apply`, or `/doctor:overlay apply`.** A path is Barter-owned only when the manifest owns it. Settle any path with `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs --guard <path>`, run from `skilled/`. It names the overlay file for an owned path and, because the manifest sets `\"strictWrites\": true`, refuses an unowned vendored path too. The edit hooks run the same check.\n    45\t\n    46\tThe live copy is output. Editing it is editing the printout.\n    47\t\n    48\t- **Wrong: open `.skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md` and change a line.** The guard refuses the write and names `../overlays/framework/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md`, the overlay file's path from `skilled/`, as the file to change.\n    49\t\n    50\t**A new Barter file starts in `overlays/` too.** Upstream has no copy of it, so a re-pin neither carries it nor warns that it is missing. Only a manifest entry keeps it. Write the new skill, command, agent or other file under `overlays/` at its source path: `framework/` plus the rest of the path for a destination under `.skilled/`, and `root/` plus the destination with its leading dots dropped for any other, so `.opencode/plugins/x.js` is written as `root/opencode/plugins/x.js`. A source under `root/skilled/` is refused. Then run `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs apply --adopt <destination>` from `skilled/`. The engine adds the manifest entry and applies it.\n    51\t\n    52\t- **Wrong: write `.skilled/skills/sk-new/SKILL.md` directly.** The guard refuses creating it and names `../overlays/framework/skills/sk-new/SKILL.md` as the file to write, and `--adopt .skilled/skills/sk-new` as the step after it.\n    53\t- A new file inside a folder an overlay already owns, such as a new reference in a Barter `sk-code` mode, needs no adopt. Write it in that overlay folder and run `apply`.\n    54\t- A new agent, command or skill under a runtime folder such as `.claude/agents/` is a mirror. Create the canonical file under `.skilled/` through `overlays/`, then regenerate the runtime mirrors.\n    55\t\n    56\t**Every write under `.skilled` or a runtime folder is checked, not only new files.** The guard decides each one:\n    57\t\n    58\t- An owned path is edited in its overlay file.\n    59\t- An upstream file no overlay owns is adopted first: `--adopt <path>` copies it into `overlays/`, at its source path under `framework/` or `root/`, and pins the upstream bytes it came from, so the next re-pin reports `upstream-moved` instead of overwriting the change. Then edit the overlay file.\n    60\t- A generated path, matched by a glob under `generated` in `overlay-manifest.json`, is never edited by hand. Change what it is generated from and rerun the generator. `overlays/README.md` names the generator behind each glob.\n    61\t- Build output, runtime state and anything else git ignores is not checked.\n    62\t\n    63\tThe write hooks see only an agent's write tools. A shell edit, a script or a person reaches the tree without them, so the commit gate checks every staged vendored path as well. The engine's `pre-commit` check, which the commit hook runs after `status`, refuses a staged path that no overlay owns, that is not generated and that differs from the pinned upstream copy, and names `--adopt` as the fix. A commit that moves the pin is a re-pin and passes.\n    64\t\n    65\t---\n    66\t\n    67\t## 1. WHY THE LIVE TREE IS OUTPUT\n    68\t\n    69\t`skilled/` holds one upstream pin, imported by `git archive`. A new pin replaces every vendored file at once, with no merge base, so a hand edit made there has no path through the next copy. `overlays/` is the other half of that arrangement: every deliberate Barter divergence lives there as its only canonical copy, and the overlay engine puts it back.\n    70\t\n    71\tThat makes the applied copy disposable and the overlay copy permanent. Edit the permanent one.\n    72\t\n    73\tA hand edit in the tree is not the smaller change. It is a change that survives until the next re-pin and then disappears, along with the reasoning behind it and any chance of noticing that it went.\n    74\t\n    75\t---\n    76\t\n    77\t## 2. HOW A CHANGE REACHES THE TREE\n    78\t\n    79\tWrite the overlay file, then apply it:\n    80\t\n8:This folder holds Barter's overlay sources, the manifest that maps each one to its destination, and the state the overlay engine records. It sits at `ai-speckit/overlays/`, beside the vendored tree `ai-speckit/skilled/`, whose `.skilled-overlays.json` names it as `../overlays`.\n40:node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs pre-commit              # exit 1 when a staged vendored change has no overlay\n47:The commit hook, `root/opencode/scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit`, runs `status` and then `pre-commit`. Each\n90:build for a newer Node, so `npm ci` under a newer default fails with\n124:     verify step fails after the live run and names each dropped item: carry it\n132:     DESTINATIONS=$(node -e 'const m = require(\"../overlays/overlay-manifest.json\");\n152:   The engine backs up every path it touches to `repin-runs/<run-id>/`, copies,\n155:   byte. Then `status` and `pre-commit` must both exit 0.\n190:   holds `git-hooks/pre-commit`, and `.opencode/plugins/lib/v2-bridge.js` must exist.\n201:   then remove the clone. A row that fails only on the new pin is a regression.\n214:     <(cd ../overlays/framework/skills/sk-git/sk-git-skilled && find references assets -type f | sort)\n234:| `.opencode/scripts/` | Upstream ships a link to `../.skilled/scripts` here, but Barter keeps a real folder. The Barter repository's `core.hooksPath` points at its `git-hooks/`. Its live `pre-commit` is unchanged; the canonical copy at `overlays/root/opencode/scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit` adds a refusal when the engine's `status` or `pre-commit` fails. A `file` overlay entry installs that copy. Five more `file` entries install a hand-over file each for `commit-msg`, `prepare-commit-msg`, `pre-push`, `post-merge` and `post-rewrite`: every one passes the call on to the Skilled hook of the same name under `.skilled/scripts/git-hooks/`, and refuses when that hook is missing. The folder is excluded from re-pins, so these entries are written into the manifest by hand rather than adopted. `tar` refuses to replace a non-empty folder with a link and exits 1; the exclude in step 2 keeps the exit clean. |\n376:stops working when it is absent, and `status` fails by name when one is\n458:  repin-runs/                    local re-pin backups, not committed\n459:  relayout-runs/                 local relayout backups, not committed","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01713fS9kwYdn74zjQffige8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChEWh5ppdZ5mwsrvY7TrB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TApSuxLmgTyvqjg3sLsXLT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/barter/ai-speckit; sed -n 44,60p overlays/README.md; cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled","description":"Read README commit hook paragraph"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3853,"cache_read_input_tokens":182108,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3853},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"faa6b93c-ce84-436d-8875-372fa8efb878","uuid":"956a7c3a-560f-43d4-b5e2-0918bc309072","timestamp":"2026-11-20T16:41:30.221Z","request_id":"req_011ChEWh5cB1UJDS6RboCDWC","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01TApSuxLmgTyvqjg3sLsXLT":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/barter/ai-speckit; sed -n 44,60p overlays/README.md; cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled","description":"Read README commit hook paragraph"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TApSuxLmgTyvqjg3sLsXLT","type":"tool_result","content":"question before any write. The engine takes a lock beside `sync-state.json` for\nevery write and refuses to run while another holder is live.\n\nThe commit hook, `root/opencode/scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit`, runs `status` and then `pre-commit`. Each\ncovers only its own check, so both must pass.\n\n### Strict writes\n\nThe manifest sets `\"strictWrites\": true`, so the doctor overlay engine refuses any write under `.skilled` or a runtime folder that no overlay owns, and any such write to a file under `repin.rootFiles`. The upstream `overlay-guard` hook runs that check at edit time in Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi and DSH. Upstream ships no OpenCode adapter, so Barter's `root/opencode/plugins/barter-overlay-guard.js` asks the engine's `--guard` there. The core that plugin calls is the `framework/hooks/barter-overlay-guard/` overlay. Nothing applies an overlay edit automatically: run `apply` after editing.\n\nAn adopted path's overlay copy follows the source rule under Layout, so `.skilled/skills/sk-new` is adopted as `overlays/framework/skills/sk-new` and `.opencode/plugins/x.js` as `overlays/root/opencode/plugins/x.js`. The manifest maps each source to its destination, and the engine refuses a source under `root/skilled/`.\n\n`.utcp_config.json` is a pinned overlay and is listed in `repin.rootFiles`, so a re-pin reports an upstream change to it as a `root-file` line and `status` reports a live edit to it. Barter marks the `clickup_official`, `mobbin` and `refero` manuals `\"disabled\": true`, so Code Mode does not register them at startup; each mode registers its manual on demand after asking.\n\nThe `generated` list holds the globs no check refuses, because a generator rewrites them. Change what each one is generated from, then rerun its generator:\n\n- **Hook registration sync**, `sync-hook-registrations.cjs`, from `hook-registry.json`: the four runtime hook settings files and `.claude/hooks/**`, `.codex/hooks/**`, `.cursor/hooks/**`, `.devin/hooks/**`.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"faa6b93c-ce84-436d-8875-372fa8efb878","uuid":"36a635f6-9c05-47ef-b84d-902d5c47817b","timestamp":"2026-11-20T16:41:30.771Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"question before any write. The engine takes a lock beside `sync-state.json` for\nevery write and refuses to run while another holder is live.\n\nThe commit hook, `root/opencode/scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit`, runs `status` and then `pre-commit`. Each\ncovers only its own check, so both must pass.\n\n### Strict writes\n\nThe manifest sets `\"strictWrites\": true`, so the doctor overlay engine refuses any write under `.skilled` or a runtime folder that no overlay owns, and any such write to a file under `repin.rootFiles`. The upstream `overlay-guard` hook runs that check at edit time in Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi and DSH. Upstream ships no OpenCode adapter, so Barter's `root/opencode/plugins/barter-overlay-guard.js` asks the engine's `--guard` there. The core that plugin calls is the `framework/hooks/barter-overlay-guard/` overlay. Nothing applies an overlay edit automatically: run `apply` after editing.\n\nAn adopted path's overlay copy follows the source rule under Layout, so `.skilled/skills/sk-new` is adopted as `overlays/framework/skills/sk-new` and `.opencode/plugins/x.js` as `overlays/root/opencode/plugins/x.js`. The manifest maps each source to its destination, and the engine refuses a source under `root/skilled/`.\n\n`.utcp_config.json` is a pinned overlay and is listed in `repin.rootFiles`, so a re-pin reports an upstream change to it as a `root-file` line and `status` reports a live edit to it. Barter marks the `clickup_official`, `mobbin` and `refero` manuals `\"disabled\": true`, so Code Mode does not register them at startup; each mode registers its manual on demand after asking.\n\nThe `generated` list holds the globs no check refuses, because a generator rewrites them. Change what each one is generated from, then rerun its generator:\n\n- **Hook registration sync**, `sync-hook-registrations.cjs`, from `hook-registry.json`: the four runtime hook settings files and `.claude/hooks/**`, `.codex/hooks/**`, `.cursor/hooks/**`, `.devin/hooks/**`.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TApSuxLmgTyvqjg3sLsXLT","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
