verb. Before you list a new file, module, option, layer or dependency, name what fails today without it, or drop it. GOOD: Add a `--keep <n>` option that deletes all but the newest n archives in `logs/archive/`. WEAK: Update the script and docs. -->\n\n### In Scope\n- Change `adoptSource` (`:5542-5546`) to the `framework/` and `root/` rule for every tree. It has eight call sites, each with one argument: `layoutMoves` (`:3454`, with the `.base` name at `:3464-3467`), the two strict-write hints (`:5628`, `:5632`), and adopt (`:5709`, `:5721`, `:5724`, `:5730`, `:5737`).\n  Line pointers in this section are to `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs` on Skilled main at `f2a608297c9`, re-derived after the review remediation phase. This spec first cited six call sites at `87de7f0`, before this phase added the root/skilled and missing-copy refusals in adopt.\n- Refuse a `source`, `fragment` or `base` at or under `root/skilled/` as a blocked overlay reported per entry id by `assertSafeToPlan` (`:2835`), and refuse an adopt or a relayout move whose new-rule source would land there. This keeps one source per destination.\n- Cap the status LAYOUT lines at 20 plus one overflow line (`:3692-3708`), leaving `status --json` complete.\n- Let adopt take an excluded path's copy from the old dot-dropped path when the new-rule path holds none (`:5709`, `:5737`).\n- Update the engine tests that state the old rule, and keep fixture sources on the old layout so they also prove old sources still apply.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/opus-medium/frontier-nodes.jsonl","hunks":[{"oldStart":5,"oldLines":3,"newStart":5,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"nodeId\":\"F-1-001\",\"parentId\":\"root\",\"depth\":1,\"scope\":[\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs\",\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/overlay-engine-follow-up.test.cjs\",\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/overlay-engine-strict-writes.test.cjs\"],\"question\":\"Follow-up on the relayout rollback: does apply --relayout now restore every moved copy and leave no half-moved overlay folder when a rename or writeRelayoutManifest fails mid-run (prior R1-P1-001)? Is the rollback itself correct when a restore rename fails, is the writeBackup split sound, and does the new mid-loop failure test fail without the fix?\",\"status\":\"active\",\"reason\":null,\"iteration\":1,\"dedupeKey\":\"follow up on the relayout rollback does apply relayout now restore every moved copy and leave no half moved overlay folder when a rename or writerelayoutmanifest fails mid run prior r1 p1 001 is the rollback itself correct when a restore rename fails is the writebackup split sound and does the new mid loop failure test fail without the fix\"}"," {\"nodeId\":\"F-1-003\",\"parentId\":\"root\",\"depth\":1,\"scope\":[\".skilled/commands/doctor/assets\",\".skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/references/overlays.md\"],\"question\":\"Do the doctor docs now match the engine: both LAYOUT remedies in doctor-overlay-presentation.txt (prior R8-P2-001), the relayout failure contract in references/overlays.md, and the apply workflow's guidance on reading a failed relayout in doctor-overlay-apply.yaml? Does any doc claim behavior the code does not have?\",\"status\":\"active\",\"reason\":null,\"iteration\":2,\"dedupeKey\":\"do the doctor docs now match the engine both layout remedies in doctor overlay presentation txt prior r8 p2 001 the relayout failure contract in references overlays md and the apply workflow s guidance on reading a failed relayout in doctor overlay apply yaml does any doc claim behavior the code does not have\"}"," {\"nodeId\":\"F-1-005\",\"parentId\":\"root\",\"depth\":1,\"scope\":[\"barter/ai-speckit/.gitignore\",\"barter/ai-speckit/overlays/README.md\",\"barter/ai-speckit/overlays/