{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YXrbzwBWvqHjgHUXvGLvTo","type":"tool_result","content":"| `route-validate` on merged main | PASS: 32 routes, 11 warnings, exit 0 |\n| `validate.sh --strict --recursive` on the parent | PASS: 9 of 9 `RESULT: PASSED`, exit 0 |\n| Trigger index `--check` on merged main | PASS: exit 0 |\n| `origin/main` equals `main` after the push | PASS: both `b5a630c6efa` |\n| ai-speckit `pin.commit` | PASS: `b5a630c6efaf30d36bb18e2bae875b03ab8f4600` |\n| ai-speckit `status --audit` and `pre-commit` after the re-pin | PASS: `in-sync=488`, `checked=136 ok=136 miss=0`, `RESULT: PASSED`, `offLayout=[]`; `pre-commit` `allow`, exit 0, as at baseline |\n| Both `overlays/checks` and `pre-commit.test.cjs` | PASS: `RESULT: PASSED` twice; 6 of 6 |\n| Overlay test set | 135 tests, 124 pass; the 11 failures are the baseline set by name |\n| `tests/run-all.sh` and `pi list` | PASS: exit 0 with 8 `PASS`; 9 project packages |\n| Hooks | The guard names `../overlays/...`, the commit gate refuses an unowned staged probe with exit 1, and the git-write gate refuses as before |\n| `git merge-base --is-ancestor 5dd004f3faa HEAD` in ai-speckit | PASS: exit 0 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:verification -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:limitations -->\n## Known Limitations\n\n1. **The push used the owner account through a per-command credential override.** The active gh account, `michelkerkmeester-barter`, has no push access to this repository. GitHub reported that the push bypassed the rules on `main`.\n2. **Nothing in ai-speckit is pushed.** Its two commits are local, and the push is the operator's.\n3. **This folder is uncommitted.** The ai-speckit session's git-write gate refuses a Skilled commit, so a Skilled session commits these files.\n4. **Left open by the re-pin.** These are recorded in ai-speckit's layout record, under known limitations:\n   - Upstream's root `.gitignore` line for `orchestration-status.log` was not carried into ai-speckit.\n   - The vibe mirror drift predates the re-pin.\n   - `record-base` still cannot resolve the pin.\n   - One deep-loop vitest case fails on Barter's Pi default, with the same inputs as before the re-pin.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:limitations -->\n\n---\n2:title: \"Tasks: Phase 8: push Skilled main with every overlay fix and re-pin Barter onto it\"\n5:  - \"push and repin tasks\"\n10:# Tasks: Phase 8: push Skilled main with every overlay fix and re-pin Barter onto it\n21:| `[ ]` | Pending |\n22:| `[x]` | Completed |\n36:- [x] T001 Record the baseline gates on local main before the merge (`S`). Verify: engine 262/262, guard 20/20, contract 9/9, each exit 0, and `route-validate` exits 0 with 32 routes.\n37:- [x] T002 Fetch origin and predict the merge (`S`). Verify: `git merge-tree --write-tree --name-only main origin/main` reports no conflict, and no path it changes is dirty in the working tree. Against `origin/main` `bbbec2ed55e` it exits 1 with `CONFLICT (content)` in `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/data/trigger-index.json` and the three retrieval fixtures `corpus-manifest.json`, `generation-diagnostics.json` and `phrase-variants.json` under `runtime/cli/retrieval/fixtures/`. No dirty path overlaps. Resolved 2026-11-20 by the operator's decision: take origin's copies of the four generated files, then rebuild them with `generate-trigger-index.mjs`.\n45:- [x] T003 Merge `origin/main` into main with a merge commit (`S`). Verify: `git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/main main` exits 0 and `git log -1 --format=%P main` prints two parents. Merge `8999aff6aac` and rebuild `83847bdb5fc`. The first push lost a race to two new origin commits, so a second merge `d6961a4b506` (parents `83847bdb5fc`, `698771ea279`) and rebuild `b5a630c6efa` followed, with the same four files the only conflicts.\n46:- [x] T004 Run the gates on the merged main (`S`). Verify: the engine suite, the guard suite and the contract test print `fail 0` with exit 0, `route-validate` exits 0, and `validate.sh --strict --recursive` on the parent prints `RESULT: PASSED`. On `b5a630c6efa`: engine 262/262, guard 20/20, contract 9/9, each exit 0; `route-validate` exit 0, 32 routes; 9 of 9 `RESULT: PASSED`, exit 0; trigger index `--check` exit 0.\n47:- [x] T005 Push main without force or `--no-verify` (`S`). Verify: `git rev-parse origin/main` equals `git rev-parse main`. Pushed `698771ea279..b5a630c6efa`, and both refs read `b5a630c6efa`.\n48:- [x] T006 Write the pushed id on the Target Skilled commit line and commit it docs-only (`spec.md`). Verify: `rg -n 'Target Skilled commit: [0-9a-f]{40}' spec.md` prints one line, and `git merge-base --is-ancestor C origin/main` exits 0. `C` is `b5a630c6efaf30d36bb18e2bae875b03ab8f4600`.\n49:- [x] T007 Re-pin ai-speckit onto `C` with `/doctor:overlay repin`, staged first (`AS/overlays/overlay-manifest.json`). Verify: `node -p \"require('./overlays/overlay-manifest.json').pin.commit\"` in `AS` prints `C`. Observed: `b5a630c6efaf30d36bb18e2bae875b03ab8f4600`.\n51:  - Stage 2 blocked six `upstream-moved` file overlays, five in `system-deep-loop` and `cli-opencode/SKILL.md`. Each was rebased with a clean `git merge-file`, and each `pinnedSha256` moved to the new upstream hash.\n54:  - ai-speckit commit `488ea9f49f5`, recorded in `e63bd038a5d`. Neither is pushed.\n62:- [x] T008 Run the engine gates after the re-pin (`AS/skilled`). Verify: `overlay-engine.cjs status --audit` prints `RESULT: PASSED` with `offLayout=[]`, and `pre-commit` prints `allow` with exit 0. Observed: `in-sync=488`, `checked=136 ok=136 miss=0`, `RESULT: PASSED`, `offLayout=[]`, and `pre-commit` printed `allow` with exit 0. These match the baseline taken before the re-pin.\n63:- [x] T009 Run Barter's checks and hook tests (`AS/overlays/checks`, `pre-commit.test.cjs`). Verify: both checks print `RESULT: PASSED`, and `pre-commit.test.cjs` passes 6 of 6. Observed:\n67:  - The git-write gate still refuses a force-push to `main`, another track, `git config` and another repository.\n68:- [x] T010 Run Barter's test runner (`AS/tests/run-all.sh`). Verify: it exits 0 with 8 `PASS` lines, and the overlay test files fail only the 11 baseline cases. Observed:\n71:- [x] T011 Confirm phase 007's fix survives the re-pin (`AS`). Verify: `git merge-base --is-ancestor 5dd004f3faa HEAD` exits 0. Observed: exit 0. The new engine, byte-identical to `C`, refuses an overlay folder outside the repository, and `status` passes with `../overlays`, which `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` places inside the ai-speckit root.\n79:- [x] All tasks marked `[x]`\n80:- [x] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n81:- [x] `origin/main` in Skilled contains `C`, and ai-speckit pins `C` with every Barter gate green\n6:    \"commit\": \"b5a630c6efaf30d36bb18e2bae875b03ab8f4600\",\n M overlays/README.md\n M overlays/framework/bin/tests/compiled-route-fold-dedupe.test.cjs\n M overlays/framework/bin/tests/compiled-route-hinted-surface.test.cjs\n M overlays/framework/bin/tests/compiled-route-surface-hint.test.cjs\n M overlays/framework/commands/assets/local-skilled-alignment/tests/aggregate-findings.test.cjs\ne63bd038a5d docs(specs): record the re-pin onto Skilled b5a630c","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"faa6b93c-ce84-436d-8875-372fa8efb878","uuid":"a1bc0b63-8aa2-44d8-ac21-542839444c6c","timestamp":"2026-11-20T16:43:08.862Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"| `route-validate` on merged main | PASS: 32 routes, 11 warnings, exit 0 |\n| `validate.sh --strict --recursive` on the parent | PASS: 9 of 9 `RESULT: PASSED`, exit 0 |\n| Trigger index `--check` on merged main | PASS: exit 0 |\n| `origin/main` equals `main` after the push | PASS: both `b5a630c6efa` |\n| ai-speckit `pin.commit` | PASS: `b5a630c6efaf30d36bb18e2bae875b03ab8f4600` |\n| ai-speckit `status --audit` and `pre-commit` after the re-pin | PASS: `in-sync=488`, `checked=136 ok=136 miss=0`, `RESULT: PASSED`, `offLayout=[]`; `pre-commit` `allow`, exit 0, as at baseline |\n| Both `overlays/checks` and `pre-commit.test.cjs` | PASS: `RESULT: PASSED` twice; 6 of 6 |\n| Overlay test set | 135 tests, 124 pass; the 11 failures are the baseline set by name |\n| `tests/run-all.sh` and `pi list` | PASS: exit 0 with 8 `PASS`; 9 project packages |\n| Hooks | The guard names `../overlays/...`, the commit gate refuses an unowned staged probe with exit 1, and the git-write gate refuses as before |\n| `git merge-base --is-ancestor 5dd004f3faa HEAD` in ai-speckit | PASS: exit 0 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:verification -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:limitations -->\n## Known Limitations\n\n1. **The push used the owner account through a per-command credential override.** The active gh account, `michelkerkmeester-barter`, has no push access to this repository. GitHub reported that the push bypassed the rules on `main`.\n2. **Nothing in ai-speckit is pushed.** Its two commits are local, and the push is the operator's.\n3. **This folder is uncommitted.** The ai-speckit session's git-write gate refuses a Skilled commit, so a Skilled session commits these files.\n4. **Left open by the re-pin.** These are recorded in ai-speckit's layout record, under known limitations:\n   - Upstream's root `.gitignore` line for `orchestration-status.log` was not carried into ai-speckit.\n   - The vibe mirror drift predates the re-pin.\n   - `record-base` still cannot resolve the pin.\n   - One deep-loop vitest case fails on Barter's Pi default, with the same inputs as before the re-pin.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:limitations -->\n\n---\n2:title: \"Tasks: Phase 8: push Skilled main with every overlay fix and re-pin Barter onto it\"\n5:  - \"push and repin tasks\"\n10:# Tasks: Phase 8: push Skilled main with every overlay fix and re-pin Barter onto it\n21:| `[ ]` | Pending |\n22:| `[x]` | Completed |\n36:- [x] T001 Record the baseline gates on local main before the merge (`S`). Verify: engine 262/262, guard 20/20, contract 9/9, each exit 0, and `route-validate` exits 0 with 32 routes.\n37:- [x] T002 Fetch origin and predict the merge (`S`). Verify: `git merge-tree --write-tree --name-only main origin/main` reports no conflict, and no path it changes is dirty in the working tree. Against `origin/main` `bbbec2ed55e` it exits 1 with `CONFLICT (content)` in `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/data/trigger-index.json` and the three retrieval fixtures `corpus-manifest.json`, `generation-diagnostics.json` and `phrase-variants.json` under `runtime/cli/retrieval/fixtures/`. No dirty path overlaps. Resolved 2026-11-20 by the operator's decision: take origin's copies of the four generated files, then rebuild them with `generate-trigger-index.mjs`.\n45:- [x] T003 Merge `origin/main` into main with a merge commit (`S`). Verify: `git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/main main` exits 0 and `git log -1 --format=%P main` prints two parents. Merge `8999aff6aac` and rebuild `83847bdb5fc`. The first push lost a race to two new origin commits, so a second merge `d6961a4b506` (parents `83847bdb5fc`, `698771ea279`) and rebuild `b5a630c6efa` followed, with the same four files the only conflicts.\n46:- [x] T004 Run the gates on the merged main (`S`). Verify: the engine suite, the guard suite and the contract test print `fail 0` with exit 0, `route-validate` exits 0, and `validate.sh --strict --recursive` on the parent prints `RESULT: PASSED`. On `b5a630c6efa`: engine 262/262, guard 20/20, contract 9/9, each exit 0; `route-validate` exit 0, 32 routes; 9 of 9 `RESULT: PASSED`, exit 0; trigger index `--check` exit 0.\n47:- [x] T005 Push main without force or `--no-verify` (`S`). Verify: `git rev-parse origin/main` equals `git rev-parse main`. Pushed `698771ea279..b5a630c6efa`, and both refs read `b5a630c6efa`.\n48:- [x] T006 Write the pushed id on the Target Skilled commit line and commit it docs-only (`spec.md`). Verify: `rg -n 'Target Skilled commit: [0-9a-f]{40}' spec.md` prints one line, and `git merge-base --is-ancestor C origin/main` exits 0. `C` is `b5a630c6efaf30d36bb18e2bae875b03ab8f4600`.\n49:- [x] T007 Re-pin ai-speckit onto `C` with `/doctor:overlay repin`, staged first (`AS/overlays/overlay-manifest.json`). Verify: `node -p \"require('./overlays/overlay-manifest.json').pin.commit\"` in `AS` prints `C`. Observed: `b5a630c6efaf30d36bb18e2bae875b03ab8f4600`.\n51:  - Stage 2 blocked six `upstream-moved` file overlays, five in `system-deep-loop` and `cli-opencode/SKILL.md`. Each was rebased with a clean `git merge-file`, and each `pinnedSha256` moved to the new upstream hash.\n54:  - ai-speckit commit `488ea9f49f5`, recorded in `e63bd038a5d`. Neither is pushed.\n62:- [x] T008 Run the engine gates after the re-pin (`AS/skilled`). Verify: `overlay-engine.cjs status --audit` prints `RESULT: PASSED` with `offLayout=[]`, and `pre-commit` prints `allow` with exit 0. Observed: `in-sync=488`, `checked=136 ok=136 miss=0`, `RESULT: PASSED`, `offLayout=[]`, and `pre-commit` printed `allow` with exit 0. These match the baseline taken before the re-pin.\n63:- [x] T009 Run Barter's checks and hook tests (`AS/overlays/checks`, `pre-commit.test.cjs`). Verify: both checks print `RESULT: PASSED`, and `pre-commit.test.cjs` passes 6 of 6. Observed:\n67:  - The git-write gate still refuses a force-push to `main`, another track, `git config` and another repository.\n68:- [x] T010 Run Barter's test runner (`AS/tests/run-all.sh`). Verify: it exits 0 with 8 `PASS` lines, and the overlay test files fail only the 11 baseline cases. Observed:\n71:- [x] T011 Confirm phase 007's fix survives the re-pin (`AS`). Verify: `git merge-base --is-ancestor 5dd004f3faa HEAD` exits 0. Observed: exit 0. The new engine, byte-identical to `C`, refuses an overlay folder outside the repository, and `status` passes with `../overlays`, which `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` places inside the ai-speckit root.\n79:- [x] All tasks marked `[x]`\n80:- [x] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n81:- [x] `origin/main` in Skilled contains `C`, and ai-speckit pins `C` with every Barter gate green\n6:    \"commit\": \"b5a630c6efaf30d36bb18e2bae875b03ab8f4600\",\n M overlays/README.md\n M overlays/framework/bin/tests/compiled-route-fold-dedupe.test.cjs\n M overlays/framework/bin/tests/compiled-route-hinted-surface.test.cjs\n M overlays/framework/bin/tests/compiled-route-surface-hint.test.cjs\n M overlays/framework/commands/assets/local-skilled-alignment/tests/aggregate-findings.test.cjs\ne63bd038a5d docs(specs): record the re-pin onto Skilled b5a630c","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/deepseek-flash-max/iterations/iteration-006.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":106,"lines":["+# Review Iteration 006","+","+## Dispatcher","+","+- Target spec folder: `specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout`","+- Review packet root: `specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/deepseek-flash-max`","+- Frontier node: `F-1-006` at depth 1 of 3","+- Dimension: security","+- Focus: Frontier node F-1-006: security","+- Executor: cli-mistral-vibe model=deepseek-flash (inline, no nested dispatch)","+- Operator review focus: follow-up round after remediation. This iteration asks the security half of the re-pin question: does the vendored copy carry the remediated engine faithfully, and does the engine treat the manifest as untrusted input when it reads the pinned checkout.","+","+## Files Reviewed","+","+| File | Lines | Why |","+|------|-------|-----|","+| `barter/ai-speckit/skilled/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs` | 4227-4300 | `runGit`, `commitBytesReader`, `pinnedUpstreamBytes`, `resolveCommit` |","+| `barter/ai-speckit/skilled/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs` | 4900-5140 | The repin job readers that call `commitBytesReader` |","+| `barter/ai-speckit/skilled/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs` | 540-600, 2920-2990 | `pin.checkout` resolution and pin comparison |","+| `barter/ai-speckit/overlays/overlay-manifest.json` | 1-20 | `pin`, `strictWrites`, `repin.runtimeFolders` |","+| `barter/ai-speckit/overlays/sync-state.json` | whole | Whether the state file carries machine-specific data |","+| `barter/ai-speckit/skilled/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/` | listing | Whether the engine suites ship with the vendored copy |","+","+## Findings - New","+","+### P0 Findings","+","+None.","+","+### P1 Findings","+","+None.","+","+### P2 Findings","+","+1. **The pinned-blob reader passes a manifest value to git without `--end-of-options`** -- `barter/ai-speckit/skilled/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:4241` -- `commitBytesReader` builds `git cat-file blob <commit>:<key>` from `pin.commit` and an overlay entry path. Its sibling `resolveCommit:4281` guards the same class of input with `--end-of-options`, and that is the only occurrence of the flag in the file. `pinnedUpstreamBytes:4267` type-checks `pin.commit` as a string and nothing more, so a value beginning with `-` reaches git as an option rather than a revision.","+   Finding class: security-hardening","+   Scope proof: read `overlay-engine.cjs:4227-4300` in full; `grep -n end-of-options` returns exactly one hit, at `:4281`, and `commitBytesReader` at `:4239-4244` has none.","+   Affected surface hints: `barter/ai-speckit/skilled/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs`, `barter/ai-speckit/skilled/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/overlay-engine-repin.test.cjs`","+   Case: a manifest records `pin.commit` as a string that starts with `-`, or an overlay entry names a source whose first path segment starts with `-`. `git cat-file blob` then reads the token as an option, and the bytes the audit compares are not the bytes at the pin, so `status --audit` can report a drift or an in-sync verdict that the pinned commit does not support.","+","+   ```json","+   {","+     \"type\": \"claim\",","+     \"claim\": \"commitBytesReader passes a manifest-supplied revision and path to git cat-file without --end-of-options, while resolveCommit guards the same input class.\",","+     \"evidenceRefs\": [","+       \"barter/ai-speckit/skilled/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:4241\",","+       \"barter/ai-speckit/skilled/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:4281\",","+       \"barter/ai-speckit/skilled/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:4267\"","+     ],","+     \"counterevidenceSought\": \"checked whether pin.commit is validated as a hex id before it reaches the reader: :4267 only tests typeof string, and :2931 lowercases it for comparison without validating the shape. Checked whether runGit uses a shell: it calls spawnSync('git', ['-C', upstream, ...args]) at :4228, so the exposure is git option parsing rather than shell injection.\",","+     \"alternativeExplanation\": \"the manifest is committed repository content, so the value is trusted in practice and the gap only matters if a manifest is ever authored by someone other than the tree's owner. That reading does not explain why resolveCommit already carries the flag.\",","+     \"finalSeverity\": \"P2\",","+     \"confidence\": \"high\",","+     \"downgradeTrigger\": \"drop to informational if a maintainer records that the manifest is trusted input and no consumer ever accepts one from elsewhere\"","+   }","+   ```","+","+## Traceability Checks","+","+| Check | Protocol | Result | Evidence |","+|-------|----------|--------|----------|","+| `checklist_evidence` | core | pass | Completion criterion 3 re-executed read-only: `cat .skilled-overlays.json` prints `{ \"overlayDir\": \"../overlays\" }` and `ls -d barter-overlays` fails |","+| `spec_code` | core | pass | The vendored engine is byte-identical to the pin, so the security fixes the packet records are the ones the consumer runs |","+| `integration_naming` | core | pass | The reader is named by path and by its two call families: `pinnedUpstreamBytes:4269` for the manifest pin, and the repin job readers at `:4924`, `:4925`, `:5048`, `:5096`, `:5135` |","+","+## Integration Evidence","+","+- `barter/ai-speckit/skilled/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:4228` invokes git as `spawnSync('git', ['-C', upstream, ...args])`, so no manifest value reaches a shell.","+- `barter/ai-speckit/skilled/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:4269` is the only producer of the manifest-pin reader, and it gates on `isDirectory(pin.checkout)` before constructing it.","+- `barter/ai-speckit/overlays/overlay-manifest.json:9` sets `strictWrites: true`, so the engine's `allow:` branch for a manifest without strict writes is not reachable in this consumer.","+","+## Edge Cases","+","+- **`pin.checkout` is an absolute local path.** `overlay-manifest.json:7` names `/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled`. The security reading adds nothing to the portability finding already raised as `R4-P2-001`: the engine only reads from that folder through `git -C`, and `pinnedUpstreamBytes:4267-4268` returns null when the folder is absent, so a clone without the checkout degrades to a skipped audit rather than a wrong verdict.","+- **The vendored copy ships the engine suites.** All six `overlay-engine-*.test.cjs` files are present under `skilled/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/`, so a consumer can run the same assertions the pin carries. This is recorded as a clean surface rather than a finding because the suites cannot be executed inside this lineage's write surface.","+- **`sync-state.json` carries no machine-specific data.** `grep -c \"/Users/\"` returns 0; the file holds relative paths and SHA-256 digests only.","+","+## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces","+","+- `overlay-engine.cjs:4281` uses `--end-of-options` before the revision, so `resolveCommit` cannot be steered by a leading dash.","+- `overlay-engine.cjs:4228` passes every git argument as an argv element, so no manifest value is shell-interpolated.","+- `overlay-engine.cjs:4267-4268` returns null rather than throwing when the checkout is absent or the pin fields are not strings, so a missing checkout degrades the audit instead of failing the run.","+- `overlay-engine.cjs:555-556` resolves a relative `pin.checkout` against the tree root, which is the form the docs recommend and the form `R4-P2-001` asks the manifest to adopt.","+- `overlay-manifest.json:9` sets `strictWrites: true`, which is what makes the engine's `allow:` branch unreachable for this consumer.","+- `sync-state.json` records only relative paths and content digests, so committing it leaks no local layout.","+","+## Ruled Out","+","+- **The vendored engine diverges from the pin in a security-relevant way.** Ruled out in iteration 4 by byte diff against `b5a630c6efa`; re-confirmed here by reading the same reader functions in the vendored copy.","+- **A manifest can make the engine read a credential file.** Ruled out in iteration 2: `protectedPathsFor` refuses a dotenv value and a value outside the entry.","+- **The strict-writes `allow:` branch is reachable here.** Ruled out: `overlay-manifest.json:9` sets `strictWrites: true`.","+- **`sync-state.json` leaks an absolute path.** Ruled out by exact search: zero `/Users/` hits.","+- **The vendored copy omits the engine tests.** Ruled out by listing the tests folder: all six `overlay-engine-*.test.cjs` files are present.","+","+## Next Focus","+","+- Dimension: traceability","+- Focus area: run-level pass over the packet docs and the six phase goals against the shipped behaviour, including the two Skilled-side completion criteria no iteration has executed","+- Reason: security is now covered on all three frontier nodes and traceability is the only canonical dimension with no iteration behind it","+- Rotation status: F-1-006 security complete; F-1-002 and F-1-004 carry two P2 each into synthesis","+- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive -- the reader audit found one hardening asymmetry that the earlier engine passes did not reach","+- Required evidence: `changelog/v1.2.0.0.md` naming `/doctor:overlay apply --relayout`; each phase goal's acceptance criteria against the tree; the packet's own checklist rows","+- Recovery note: `node --test` on the engine suites still cannot run inside this lineage because the suites write fixtures outside the write surface; record that limit rather than claiming a pass","+","+Review verdict: PASS"]}],"created":true}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/deepseek-flash-max/iterations/iteration-006.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01YXrbzwBWvqHjgHUXvGLvTo","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
