t -> 6 of 6, exit 0\n- Git: \\`merge-base --is-ancestor b5a630c6efa origin/main\\` exit 0; \\`git log -- 008-push-and-repin\\` (b4799f7d547, 3101c9ed363, 28aa6f9f83d); in ai-speckit \\`git branch -r --contains 5dd004f3faa\\` prints nothing\n\n## Findings by Severity\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **Phase 008's summary says its folder is uncommitted, in the commit that commits it** -- $I8:115 -- Known Limitation 3 reads \"This folder is uncommitted ... a Skilled session commits these files\", and the continuity block's next_safe_action is \"Commit this folder in a Skilled session\" (\\`$I8:14\\`). Both lines are in HEAD as committed by b4799f7d547 (\"close the Barter re-pin onto the pushed Skilled fixes\"), which committed the folder. A resume reads the next safe action and tries to commit work that is already committed.\n   - Finding class: stale-status-claim\n   - Scope proof: \\`git show HEAD:...008-push-and-repin/implementation-summary.md | grep uncommitted\\` prints line 115; git log shows the folder in three commits.\n   - Affected surface hints: 008 implementation-summary.md limitations and _memory.continuity; graph-metadata.json derived from it.\n   - Case: /speckit:resume on 008 reads next_safe_action \"Commit this folder\" although git status shows nothing to commit there.\n\n2. **Phase 007's summary says the ai-speckit fix reaches origin with phase 008, but phase 008 pushed nothing in ai-speckit** -- $I7:91 -- The How It Was Delivered line says the commit \"reaches origin with phase 008's re-pin session\". Phase 008 records \"Nothing in ai-speckit is pushed. Its two commits are local, and the push is the operator's\" (\\`$I8:114\\`), and \\`git branch -r --contains 5dd004f3faa\\` in ai-speckit prints no branch. The two phase records disagree on whether the Barter fix is published.\n   - Finding class: contradicting-records\n   - Scope proof: the only push forecast in 007; 008's tasks T007 also say \"Neither is pushed\" (\\`$S/008-push-and-repin/tasks.md:54\\`).\n   - Affected surface hints: 007 implementation-summary.md delivery paragraph.\n   - Case: a reader of 007 alone concludes the Barter commit gate fix is on ai-speckit's remote; a fresh clone of ai-speckit still has the fail-open gate.\n\n## Prior-Finding Verification\n\n- R6-P2-001 (002 spec adoptSource pointers stale, caller count wrong): FIXED. \\`$S/002-engine-framework-root-source-layout/spec.md:109\\` names eight call sites at :3454, :5628, :5632, :5709, :5721, :5724, :5730, :5737, which match grep at HEAD and at f2a608297c9 line for line.\n- R4-P2-001 (005 AC rows Met while recording a deviation): FIXED at the closure rows. AC-008 and AC-009 Then clauses now name the baseline-equal bar they were judged on (\\`acceptance-criteria.md:66-67\\`). Residual: spec.md REQ-007 and REQ-008 (\\`$S/005-barter-move-overlays-out-of-tree/spec.md:144-145\\`) still state the original bars; 006's Known Limitation 4 records this openly, so it is not raised again.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- checklist_evidence: partial. 006 test counts reproduced (262/262); 008 push verified (b5a630c6efa on origin/main); 007 and 008 disagree on publication (finding 2); 008 records a stale uncommitted state (finding 1).\n- spec_code: pass for 002 spec pointers and 006's list of engine fixes against the code read in iterations 1-2.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- Blocked merge: 008 tasks T002-T003 record the conflict set (four generated trigger-index files), the operator's decision, both merges and both rebuilds by id; \\`b5a630c6efa\\` is an ancestor of origin/main. Evidence is present for the push claim.\n- Local main is now 1 ahead and 3 behind origin/main; that is later work, not a claim the records make.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- ai-speckit has uncommitted working-tree edits (vibe mirror rows in overlays/README.md and tests). This review covers the committed state at e63bd038a5d; the uncommitted hunks do not touch the lines cited in iteration 3.\n- 007's Verification table says its numbers are quoted, not re-run; this iteration re-ran pre-commit.test.cjs and it matches.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- 006 verification table (engine suite count), 008 push and pin claims, 002 pointers.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Push claimed without evidence: origin/main contains b5a630c6efa.\n- Blocked merge left unrecorded: T002 names it and its resolution.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: security\n- Focus area: frontier node F-1-001 (resolveOverlayDir outside-repository refusal, relayout path containment)\n- Reason: all four nodes have had a first pass; F-1-001 holds the path-safety surface the review focus names\n- Rotation status: F-1-001 correctness, F-1-003 correctness, F-1-005 correctness, F-1-007 traceability done\n- Required evidence: overlay-engine.cjs resolveOverlayDir, containedOverlayPath, stagedUnownedChanges top-level probe\n\nReview verdict: PASS\nEOF\ncat > $L/prompts/spec-004.json <<EOF\n{\"iteration\":4,\"node\":\"F-1-007\",\"dimension\":\"traceability\",\"scope\":[\"$S\"],\"priorWeighted\":6,\n\"filesReviewed\":[\"$I8:115\",\"$I7:91\",\"$S/002-engine-framework-root-source-layout/spec.md:109\",\"$S/005-barter-move-overlays-out-of-tree/acceptance-criteria.md:66\",\"$S/008-push-and-repin/tasks.md:47\"],\n\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"R4-P2-001\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"title\":\"Phase 008 summary says its folder is uncommitted, in the commit that commits it\",\"file\":\"$I8:115\",\"findingClass\":\"stale-status-claim\"},\n{\"id\":\"R4-P2-002\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"title\":\"Phase 007 summary says the ai-speckit fix reaches origin with phase 008, which pushed nothing in ai-speckit\",\"file\":\"$I7:91\",\"findingClass\":\"contradicting-records\"}],\n\"traceability\":[{\"protocolId\":\"checklist_evidence\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"gateClass\":\"hard\",\"applicable\":true,\"evidence\":[\"$S/008-push-and-repin/tasks.md:47\",\"$I8:115\"],\"summary\":\"test counts and push reproduced; two stale or conflicting status lines\"},{\"protocolId\":\"spec_code\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"gateClass\":\"hard\",\"applicable\":true,\"evidence\":[\"$S/002-engine-framework-root-source-layout/spec.md:109\",\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:5542\"],\"summary\":\"002 pointers match HEAD\"}],\n\"novelty\":\"Two new record-drift P2s; prior R4-P2-001 and R6-P2-001 verified fixed; 262/262 and 6/6 reproduced.\",\n\"ledger\":[{\"bugClass\":\"unevidenced_completion\",\"targetRefs\":[\"$S/008-push-and-repin/tasks.md\"],\"hypothesis\":\"push claimed without evidence\",\"result\":\"b5a630c6efa is an ancestor of origin/main\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"$S/008-push-and-repin/tasks.md:47\"],\"disposition\":\"ruled_out\"},\n{\"bugClass\":\"stale_status\",\"targetRefs\":[\"$I8\"],\"hypothesis\":\"records claim a state git contradicts\",\"result\":\"uncommitted claim in a committed file\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"$I8:115\",\"$I8:14\"],\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"linkedFindingId\":\"R4-P2-001\"},\n{\"bugClass\":\"record_contradiction\",\"targetRefs\":[\"$I7\"],\"hypothesis\":\"phase records disagree on publication\",\"result\":\"007 forecasts a push 008 did not make\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"$I7:91\",\"$I8:114\"],\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"linkedFindingId\":\"R4-P2-002\"}],\n\"ruledOut\":[{\"direction\":\"push claim without evidence\",\"reason\":\"origin/main contains b5a630c6efa\"},{\"direction\":\"engine suite count claim\",\"reason\":\"rerun prints 262/262\"}]}\nEOF\nnode $L/prompts/emit.cjs $L/prompts/spec-004.json $L 2026-11-20T16:48:00Z 2>&1 | cut -c1-100","description":"Write and record iteration 4"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UKCbdLMCMVetrqYTUovegt","type":"tool_result","content":"gateway rc=0 {\"ok\":true,\"receipt\":{\"ledger_id\":\"deep-review-ledger\",\"sequence\":5,\"event_id\":\"event-2\nreduce rc=0 { \"registryPath\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/specs/system-skille","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"faa6b93c-ce84-436d-8875-372fa8efb878","uuid":"931b452e-2ac4-450f-9fcc-b1f91f7d0689","timestamp":"2026-11-20T16:45:27.970Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"gateway rc=0 {\"ok\":true,\"receipt\":{\"ledger_id\":\"deep-review-ledger\",\"sequence\":5,\"event_id\":\"event-2\nreduce rc=0 { \"registryPath\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/specs/system-skille","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/deepseek-flash-max/review-report.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":108,"lines":["+# Deep Review Report","+","+- Target: `specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout`","+- Review packet: `specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/deepseek-flash-max`","+- Run: `fanout-deepseek-flash-max-1795192401900-xpt66n`","+- Executor: cli-mistral-vibe model=deepseek-flash","+- Lineage: `new`, generation 1, parent `2026-11-20T16:33:02.758Z`","+- Iterations: 8 of a permitted 24","+- Dimensions: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability (all four covered)","+- Frontier nodes: F-1-002, F-1-004, F-1-006","+","+## 1. Executive Summary","+","+**Verdict: PASS with advisories.**","+","+| Severity | Active | Resolved |","+|----------|--------|----------|","+| P0 | 0 | 0 |","+| P1 | 0 | 0 |","+| P2 | 9 | 0 |","+","+`hasAdvisories = true`.","+","+This is a follow-up round after remediation. The prior generation raised 1 P1 and 15 P2 across two lineages. Every one of those 16 findings was re-verified against the current tree and every one is fixed. The remediation held: the relayout rollback restores from a snapshot and is covered by injected-failure tests, the outside-repository refusal fires from `resolveOverlayDir` on every command, both LAYOUT and strict-write remedies are branched and documented, `overlayOutside` is on the context, `writeBackup` is split, the commit gate fails closed without a manifest, the hooks read `overlayDir`, the plugin test loads the real bridge, and no live `barter-overlays` path reference survives.","+","+The nine findings this round are new, all P2, and none of them is a regression of a prior fix. They cluster in three places: two fail-open asymmetries in the Barter hooks, one argument-hardening omission in the engine's pinned-blob reader, one ticked completion criterion that no longer reproduces, and five smaller hardening and diagnostic items.","+","+Scope: the Skilled engine and its docs, the Barter vendored copy, the Barter overlay folder, and the three hook entrypoints. Two completion criteria could not be executed inside this lineage's write surface and are recorded as limits rather than passes.","+","+## 2. Planning Trigger","+","+The verdict is PASS, so the follow-on is `/create:changelog` rather than `/speckit:plan`. The nine P2 findings are advisories: they do not block release, and each carries a concrete file:line and a one-line fix. A maintainer who wants them closed before the changelog should route to `/speckit:plan` instead, and the remediation workstreams in section 4 are written to support that.","+","+## 3. Active Finding Registry","+","+| ID | Severity | Dimension | Location | Title |","+|----|----------|-----------|----------|-------|","+| R1-P2-001 | P2 | correctness | `overlay-engine.cjs:478` | A sibling link resolving back inside the tree is refused with the outside-the-tree message |","+| R2-P2-001 | P2 | security | `overlay-engine.cjs:2514` | `layoutLinks[].path` and `replaces.path` escape the root unvalidated |","+| R3-P2-001 | P2 | correctness | `pre-commit:88` | The re-resolution block can point `TREE_ROOT` one level too deep, then reports a missing engine with no fix line |","+| R4-P2-001 | P2 | correctness | `overlay-manifest.json:7` | `pin.checkout` is committed as an absolute local path although the engine documents a relative form |","+| R5-P2-001 | P2 | security | `barter-git-write-gate.mjs:2313` | The git write gate fails open and silently through its CLI entrypoint |","+| R5-P2-002 | P2 | security | `pre-commit:73` | A missing prompt-card guard skips its check with no message |","+| R6-P2-001 | P2 | security | `overlay-engine.cjs:4241` | The pinned-blob reader passes a manifest value to git without `--end-of-options` |","+| R7-P2-001 | P2 | traceability | `003-engine-docs-and-release/goal.md:62` | A checked completion criterion does not reproduce |","+| R8-P2-001 | P2 | maintainability | `pre-commit:45` | The three staged-list scans disagree on which change types they see |","+","+Each finding's full claim-adjudication packet, case, scope proof and affected surface hints are in its iteration file under `iterations/`.","+","+## 4. Remediation Workstreams","+","+**Lane A -- hook failure modes (R5-P2-001, R5-P2-002, R8-P2-001).** One change to `barter-git-write-gate.mjs:2313` and `:2317` so a `main()` rejection refuses an interesting git command and writes a note, matching `barter-git-write-gate.js:57-62`. One `else` arm at `pre-commit:73` so a missing card guard warns the way `:55` does. One decision at `pre-commit:45` and `:71` about whether a staged deletion should reach the card check, then the same filter on all three scans.","+","+**Lane B -- engine input hardening (R2-P2-001, R6-P2-001).** Add `--end-of-options` at `overlay-engine.cjs:4241`, and extend `assertSafeToPlan` to cover `layoutLinks` and `replaces` the way it already covers the other plan fields.","+","+**Lane C -- diagnostics (R1-P2-001, R3-P2-001).** Two message fixes: the sibling-link refusal at `:478` should say the link resolves back inside the tree, and the missing-engine refusal at `pre-commit:153` should carry a fix line.","+","+**Lane D -- portability and checklist (R4-P2-001, R7-P2-001).** Change `pin.checkout` to the relative form the docs recommend, and narrow the phase-003 criterion's third pattern so the tick reproduces.","+","+## 5. Spec Seed","+","+- The packet's phase 006 goal should record that a hook entrypoint's failure mode is part of the contract, not an implementation detail: the same evaluator must fail the same way through every entrypoint.","+- The packet should state that a completion criterion is a command a later reader re-runs, so a pattern that can drift into a false hit is a defect in the criterion rather than in the tree.","+- The packet should record that a manifest field reaching a subprocess is untrusted input even when the manifest is committed.","+","+## 6. Plan Seed","+","+1. Fix the two hook fail-open arms and the card-guard skip, with one test each.","+2. Add `--end-of-options` to the pinned-blob reader and extend `assertSafeToPlan`.","+3. Correct the two misleading diagnostics.","+4. Switch `pin.checkout` to the relative form and re-run `status --audit`.","+5. Narrow the phase-003 criterion and re-tick it from a clean run.","+6. Re-run `node --test .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/overlay-engine-*.test.cjs` and `validate.sh --recursive --strict` outside this lineage.","+","+## 7. Traceability Status","+","+| Protocol | Status | Evidence |","+|----------|--------|----------|","+| `checklist_evidence` | partial | Four of six packet criteria executed read-only and all four pass; phase 003's first criterion prints one hit where it promises none (R7-P2-001); two criteria need execution and could not run here |","+| `spec_code` | pass | Every documented LAYOUT form, exit code and backup path matches the code |","+| `decision_alignment` | pass | D1 through D4 hold in the tree; D5 and D6 are out of this review's scope |","+| `integration_naming` | pass | Every hook, plugin, command and doc surface is cited by path |","+","+Unresolved gaps: the two unrun criteria, and the phase-003 criterion that does not reproduce.","+","+## 8. Deferred Items","+","+- **`node --test .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/overlay-engine-*.test.cjs` was not run.** The suites write fixtures outside this lineage's write surface. Every assertion cited in this run was read from the suite source. This is the packet's first completion criterion and it remains unverified by execution.","+- **`validate.sh --recursive --strict` was not run.** Forbidden by the dispatch. This is the packet's sixth completion criterion and it remains unverified.","+- **The `sniffPayload` patch path is untested.** `barter-overlay-guard-core.cjs:129-138` scans `command`, `input` and `patch` for `*** Add File:` markers, but the test exercises only `filePath` and `path` payloads. No evidence in this tree shows which field name the OpenCode patch tool uses, so the gap is recorded as unverified coverage rather than a finding.","+- **The duplicated session-directory fallback is not a finding.** `barter-overlay-guard.js:26-28` and `barter-git-write-gate.js:34-36` carry the same three lines with no behavioural divergence; it is cleanup.","+- **The `.git/hooks` symlink install mode is a latent hazard.** `pre-commit:6` computes `TREE_ROOT` as `$SCRIPT_DIR/../../..`, correct for the `core.hooksPath` install in use but one level high for a `.git/hooks` symlink. The repository does not use that mode.","+","+## 9. Audit Appendix","+","+**Convergence.** `newFindingsRatio` by iteration: 1.0, 0.5, 0.333, 0.25, 0.333, 0.143, 0.125, 0.111. The reducer's `convergenceScore` finished at 0.889 against a 0.10 threshold, so the run did not converge on the score. It stopped because all four canonical dimensions were covered and the remaining findings are all P2. That is the honest stop reason: dimension coverage, not convergence.","+","+**Replay validation.** The reducer was re-run after every gateway append and reported `corruptionCount: 0` on every pass. The ledger holds nine events: one config row and eight iteration records, each with the full route proof (`mode=review`, `target_agent=deep-review`, `agent_definition_loaded=true`, `resolved_route`). Each delta's first row is byte-identical to the record handed to the gateway.","+","+**Coverage.** correctness (iterations 1, 3, 4), security (2, 5, 6), traceability (7), maintainability (8). All three frontier nodes carry at least two dimensions.","+","+**Prior-generation re-verification.** All 16 prior findings were re-checked against the current tree and all 16 are fixed. The evidence is in the `Confirmed-Clean Surfaces` section of each iteration file.","+","+**Recorded conflict.** The loop protocol's synthesis Step 6 asks for `status: \"complete\"` in `deep-review-config.json`. The `@deep-review` persona's write-safety table lists the config as read-only and forbids writing it. The persona's limit was followed: the config was left untouched, and the completed status is carried by the ledger and the dashboard the reducer derives from it. This conflict is recorded here rather than resolved silently.","+","+**Dimension rotation note.** Iteration 8 kept the reducer's node (F-1-004) but took maintainability rather than the traceability dimension the projection named, because traceability was already covered and maintainability was the only dimension still listed as remaining. Recorded in `iterations/iteration-008.md` under Edge Cases.","+","+**Write surface.** Every file this run created or modified sits under `specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/deepseek-flash-max`. No review target, config, registry, reducer output, dashboard, report, command, skill, canonical agent or runtime mirror was modified by this run."]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/opus-medium/deep-review-audit-ledger/frames/0000000000000006.frame","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":1,"lines":["+{\"canonical_event_bytes\":\"\",\"canonical_event_hash\":\"65cdec97b14da7c9a7640765ad6081054de741b4204b39323c665ed81a3db919\",\"decision_digest\":\"5157174336f82d574cc42535add99f1309f113ac5fa68277743553878ceacc97\",\"frame_version\":1,\"ledger_id\":\"deep-review-audit-ledger\",\"prev_record_hash\":\"65aa25c033b3b0d60c0a1e9c7c004062e4590fafad1c396671b730155ebdf86d\",\"record_hash\":\"6be0e8eb7b69c865169a28e61b65a56a4e990edf8a215def2ac0aa02e96eaeda\",\"sequence\":6}"]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/opus-medium/deep-review-dashboard.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":18,"oldLines":7,"newStart":18,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - Review Target: specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout (spec-folder)"," - Started: 2026-11-20T16:34:59.815Z"," - Status: INITIALIZED","-- Iteration: 3 of 24","+- Iteration: 4 of 24"," - Provisional Verdict: CONDITIONAL"," - hasSearchDebt: true"," - hasAdvisories: false"]},{"oldStart":46,"oldLines":7,"newStart":46,"newLines":7,"lines":[" |----------|------:|"," | P0 (Blockers) | 0 |"," | P1 (Required) | 0 |","-| P2 (Suggestions) | 5 |","+| P2 (Suggestions) | 7 |"," | Resolved | 0 |"," "," <!-- /ANCHOR:findings-summary -->"]},{"oldStart":58,"oldLines":6,"newStart":58,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | 1 | Frontier node F-1-001: correctness | correctness | 1.00 | 0/0/2 | complete |"," | 2 | Frontier node F-1-003: correctness | correctness | 0.50 | 0/0/2 | complete |"," | 3 | Frontier node F-1-005: correctness | correctness | 0.33 | 0/0/2 | complete |","+| 4 | Frontier node F-1-007: traceability | traceability | 0.25 | 0/0/2 | complet