wStart":15,"newLines":6,"lines":[" "," <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->"," ## Task Notation","-<!-- FILL: Keep the prefix table and add the two shell variables this task list uses. GOOD: `R` is `scripts/rotate-logs.sh`. `A` is `logs/archive/`. WEAK: Variables are defined below. -->"," "," | Prefix | Meaning |"," |--------|---------|"]},{"oldStart":31,"oldLines":41,"newStart":30,"newLines":37,"lines":[" "," <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->"," ## Phase 1: Setup","-<!-- FILL: Replace the sample tasks with the real setup steps. Each task names a file and a verify command. GOOD: T001 Confirm `logs/archive/` holds 10 archives. Verify: `ls logs/archive | wc -l` prints 10. WEAK: T001 Set up the project. -->"," ","-- [ ] T001 Create project structure (`<folder>`). Verify: `ls <folder>` lists it.","-- [ ] T002 Install dependencies (`<manifest>`). Verify: `<install command>` exits 0.","-- [ ] T003 [P] Configure development tools (`<config>`). Verify: `<tool> --version` exits 0.","+- [x] T001 Bring the worktree branch current with local main (`worktrees/481-overlay-framework-root-layout`). Verify: `git -C <worktree> log -1 --format=%h` prints `b4799f7d547`.","+- [x] T002 Take the baseline gates on the worktree at main tip (`plan.md` §2). Verify: the engine suite prints `tests 262`, the guard suite `tests 20`, the contract test `tests 9`.","+- [x] T003 Confirm each item before fixing it (`spec.md` Measured Behavior). Verify: each item has a quoted command output there."," <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->"," "," ---"," "," <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->"," ## Phase 2: Implementation","-<!-- FILL: Write one implementation task per file change. Add a `Verify:` line with the command and its expected output. GOOD: T002 Add the `--keep <n>` branch. Verify: `--keep 3` leaves 3 archives. WEAK: T002 Implement the feature. -->"," ","-- [ ] T004 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 1]","-- [ ] T005 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 2]","-- [ ] T006 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 3]","-- [ ] T007 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Add error handling]","+- [ ] T004 [P] Resolve a pinned commit without reading `FETCH_HEAD`, from the consumer, a local upstream checkout or a checked fetch, and refuse naming every place looked (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/release-update.cjs`), with a stale-`FETCH_HEAD` test (`release-update.test.cjs`). Verify: the new test fails on the unfixed engine and passes after.","+- [ ] T005 [P] Run scope discovery once at the fan-out root and hand the list to every lineage config through an optional runner input (`deep-review.yaml`, `fanout-run.cjs`), with a test and the contract docs in step. Verify: the new test passes and a run without the input writes `reviewScopeFiles: []` as before.","+- [ ] T006 [P] Probe the top level in `stagedUnownedChanges` with `gitTopLevelOrNull` (`overlay-engine.cjs`), with a real linked-worktree commit test. Verify: the new test fails on the unfixed engine and passes after.","+- [ ] T007 [P] Replace the bare `generate-context.js <spec-folder>` line with the `--json` form (`.skilled/skills/sk-git/references/large-reorg-playbook.md`). Verify: the new form exits 0 on this phase folder."," <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->"," "," ---"," "," <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->"," ## Phase 3: Verification","-<!-- FILL: Write one verification task per requirement. Each one runs a command. GOOD: T003 Run both invocations. Verify: `ls logs/archive | wc -l` prints 3 and 10. WEAK: T003 Test everything. -->"," ","-- [ ] T008 Test happy path manually (`<file>`). Verify: `<command>` prints <expected output>.","-- [ ] T009 Test edge cases (`<test>`). Verify: `<test command>` exits 0.","-- [ ] T010 Update documentation (`<doc>`). Verify: `rg -n '<term>' <doc>` prints one line.","+- [ ] T008 Run an `@review` pass on the branch diff and fix until it approves. Verify: its final `Review status:` line is a pass.","+- [ ] T009 Rerun the gates on the branch, merge into main, and rerun them on merged main (`plan.md` §2). Verify: every gate exits 0 at or above its baseline count.","+- [ ] T010 Strict-validate this phase, phases 010 and 011, and the parent recursively. Verify: every run prints `RESULT: PASSED`."," <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->"," "," ---"," "," <!-- ANCHOR:completion -->"," ## Completion Criteria","-<!-- FILL: Keep the three completion lines and add the one artifact that proves the phase is done. GOOD: `--keep 3` leaves 3 archives and the suite passes. WEAK: Work is complete. -->"," "," - [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`"," - [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining"]},{"oldStart":76,"oldLines":13,"newStart":71,"newLines":9,"lines":[" "," <!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->"," ## Cross-References","-<!-- FILL: Name the spec and plan files. Add the decision record when the packet has one. GOOD: Specification: `spec.md`. Plan: `plan.md`. WEAK: See the other docs. -->"," "," - **Specification**: See `spec.md`"," - **Plan**: See `plan.md`"," <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->"," "," ---","-","-","-"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/009-skilled-open-items/tasks.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019ZvnvWn3KgRtKzWdYCwCNW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
