{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChEXAucBpnUXtRtyHLEoB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01K7pckHoxKQjvGQFmQFFU5z","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled; L=specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/opus-medium; E=.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs; H=barter/ai-speckit/overlays/root/opencode/scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit; S6=specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/006-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md; grep -n \"pre-commit\\` keeps its own top-level probe\" $S6 | cut -c1-80; cat > $L/iterations/iteration-005.md <<EOF\n# Iteration 005 - Frontier node F-1-001: security\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Lineage: opus-medium, session fanout-opus-medium-1795192401900-xpt66n\n- Node: F-1-001 (engine), dimension security\n- Review focus addressed: path safety and hook fail-open or fail-closed behavior. Verified the phase 006 outside-repository refusal at resolveOverlayDir (prior R1-P2-001 sibling variant) and overlayOutside on the context (prior R13-P2-001), then probed the engine's commit check under the environment git gives a hook.\n- Sources: steer.md absent; strategy; dashboard frontier block (active node F-1-001, security).\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- \\`$E:465-545\\` (resolveOverlayDir, gitTopLevelOrNull, createContext)\n- \\`$E:4227-4231\\` (runGit), \\`$E:5820-5823\\` (gitTextOrNull), \\`$E:5524-5527\\` (isVendoredKey)\n- \\`$E:5862-5895\\` (stagedUnownedChanges)\n- \\`$E:6152-6159\\` (containedOverlayPath)\n- \\`$H:148-170\\` (Barter commit hook calls engine pre-commit with the hook's environment)\n- \\`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/overlay-engine-strict-writes.test.cjs:624-639, 763-800\\`\n- \\`$S6\\` Known Limitation 1\n- Probes (temp folders under /tmp only): (a) a git repository with a pre-commit hook printing its environment, committed from the main checkout and from a linked worktree; (b) a copy of the strict-writes fixture (sibling overlay folder, git at the workspace, tree in a subfolder, an unowned vendored edit staged) running \\`overlay-engine.cjs pre-commit --root <tree>\\` with and without \\`GIT_DIR\\` set.\n\n## Findings by Severity\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\n1. **The engine's commit check allows every unowned vendored change when git runs it from a hook in a linked worktree** -- $E:5864 -- stagedUnownedChanges asks \\`git rev-parse --show-toplevel\\` through runGit (\\`$E:4228\\`), which passes the caller's environment. Git exports \\`GIT_DIR\\` to hooks in a linked worktree (probe a: \\`GIT_DIR=.../.git/worktrees/wt\\`, and \\`git -C sub rev-parse --show-toplevel\\` printed \\`.../wt/sub\\`). With \\`GIT_DIR\\` set and no work tree, git reports the working folder as the top level, so for a tree in a subfolder the prefix becomes empty, the staged names keep their \\`skilled/\\` prefix, isVendoredKey (\\`$E:5524\\`) matches none of them, and the function returns no changes. Probe b: the same staged unowned edit gives exit 1 \"refuse: staged change to .skilled/skills/hub/fix.md ...\" without \\`GIT_DIR\\` and exit 0 \"allow\" with it. Barter's commit hook calls the engine with the hook's environment (\\`$H:164\\`), its tree is the \\`skilled/\\` subfolder, and \\`status\\` does not check unowned paths, so in a linked ai-speckit worktree the strict-writes commit gate passes an edit no overlay owns. The engine already strips these variables in gitTopLevelOrNull (\\`$E:524-527\\` comment: \"A git hook exports GIT_DIR without GIT_WORK_TREE\") but this probe does not use it. Phase 006 records the probe as Known Limitation 1 and predicts it \"would likely ... refuse\"; the observed effect is a silent allow, the opposite posture.\n   - Finding class: fail-open-gate (pre-existing code, outcome mis-recorded by phase 006)\n   - Scope proof: stagedUnownedChanges is the only caller of the hook-environment top-level probe on the commit path; gitTopLevelOrNull is used only by resolveOverlayDir.\n   - Affected surface hints: overlay-engine.cjs stagedUnownedChanges and gitTextOrNull callers on the pre-commit path; Barter pre-commit hook; 006 implementation-summary Known Limitation 1; a strict-writes test running pre-commit with GIT_DIR set.\n   - Case: in a linked worktree of ai-speckit, edit skilled/.skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md (no overlay owns it), stage it and run git commit; the hook's pre-commit step prints allow and the commit lands.\n\n\\`\\`\\`json\n{\"type\":\"fail-open-gate\",\"claim\":\"Under a hook-exported GIT_DIR, overlay-engine pre-commit returns allow for a staged unowned vendored change in a tree below the git top level\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"$E:5864\",\"$E:4228\",\"$E:5524\",\"$H:164\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"Checked whether the Barter hook unsets GIT_DIR (it does not, $H:148-170), whether git exports GIT_DIR in a linked worktree hook (it does, probe a), whether the main checkout is affected (it is not: GIT_DIR unset there, probe a), and reproduced end to end with the engine (probe b)\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"If Barter never commits from a linked worktree the path is unreachable in practice; sk-git's numbered worktrees make it reachable\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P1\",\"confidence\":0.85,\"downgradeTrigger\":\"Evidence that ai-speckit commits never run from a linked worktree, or that the hook path clears GIT_DIR before calling the engine\"}\n\\`\\`\\`\n\nSkeptic/referee (compact): the skeptic case is that GIT_DIR is not exported for a normal checkout, which probe a confirms, so the main checkout is safe; the referee keeps P1 because the linked-worktree case is a supported workflow and the failure is a silent pass of a gate whose sibling bug (prior R2-P1-001) was itself rated P1.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **An overlayDir inside the tree that is a link to a folder outside the repository skips the outside-repository refusal** -- $E:487 -- resolveOverlayDir runs the git-repository containment check only for a \\`../<name>\\` sibling (\\`$E:487-516\\`). An in-tree value such as \\`ov\\` returns at the final line without resolving links, and createContext computes overlayOutside lexically (\\`$E:524\\`), so a tree whose \\`ov\\` is a link to a folder outside the repository is accepted as an in-tree overlay folder. The reason the sibling case is refused, \"its overlays and pin are never committed with the tree\" (\\`$E:505-507\\`), applies equally: git commits the link, not the overlays.\n   - Finding class: containment-gap\n   - Scope proof: the only canonicalPath call in resolveOverlayDir sits inside the sibling branch.\n   - Affected surface hints: resolveOverlayDir final branch; createContext overlayOutside.\n   - Case: skilled/.skilled-overlays.json names \"ov\", and skilled/ov is a link to ~/private-overlays; status and apply run against it, and a commit carries only the link.\n\n## Prior-Finding Verification\n\n- R1-P2-001 sibling variant (the sibling check accepted ../.git and other non-overlay siblings): FIXED. A sibling outside the tree must sit inside the tree's git top level and not under its \\`.git\\` (\\`$E:505-513\\`), and a dangling or looping link is refused (\\`$E:493-499\\`). Tests at strict-writes.test.cjs:786 cover the outside-repository refusal.\n- R13-P2-001 (overlay-outside test recomputed in four command paths): FIXED. overlayOutside is set once in createContext (\\`$E:524\\`) and read at \\`$E:4631, 5286, 5883\\`; grep finds no other recomputation.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- spec_code: partial. Phase 006's outside-repository refusal matches its claim; its Known Limitation 1 predicts a refusal where the code allows (P1 above).\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- Barter commit hook \\`$H:164\\` -> \\`overlay-engine.cjs pre-commit --root \"\\$TREE_ROOT\"\\` with the inherited hook environment.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- A tree in no git repository keeps any sibling folder by design (\\`$E:508-509\\`).\n- stagedUnownedChanges also returns no changes when \\`git diff --cached\\` fails (\\`$E:5869\\`), another silent allow on a git error; folded into the P1's affected surfaces rather than raised separately.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- containedOverlayPath keeps relayout moves inside the overlay folder (\\`$E:6152-6159\\` through sourceRelative).\n- resolveOverlayDir refuses absolute, backslash and NUL values (\\`$E:483-485\\`).\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Main-checkout commit gate bypass: git exports no GIT_DIR there (probe a), and the engine refuses (probe b, plain run).\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: security\n- Focus area: frontier node F-1-005 (Barter hooks: guard core and git-write gate fail-open posture)\n- Reason: the P1 opens the question of what each Barter hook does when its lookup or the engine fails\n- Rotation status: F-1-001 correctness and security done\n- Required evidence: barter-overlay-guard-core.cjs and the OpenCode plugin error path; barter-git-write-gate.mjs aiSpeckitRoot null path\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Write iteration 5 narrative"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1384,"cache_read_input_tokens":238363,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1384},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"faa6b93c-ce84-436d-8875-372fa8efb878","uuid":"e259a1ad-5551-498d-9cad-97f79b8b4755","timestamp":"2026-11-20T16:48:31.618Z","request_id":"req_011ChEXAuLotMEdZrLd41cxu","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01K7pckHoxKQjvGQFmQFFU5z":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled; L=specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/opus-medium; E=.