{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K7pckHoxKQjvGQFmQFFU5z","type":"tool_result","content":"126:1. **`pre-commit` keeps its own top-level probe.** `stagedUnownedChanges` st\nok","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"faa6b93c-ce84-436d-8875-372fa8efb878","uuid":"bc8a94db-7d7f-4a92-b9fc-726281236132","timestamp":"2026-11-20T16:48:32.811Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"126:1. **`pre-commit` keeps its own top-level probe.** `stagedUnownedChanges` st\nok","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/opus-medium/iterations/iteration-005.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":84,"lines":["+# Iteration 005 - Frontier node F-1-001: security","+","+## Dispatcher","+","+- Lineage: opus-medium, session fanout-opus-medium-1795192401900-xpt66n","+- Node: F-1-001 (engine), dimension security","+- Review focus addressed: path safety and hook fail-open or fail-closed behavior. Verified the phase 006 outside-repository refusal at resolveOverlayDir (prior R1-P2-001 sibling variant) and overlayOutside on the context (prior R13-P2-001), then probed the engine's commit check under the environment git gives a hook.","+- Sources: steer.md absent; strategy; dashboard frontier block (active node F-1-001, security).","+","+## Files Reviewed","+","+- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:465-545` (resolveOverlayDir, gitTopLevelOrNull, createContext)","+- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:4227-4231` (runGit), `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:5820-5823` (gitTextOrNull), `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:5524-5527` (isVendoredKey)","+- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:5862-5895` (stagedUnownedChanges)","+- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:6152-6159` (containedOverlayPath)","+- `barter/ai-speckit/overlays/root/opencode/scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit:148-170` (Barter commit hook calls engine pre-commit with the hook's environment)","+- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/overlay-engine-strict-writes.test.cjs:624-639, 763-800`","+- `specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/006-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md` Known Limitation 1","+- Probes (temp folders under /tmp only): (a) a git repository with a pre-commit hook printing its environment, committed from the main checkout and from a linked worktree; (b) a copy of the strict-writes fixture (sibling overlay folder, git at the workspace, tree in a subfolder, an unowned vendored edit staged) running `overlay-engine.cjs pre-commit --root <tree>` with and without `GIT_DIR` set.","+","+## Findings by Severity","+","+### P0 Findings","+","+None.","+","+### P1 Findings","+","+1. **The engine's commit check allows every unowned vendored change when git runs it from a hook in a linked worktree** -- .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:5864 -- stagedUnownedChanges asks `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` through runGit (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:4228`), which passes the caller's environment. Git exports `GIT_DIR` to hooks in a linked worktree (probe a: `GIT_DIR=.../.git/worktrees/wt`, and `git -C sub rev-parse --show-toplevel` printed `.../wt/sub`). With `GIT_DIR` set and no work tree, git reports the working folder as the top level, so for a tree in a subfolder the prefix becomes empty, the staged names keep their `skilled/` prefix, isVendoredKey (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:5524`) matches none of them, and the function returns no changes. Probe b: the same staged unowned edit gives exit 1 \"refuse: staged change to .skilled/skills/hub/fix.md ...\" without `GIT_DIR` and exit 0 \"allow\" with it. Barter's commit hook calls the engine with the hook's environment (`barter/ai-speckit/overlays/root/opencode/scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit:164`), its tree is the `skilled/` subfolder, and `status` does not check unowned paths, so in a linked ai-speckit worktree the strict-writes commit gate passes an edit no overlay owns. The engine already strips these variables in gitTopLevelOrNull (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:524-527` comment: \"A git hook exports GIT_DIR without GIT_WORK_TREE\") but this probe does not use it. Phase 006 records the probe as Known Limitation 1 and predicts it \"would likely ... refuse\"; the observed effect is a silent allow, the opposite posture.","+   - Finding class: fail-open-gate (pre-existing code, outcome mis-recorded by phase 006)","+   - Scope proof: stagedUnownedChanges is the only caller of the hook-environment top-level probe on the commit path; gitTopLevelOrNull is used only by resolveOverlayDir.","+   - Affected surface hints: overlay-engine.cjs stagedUnownedChanges and gitTextOrNull callers on the pre-commit path; Barter pre-commit hook; 006 implementation-summary Known Limitation 1; a strict-writes test running pre-commit with GIT_DIR set.","+   - Case: in a linked worktree of ai-speckit, edit skilled/.skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md (no overlay owns it), stage it and run git commit; the hook's pre-commit step prints allow and the commit lands.","+","+```json","+{\"type\":\"fail-open-gate\",\"claim\":\"Under a hook-exported GIT_DIR, overlay-engine pre-commit returns allow for a staged unowned vendored change in a tree below the git top level\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:5864\",\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:4228\",\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:5524\",\"barter/ai-speckit/overlays/root/opencode/scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit:164\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"Checked whether the Barter hook unsets GIT_DIR (it does not, barter/ai-speckit/overlays/root/opencode/scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit:148-170), whether git exports GIT_DIR in a linked worktree hook (it does, probe a), whether the main checkout is affected (it is not: GIT_DIR unset there, probe a), and reproduced end to end with the engine (probe b)\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"If Barter never commits from a linked worktree the path is unreachable in practice; sk-git's numbered worktrees make it reachable\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P1\",\"confidence\":0.85,\"downgradeTrigger\":\"Evidence that ai-speckit commits never run from a linked worktree, or that the hook path clears GIT_DIR before calling the engine\"}","+```","+","+Skeptic/referee (compact): the skeptic case is that GIT_DIR is not exported for a normal checkout, which probe a confirms, so the main checkout is safe; the referee keeps P1 because the linked-worktree case is a supported workflow and the failure is a silent pass of a gate whose sibling bug (prior R2-P1-001) was itself rated P1.","+","+### P2 Findings","+","+1. **An overlayDir inside the tree that is a link to a folder outside the repository skips the outside-repository refusal** -- .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:487 -- resolveOverlayDir runs the git-repository containment check only for a `../<name>` sibling (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:487-516`). An in-tree value such as `ov` returns at the final line without resolving links, and createContext computes overlayOutside lexically (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:524`), so a tree whose `ov` is a link to a folder outside the repository is accepted as an in-tree overlay folder. The reason the sibling case is refused, \"its overlays and pin are never committed with the tree\" (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:505-507`), applies equally: git commits the link, not the overlays.","+   - Finding class: containment-gap","+   - Scope proof: the only canonicalPath call in resolveOverlayDir sits inside the sibling branch.","+   - Affected surface hints: resolveOverlayDir final branch; createContext overlayOutside.","+   - Case: skilled/.skilled-overlays.json names \"ov\", and skilled/ov is a link to ~/private-overlays; status and apply run against it, and a commit carries only the link.","+","+## Prior-Finding Verification","+","+- R1-P2-001 sibling variant (the sibling check accepted ../.git and other non-overlay siblings): FIXED. A sibling outside the tree must sit inside the tree's git top level and not under its `.git` (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:505-513`), and a dangling or looping link is refused (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:493-499`). Tests at strict-writes.test.cjs:786 cover the outside-repository refusal.","+- R13-P2-001 (overlay-outside test recomputed in four command paths): FIXED. overlayOutside is set once in createContext (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:524`) and read at `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:4631, 5286, 5883`; grep finds no other recomputation.","+","+## Traceability Checks","+","+- spec_code: partial. Phase 006's outside-repository refusal matches its claim; its Known Limitation 1 predicts a refusal where the code allows (P1 above).","+","+## Integration Evidence","+","+- Barter commit hook `barter/ai-speckit/overlays/root/opencode/scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit:164` -> `overlay-engine.cjs pre-commit --root \"$TREE_ROOT\"` with the inherited hook environment.","+","+## Edge Cases","+","+- A tree in no git repository keeps any sibling folder by design (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:508-509`).","+- stagedUnownedChanges also returns no changes when `git diff --cached` fails (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:5869`), another silent allow on a git error; folded into the P1's affected surfaces rather than raised separately.","+","+## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces","+","+- containedOverlayPath keeps relayout moves inside the overlay folder (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:6152-6159` through sourceRelative).","+- resolveOverlayDir refuses absolute, backslash and NUL values (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:483-485`).","+","+## Ruled Out","+","+- Main-checkout commit gate bypass: git exports no GIT_DIR there (probe a), and the engine refuses (probe b, plain run).","+","+## Next Focus","+","+- Dimension: security","+- Focus area: frontier node F-1-005 (Barter hooks: guard core and git-write gate fail-open posture)","+- Reason: the P1 opens the question of what each Barter hook does when its lookup or the engine fails","+- Rotation status: F-1-001 correctness and security done","+- Required evidence: barter-overlay-guard-core.cjs and the OpenCode plugin error path; barter-git-write-gate.mjs aiSpeckitRoot null path","+","+Review verdict: CONDITIONAL"]}],"created":true}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/opus-medium/iterations/iteration-005.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01K7pckHoxKQjvGQFmQFFU5z","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
