{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014E8zcKLjWnwzHXFfcb45Nj","type":"tool_result","content":"9\n */\nfunction trackedTreeKeys(root) {\n  // A temporary folder sits behind a link on some systems, so the tree's own\n  // path is resolved before it is compared with the repository's top level.\n  const projectRoot = canonicalPath(root);\n  const top = gitTextOrNull(projectRoot, ['rev-parse', '--show-toplevel']);\n  if (top === null) return [];\n  const topLevel = canonicalPath(top.trim());\n  const prefix = toPosix(path.relative(topLevel, projectRoot));\n  const listing = gitTextOrNull(topLevel, ['ls-files', '-z']);\n  if (!listing) return [];\n  const keys = [];\n5971:function trackedTreeKeys(root) {","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"faa6b93c-ce84-436d-8875-372fa8efb878","uuid":"62f56053-6bce-434f-a356-81707a8ad08f","timestamp":"2026-11-20T16:48:51.014Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"9\n */\nfunction trackedTreeKeys(root) {\n  // A temporary folder sits behind a link on some systems, so the tree's own\n  // path is resolved before it is compared with the repository's top level.\n  const projectRoot = canonicalPath(root);\n  const top = gitTextOrNull(projectRoot, ['rev-parse', '--show-toplevel']);\n  if (top === null) return [];\n  const topLevel = canonicalPath(top.trim());\n  const prefix = toPosix(path.relative(topLevel, projectRoot));\n  const listing = gitTextOrNull(topLevel, ['ls-files', '-z']);\n  if (!listing) return [];\n  const keys = [];\n5971:function trackedTreeKeys(root) {","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/opus-medium/iterations/iteration-005.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":9,"oldLines":7,"newStart":9,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ## Files Reviewed"," ","-- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:465-545` (resolveOverlayDir, gitTopLevelOrNull, createContext)","+- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:426-526` (resolveOverlayDir, gitTopLevelOrNull, createContext)"," - `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:4227-4231` (runGit), `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:5820-5823` (gitTextOrNull), `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:5524-5527` (isVendoredKey)"," - `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:5862-5895` (stagedUnownedChanges)"," - `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:6152-6159` (containedOverlayPath)"]},{"oldStart":26,"oldLines":7,"newStart":26,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ### P1 Findings"," ","-1. **The engine's commit check allows every unowned vendored change when git runs it from a hook in a linked worktree** -- .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:5864 -- stagedUnownedChanges asks `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` through runGit (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:4228`), which passes the caller's environment. Git exports `GIT_DIR` to hooks in a linked worktree (probe a: `GIT_DIR=.../.git/worktrees/wt`, and `git -C sub rev-parse --show-toplevel` printed `.../wt/sub`). With `GIT_DIR` set and no work tree, git reports the working folder as the top level, so for a tree in a subfolder the prefix becomes empty, the staged names keep their `skilled/` prefix, isVendoredKey (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:5524`) matches none of them, and the function returns no changes. Probe b: the same staged unowned edit gives exit 1 \"refuse: staged change to .skilled/skills/hub/fix.md ...\" without `GIT_DIR` and exit 0 \"allow\" with it. Barter's commit hook calls the engine with the hook's environment (`barter/ai-speckit/overlays/root/opencode/scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit:164`), its tree is the `skilled/` subfolder, and `status` does not check unowned paths, so in a linked ai-speckit worktree the strict-writes commit gate passes an edit no overlay owns. The engine already strips these variables in gitTopLevelOrNull (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:524-527` comment: \"A git hook exports GIT_DIR without GIT_WORK_TREE\") but this probe does not use it. Phase 006 records the probe as Known Limitation 1 and predicts it \"would likely ... refuse\"; the observed effect is a silent allow, the opposite posture.","+1. **The engine's commit check allows every unowned vendored change when git runs it from a hook in a linked worktree** -- .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:5864 -- stagedUnownedChanges asks `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` through runGit (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:4228`), which passes the caller's environment. Git exports `GIT_DIR` to hooks in a linked worktree (probe a: `GIT_DIR=.../.git/worktrees/wt`, and `git -C sub rev-parse --show-toplevel` printed `.../wt/sub`). With `GIT_DIR` set and no work tree, git reports the working folder as the top level, so for a tree in a subfolder the prefix becomes empty, the staged names keep their `skilled/` prefix, isVendoredKey (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:5524`) matches none of them, and the function returns no changes. Probe b: the same staged unowned edit gives exit 1 \"refuse: staged change to .skilled/skills/hub/fix.md ...\" without `GIT_DIR` and exit 0 \"allow\" with it. Barter's commit hook calls the engine with the hook's environment (`barter/ai-speckit/overlays/root/opencode/scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit:164`), its tree is the `skilled/` subfolder, and `status` does not check unowned paths, so in a linked ai-speckit worktree the strict-writes commit gate passes an edit no overlay owns. The engine already strips these variables in gitTopLevelOrNull (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:493` comment: \"A git hook exports GIT_DIR without GIT_WORK_TREE\") but this probe does not use it. Phase 006 records the probe as Known Limitation 1 and predicts it \"would likely ... refuse\"; the observed effect is a silent allow, the opposite posture.","    - Finding class: fail-open-gate (pre-existing code, outcome mis-recorded by phase 006)","    - Scope proof: stagedUnownedChanges is the only caller of the hook-environment top-level probe on the commit path; gitTopLevelOrNull is used only by resolveOverlayDir.","    - Affected surface hints: overlay-engine.cjs stagedUnownedChanges and gitTextOrNull callers on the pre-commit path; Barter pre-commit hook; 006 implementation-summary Known Limitation 1; a strict-writes test running pre-commit with GIT_DIR set."]},{"oldStart":40,"oldLines":7,"newStart":40,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ### P2 Findings"," ","-1. **An overlayDir inside the tree that is a link to a folder outside the repository skips the outside-repository refusal** -- .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:487 -- resolveOverlayDir runs the git-repository containment check only for a `../<name>` sibling (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:487-516`). An in-tree value such as `ov` returns at the final line without resolving links, and createContext computes overlayOutside lexically (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:524`), so a tree whose `ov` is a link to a folder outside the repository is accepted as an in-tree overlay folder. The reason the sibling case is refused, \"its overlays and pin are never committed with the tree\" (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:505-507`), applies equally: git commits the link, not the overlays.","+1. **An overlayDir inside the tree that is a link to a folder outside the repository skips the outside-repository refusal** -- .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:450 -- resolveOverlayDir runs the git-repository containment check only for a `../<name>` sibling (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:450-479`). An in-tree value such as `ov` returns at the final line without resolving links, and createContext computes overlayOutside lexically (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:524`), so a tree whose `ov` is a link to a folder outside the repository is accepted as an in-tree overlay folder. The reason the sibling case is refused, \"its overlays and pin are never committed with the tree\" (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:466-468`), applies equally: git commits the link, not the overlays.","    - Finding class: containment-gap","    - Scope proof: the only canonicalPath call in resolveOverlayDir sits inside the sibling branch.","    - Affected surface hints: resolveOverlayDir final branch; createContext overlayOutside."]},{"oldStart":48,"oldLines":7,"newStart":48,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ## Prior-Finding Verification"," ","-- R1-P2-001 sibling variant (the sibling check accepted ../.git and other non-overlay siblings): FIXED. A sibling outside the tree must sit inside the tree's git top level and not under its `.git` (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:505-513`), and a dangling or looping link is refused (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:493-499`). Tests at strict-writes.test.cjs:786 cover the outside-repository refusal.","+- R1-P2-001 sibling variant (the sibling check accepted ../.git and other non-overlay siblings): FIXED. A sibling outside the tree must sit inside the tree's git top level and not under its `.git` (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:466-474`), and a dangling or looping link is refused (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:455-460`). Tests at strict-writes.test.cjs:786 cover the outside-repository refusal."," - R13-P2-001 (overlay-outside test recomputed in four command paths): FIXED. overlayOutside is set once in createContext (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:524`) and read at `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:4631, 5286, 5883`; grep finds no other recomputation."," "," ## Traceability Checks"]},{"oldStart":61,"oldLines":13,"newStart":61,"newLines":13,"lines":[" "," ## Edge Cases"," ","-- A tree in no git repository keeps any sibling folder by design (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:508-509`).","-- stagedUnownedChanges also returns no changes when `git diff --cached` fails (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:5869`), another silent allow on a git error; folded into the P1's affected surfaces rather than raised separately.","+- A tree in no git repository keeps any sibling folder by design (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:469-470`).","+- stagedUnownedChanges also returns no changes when `git diff --cached` fails (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:5868`), another silent allow on a git error; folded into the P1's affected surfaces rather than raised separately."," "," ## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces"," "," - containedOverlayPath keeps relayout moves inside the overlay folder (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:6152-6159` through sourceRelative).","-- resolveOverlayDir refuses absolute, backslash and NUL values (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:483-485`).","+- resolveOverlayDir refuses absolute, backslash and NUL values (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs:440-441`)."," "," ## Ruled Out"," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/opus-medium/iterations/iteration-005.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014E8zcKLjWnwzHXFfcb45Nj","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
