{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014ZpvNnsS8aRsNYVWgFmhUs","type":"tool_result","content":"The value is a path relative to the tree root, written with forward slashes. It names a folder inside the tree, or a folder beside it as a direct sibling `../<name>`, such as `../team-overlays`. With no setting file the folder is `skilled-overlays/`. A backslash or an absolute path is refused with `.skilled-overlays.json must name a relative folder with forward slashes: <value>`. A deeper path such as `../../x` or `../a/b`, the tree itself, a sibling that links back into the tree and a dangling link are refused with `.skilled-overlays.json names a folder outside the tree root: <value>`. When the tree is inside a git repository, a sibling folder must sit inside that repository too: a sibling that resolves outside the repository's top level, or into its `.git`, is refused by every command with `.skilled-overlays.json names a folder outside the git repository at <top>: <value>`. A tree in no git repository keeps any direct sibling, and `pre-commit` keeps its own check, which exits 2 with `the overlay folder must sit inside the same git repository as the tree`. The folder holds:\n\n| File | What it holds |\n| `.skilled-overlays.json` is refused | The setting must name a relative folder with forward slashes, inside the tree or a direct sibling `../<name>`. A backslash or an absolute path prints `.skilled-overlays.json must name a relative folder with forward slashes: <value>`, and a deeper path such as `../../x` prints `.skilled-overlays.json names a folder outside the tree root: <value>`. A folder outside the tree's git repository is refused by `pre-commit` with exit 2: `the overlay folder must sit inside the same git repository as the tree; <label> is outside the git repository at <top level>`. Fix the file, then rerun `/doctor:overlay status` |\n51:The value is a path relative to the tree root, written with forward slashes. It names a fold