{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChEXmp6HXghE3nvG6HSG5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YaLA5SP5p3KfSKJmiB1672","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled; L=specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/opus-medium; B=barter/ai-speckit/overlays; PG=$B/root/opencode/plugins/barter-overlay-guard.js; W=$B/framework/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/barter-git-write-gate.mjs; TG=$B/root/opencode/plugins/tests/barter-overlay-guard.test.cjs; TW=$B/root/opencode/plugins/tests/barter-git-write-gate.test.cjs; H=$B/root/opencode/scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit; cat > $L/iterations/iteration-007.md <<EOF\n# Iteration 007 - Frontier node F-1-005: security\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Lineage: opus-medium, session fanout-opus-medium-1795192401900-xpt66n\n- Node: F-1-005 (Barter hooks and hygiene, read-only nested repo), dimension security\n- Review focus addressed: hook fail-open or fail-closed behavior. Traced what each Barter hook does when its overlay lookup or its core fails, and verified prior R12-P2-001 (plugin tests stub the upstream bridge).\n- Sources: steer.md absent; strategy; registry frontier (F-1-005 next dimension security).\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- \\`$PG:9-50\\` (OpenCode edit guard plugin, warnCoreFailure)\n- \\`$W:177-200\\` (overlaysRootFor, aiSpeckitRoot), \\`$W:225-230\\` (sessionInside), \\`$W:1731-1739\\` (outsideRefusal), \\`$W:2153-2173, 2290-2306\\` (evaluateCommand and hook entry)\n- \\`$H:120-170\\` (commit hook)\n- \\`$TG:148-168\\` (real-bridge case), \\`$TW:59-180\\` (stub bridge at :84-87, :131-133, :175-177)\n- Test run: \\`node --test $TG\\` -> 3 of 3 pass, exit 0\n\n## Findings by Severity\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. R5-P1-001 (engine commit check allows under a hook-exported GIT_DIR) stays active; this iteration found no Barter hook step that would catch it, because the commit hook passes its environment straight to the engine (\\`$H:156-164\\`).\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n## Posture Map\n\n| Hook | On lookup or core failure | Evidence | Verdict |\n|------|---------------------------|----------|---------|\n| OpenCode edit guard plugin | Fails open: prints \"guard failed, allowing the edit\" to stderr and lets the write through | \\`$PG:19-22, 39-43\\` | By design and documented in the plugin comment (\\`$PG:12-14\\`); the commit gate is the backstop |\n| git-write gate | aiSpeckitRoot returns null when the manifest the setting names is missing (\\`$W:195-197\\`); sessionInside is then false (\\`$W:226\\`) and every git write gets outsideRefusal (\\`$W:1567, 1744\\`) | \\`$W:1731-1733\\` | Fails closed |\n| Commit hook, no manifest | Exit 1 when a vendored path is staged | \\`$H:134-143\\` | Fails closed |\n| Commit hook, engine error | Exit 1 on any non-zero status or pre-commit exit | \\`$H:156-168\\` | Fails closed |\n| Commit hook, linked worktree | Engine pre-commit prints allow (R5-P1-001) | iteration 5 probe | Fails open |\n\n## Prior-Finding Verification\n\n- R12-P2-001 (plugin tests stub the upstream bridge): FIXED for the class it named. \\`$TG:157-168\\` imports the applied guard plugin beside the real vendored v2-bridge.js. The git-write gate plugin tests still use a stub bridge (\\`$TW:84-87\\`), but both plugins import only the same definePlugin export, so a rename of that export now fails the guard plugin's real-bridge case. Not raised again.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- spec_code: pass. 007's decision \"Keep the setting-reading rule in each of the three hooks ... each keeps its fail-open or fail-closed posture\" matches the map above.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- OpenCode plugin -> \\`../../.skilled/hooks/barter-overlay-guard/lib/barter-overlay-guard-core.cjs\\` (\\`$PG:7\\`); git-write gate plugin -> \\`../skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/barter-git-write-gate.mjs\\`.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The guard's fail-open warning goes to stderr only; an agent runtime that hides plugin stderr shows no sign the guard is off. Recorded as an edge case: the plugin comment makes this an explicit trade-off.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- git-write gate null-root path, commit hook no-manifest and engine-error paths.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- git-write gate failing open when the overlay folder moves: it refuses every write instead.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: correctness\n- Focus area: frontier node F-1-007 (records), the registry's next node and dimension\n- Reason: registry frontier rotation\n- Rotation status: F-1-005 correctness and security done\n- Required evidence: 006, 007, 008 spec and tasks correctness of stated behavior and counts\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\nEOF\ncat > $L/prompts/spec-007.json <<EOF\n{\"iteration\":7,\"node\":\"F-1-005\",\"dimension\":\"security\",\"scope\":[\"$PG\",\"$W\",\"$H\"],\"priorWeighted\":15,\n\"filesReviewed\":[\"$PG:39\",\"$W:190\",\"$W:1731\",\"$H:134\",\"$TG:157\",\"$TW:84\"],\n\"findings\":[],\n\"traceability\":[{\"protocolId\":\"spec_code\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"gateClass\":\"hard\",\"applicable\":true,\"evidence\":[\"$PG:39\",\"$W:226\"],\"summary\":\"each hook keeps the posture 007 records\"}],\n\"novelty\":\"No new findings; posture map confirms R5-P1-001 is the only fail-open path; R12-P2-001 verified fixed.\",\n\"ledger\":[{\"bugClass\":\"fail_open_gate\",\"targetRefs\":[\"$W\"],\"hypothesis\":\"git-write gate fails open when the overlay lookup fails\",\"result\":\"null root refuses every write\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"$W:226\",\"$W:1731\"],\"disposition\":\"ruled_out\"},\n{\"bugClass\":\"test_coverage\",\"targetRefs\":[\"$TG\"],\"hypothesis\":\"plugin tests still cannot see a bridge rename\",\"result\":\"real-bridge case imports the applied plugin\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"$TG:157\"],\"disposition\":\"ruled_out\"}],\n\"ruledOut\":[{\"direction\":\"git-write gate fail-open on lookup failure\",\"reason\":\"sessionInside false refuses every git write\"}]}\nEOF\nnode $L/prompts/emit.cjs $L/prompts/spec-007.json $L 2026-11-20T17:02:00Z 2>&1 | cut -c1-60; node $L/prompts/graph.cjs $L 7 | cut -c1-60; node $L/prompts/conv.cjs $L 7 3 3","description":"Write, record, graph and converge iteration 7"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":831,"cache_read_input_tokens":287449,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":831},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"faa6b93c-ce84-436d-8875-372fa8efb878","uuid":"2a27f42a-5905-4404-8277-e979ddcd9a72","timestamp":"2026-11-20T16:56:03.941Z","request_id":"req_011ChEXmorPg94mfjfhc1jmt","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01YaLA5SP5p3KfSKJmiB1672":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled; L=specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/opus-medium; B=barter/ai-speckit/overlays; PG=$B/root/opencode/plugins/barter-overlay-guard.js; W=$B/framework/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/barter-git-write-gate.mjs; TG=$B/root/opencode/plugins/tests/barter-overlay-guard.test.cjs; TW=$B/root/opencode/plugins/tests/barter-git-write-gate.test.cjs; H=$B/root/opencode/scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit; cat > $L/iterations/iteration-007.md <<EOF\n# Iteration 007 - Frontier node F-1-005: security\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Lineage: opus-medium, session fanout-opus-medium-1795192401900-xpt66n\n- Node: F-1-005 (Barter hooks and hygiene, read-only nested repo), dimension security\n- Review focus addressed: hook fail-open or fail-closed behavior. Traced what each Barter hook does when its overlay lookup or its core fails, and verified prior R12-P2-001 (plugin tests stub the upstream bridge).\n- Sources: steer.md absent; strategy; registry frontier (F-