terations left for four nodes; each dimension got its own pass below.\n- Review focus addressed: traced phase 006 REQ-001 to REQ-008 to code and tests, checked the remediation commit 3aab896957e for comment hygiene and maintainability, and looked for the test that should have caught R5-P1-001.\n- Sources: steer.md absent; strategy; registry frontier (F-1-001 next traceability).\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- \\`$S/006-review-remediation/spec.md:128-140\\` (REQ-001..REQ-008)\n- \\`git show 3aab896957e\\` (engine +214 lines, follow-up and strict-writes tests); grep of its added comment lines for ephemeral ids\n- \\`$TS:817-877\\` (.git sibling test, hook GIT_DIR test, repository-boundary test)\n- \\`$TF:1171-1227\\` (relayoutWithFailingRename helper and its two uses)\n- \\`$E:170-177\\` (relativeKey), \\`$E:4652\\` (writeBackup), \\`$E:6420-6559\\` (rollbackRelayout, relayoutUnderLock)\n\n## Findings by Severity\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. R5-P1-001 stays active; finding 1 below names the test gap that let it through.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **The one test that runs the engine under a hook's GIT_DIR checks status's repository test, never pre-commit's ownership check** -- $TS:858 -- \"a sibling overlay folder inside the repository is kept when GIT_DIR comes from a hook\" sets GIT_DIR exactly as git does for a hook and even asserts the consequence that breaks pre-commit, that \\`git rev-parse --show-toplevel\\` reports the tree as the top level (\\`$TS:863-865\\`). It then runs only \\`status\\` (\\`$TS:868\\`). No test runs \\`pre-commit\\` with GIT_DIR set, so the suite stays green while that command prints allow for an unowned staged change (R5-P1-001, reproduced at iteration 5).\n   - Finding class: test-gap (refines R5-P1-001)\n   - Scope proof: grep for GIT_DIR in the doctor tests finds only \\`$TS:856-872\\`.\n   - Affected surface hints: overlay-engine-strict-writes.test.cjs hook-environment test; a pre-commit case beside it with a staged unowned edit.\n   - Case: copy the test at \\`$TS:858\\`, stage an unowned vendored edit and run pre-commit with the same env; it exits 0 with allow, and no existing test fails.\n\n## Traceability Pass\n\n- REQ-001 (relayout restore on mid-loop failure): code \\`$E:6512-6549\\`, tests \\`$TF:1196, 1212\\` and the relink case; pass.\n- REQ-002 (outside-repository sibling refused at context build): code \\`$E:466-474\\`, tests \\`$TS:786, 806, 817\\`; pass.\n- REQ-003 (tree in no repository keeps its sibling): code \\`$E:469-470\\`; pass.\n- REQ-004 (LAYOUT overflow split): code \\`$E:3698-3708\\`; pass (iteration 2).\n- REQ-005 (remove-list strict-write remedy): code \\`$E:5605-5614\\`; pass (iteration 8).\n- REQ-006 (both LAYOUT remedies in both docs): pass, with the generic next-step rows still unexcepted (R2-P2-001).\n- REQ-007 (layoutMoves, overlayOutside, writeBackup read as the code behaves): pass.\n- REQ-008 (002 pointers, 005 AC rows, 004 close-out): pass for 002 and 005 (iteration 4).\n- Comment hygiene: no added comment line in 3aab896957e carries a finding id, REQ or task id, phase number or spec path.\n\n## Maintainability Pass\n\n- rollbackRelayout keeps undo order (links, manifest, moves, created folders) in one function with one \\`attempt\\` wrapper (\\`$E:6420-6444\\`); the done record names each step it can undo. Clear and cheap to extend.\n- relayoutWithFailingRename (\\`$TF:1178-1191\\`) is the right seam for the missing restore-failed test (R1-P2-002): it already counts rename calls.\n- The three Barter hooks each carry their own overlaysRootFor; phase 007 records why (bash, CommonJS and ESM with no shared module). Not raised.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- spec_code: pass for REQ-001..REQ-008 as listed.\n- checklist_evidence: partial. The test suite backs every REQ, but the hook-environment coverage stops at status (finding 1).\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- \\`$E:4652\\` calls relativeKey only for its throw on an escaping path and discards the value. It predates the remediation (a context line in 3aab896957e) and has no comment saying so; noted, not raised.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- Comment hygiene of the remediation diff; rollback structure; REQ coverage.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Ephemeral ids in the remediation's code comments: none found.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: traceability\n- Focus area: frontier node F-1-003 (docs), with maintainability in the same pass\n- Reason: registry rotation; close each node's remaining dimensions inside the depth-1 budget\n- Rotation status: F-1-001 all four dimensions done\n- Required evidence: doc pointers (file:line) in overlays.md and the presentation contract\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\nEOF\ncat > $L/prompts/spec-009.json <<EOF\n{\"iteration\":9,\"node\":\"F-1-001\",\"dimension\":\"traceability\",\"scope\":[\"$E\",\"$TS\",\"$TF\"],\"priorWeighted\":15,\n\"filesReviewed\":[\"$TS:858\",\"$S/006-review-remediation/spec.md:128\",\"$E:6420\",\"$TF:1178\",\"$E:4652\"],\n\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"R9-P2-001\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"title\":\"The hook GIT_DIR test checks status's repository test, never pre-commit's ownership check\",\"file\":\"$TS:858\",\"findingClass\":\"test-gap\",\"refines\":\"R5-P1-001\"}],\n\"traceability\":[{\"protocolId\":\"spec_code\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"gateClass\":\"hard\",\"applicable\":true,\"evidence\":[\"$S/006-review-remediation/spec.md:128\",\"$E:6512\"],\"summary\":\"006 REQ-001..008 trace to code and tests\"},{\"protocolId\":\"checklist_evidence\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"gateClass\":\"hard\",\"applicable\":true,\"evidence\":[\"$TS:868\"],\"summary\":\"hook-environment coverage stops at status\"}],\n\"novelty\":\"One P2 test gap refining R5-P1-001; REQ trace and maintainability pass clean.\",\n\"ledger\":[{\"bugClass\":\"test_coverage\",\"targetRefs\":[\"$TS\"],\"hypothesis\":\"no test runs pre-commit under a hook GIT_DIR\",\"result\":\"only status runs under GIT_DIR\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"$TS:868\"],\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"linkedFindingId\":\"R9-P2-001\"},\n{\"bugClass\":\"comment_hygiene\",\"targetRefs\":[\"$E\"],\"hypothesis\":\"remediation comments carry ephemeral ids\",\"result\":\"none in added comment lines\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"$E:6413\"],\"disposition\":\"ruled_out\"}],\n\"ruledOut\":[{\"direction\":\"ephemeral ids in remediation comments\",\"reason\":\"grep of added comment lines found none\"}]}\nEOF\nnode -e 'const f=process.argv[1];const s=JSON.parse(require(\"fs\").readFileSync(f));s.dimensionsOverride=[\"traceability\",\"maintainability\"];require(\"fs\").writeFileSync(f,JSON.stringify(s))' $L/prompts/spec-009.json; sed -i '' 's/dimensions:\\[s.dimension\\]/dimensions:s.dimensionsOverride||[s.dimension]/; s/focus:`Frontier node ${s.node}: ${s.dimension}`/focus:`Frontier node ${s.node}: ${(s.dimensionsOverride||[s.dimension]).join(\" and \")}`/' $L/prompts/emit.cjs; grep -c dimensionsOverride $L/prompts/emit.cjs; node $L/prompts/emit.cjs $L/prompts/spec-009.json $L 2026-11-20T17:10:00Z 2>&1 | cut -c1-60; node $L/prompts/graph.cjs $L 9 | cut -c1-60; node $L/prompts/conv.cjs $L 9 3 3; node -e 'const r=JSON.parse(require(\"fs\").readFileSync(process.argv[1]));for(const n of (r.frontier.nodes||[]))console.log(n.nodeId,n.status,n.nextDimension)' $L/deep-review-findings-registry.json","description":"Write, record, graph and converge iteration 9"}}}
