{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CjsGSLyYUh8C6QJ7ErhTVU","type":"tool_result","content":"28:  invariant: \"This route prints and never writes. It runs the engine's status mode only, never apply, apply --capture or apply --relayout, and status takes no lock. The verify steps status starts are the read-only check modes the overlay manifest names. A repair is an explicit action the operator runs through /doctor:overlay apply, apply --capture or apply --relayout.\"\n56:    - \"After those lines the engine prints its state counts, one MISS line per failed check, one STALE line per root file upstream changed under a repin.rootFiles overlay, one LAYOUT line per overlay source kept off its layout path, one NOTE line per note, its checked line and RESULT: PASSED or RESULT: FAILED. Keep every line as printed, because the counts and the fix text are the engine's answ\n58:    - \"A STALE line fails the status and a LAYOUT line does not: a stale root file is outstanding work, while an off-layout source still applies. Show both with the engine's own fix, and name /doctor:overlay apply --relayout beside each LAYOUT line. A NOTE line never fails the status: it names a check the run skipped, a value no record covers, an operation whose path names an array item by posi\n68:  STATUS=FINDINGS when the engine exits 1. Show each line not in sync first with its fix, then each MISS line, then each STALE, LAYOUT, NOTE and AUDIT line, then the DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT summary.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"faa6b93c-ce84-436d-8875-372fa8efb878","uuid":"b65c3947-2821-4206-bc87-3ea4985d31a6","timestamp":"2026-11-20T16:58:40.981Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"28:  invariant: \"This route prints and never writes. It runs the engine's status mode only, never apply, apply --capture or apply --relayout, and status takes no lock. The verify steps status starts are the read-only check modes the overlay manifest names. A repair is