{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017nyoSkUPsCKcmA9T2wJddK","type":"tool_result","content":"### Follow-up: review remediation\n\nThe extended deep review of the layout change raised six ai-speckit findings. Its report is the Skilled packet's `review/review-report.md`. Each finding held when checked against the code, and each is fixed in one local commit above `ad3246feba2`, together with this record.\n\n| Finding | Fix | Proof |\n|---------|-----|-------|\n| The commit gate skipped every overlay check silently when no manifest was found | The gate refuses with exit 1 when a vendored path is staged, and names the manifest path it looked for. Otherwise it prints `overlay checks skipped: no overlay manifest at <path>` and exits 0 | `pre-commit.test.cjs`: the visible skip, the refusal and lookup success |\n| No test covered that branch | New `overlays/root/opencode/scripts/git-hooks/tests/pre-commit.test.cjs`, adopted into the manifest | 6 of 6 |\n| The edit guard core, the commit gate and the git-write gate each hard-coded `overlays` beside the tree | Each reads `overlayDir` from `skilled/.skilled-overlays.json`, with `../overlays` as the fallback, and keeps its fail-open or fail-closed posture | One `\"../ovl\"` case in each hook's tests |\n| The plugin tests used only a stub bridge | One case imports the applied plugin beside the real vendored `v2-bridge.js` | Fails when `definePlugin` is renamed in the live bridge, which was then restored byte for byte |\n| `overlays/relayout-runs/` was not ignored | `.gitignore` and `overlays/README.md` name it beside `repin-runs/` | Diff |\n| A temp fixture folder was still named `barter-overlays` | Renamed to `overlays` | `compiled-routing-byte-parity.test.cjs` 5 of 5 |\n| The overlay-first rule quoted `overlays/...` where the guard prints `../overlays/...` | The rule's guard and status examples quote `../overlays/...` | Matches `--guard` output from `skilled/` |\n\n## Known Limitations\n\n1. **`/doctor:update record-base` did not record.** The engine resolves the pin against ai-speckit, whose framework sits under `skilled/`; `base.json` is unchanged.\n2. **`npm ci` in `.opencode` is still to run.** Upstream changed its lockfile, and an install waits for the operator.\n3. **Eleven overlay tests fail as before this phase.** They import modules that exist only at the destination.\n4. **Engine gaps.** The relayout cannot move nested sources in one run, and it leaves a folder only a layout link reaches.\n5. **Doc wording, fixed by the review remediation.** The rule file now quotes `../overlays/framework/...`, the path the guard prints from `skilled/`.\n6. **One old-name hit stays.** The vendored upstream test `overlay-engine-fixes.test.cjs` uses `barter-overlays` on purpose, as a custom setting value. It is an upstream engine file, so ai-speckit does not change it.\n7. **Left open by the re-pin onto `b5a630c`.**\n   - Upstream's root `.gitignore` line `!specs/**/orchestration-status.log` was not carried, because it would change what every developer track tracks.\n   - The vibe mirrors miss 14 Barter skill links and 1 prompt. That gap predates this re-pin, because the runbook does not run the vibe syncs.\n   - One `executor-config.vitest.ts` case fails on Barter's Pi default with inputs identical to `HEAD`.\n   - The `git-setup-check` `hooks` row fails by design, against Barter's own `core.hooksPath`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:limitations -->\n\n---","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"faa6b93c-ce84-436d-8875-372fa8efb878","uuid":"a969d7f2-24f5-4982-9374-02440f65f351","timestamp":"2026-11-20T16:59:25.779Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### Follow-up: review remediation\n\nThe extended deep review of the layout change raised six ai-speckit findings. Its report is the Skilled packet's `review/review-report.md`. Each finding held when checked against the code, and each is fixed in one local commit above `ad3246feba2`, together with this record.\n\n| Finding | Fix | Proof |\n|---------|-----|-------|\n| The commit gate skipped every overlay check silently when no manifest was found | The gate refuses with exit 1 when a vendored path is staged, and names the manifest path it looked for. Otherwise it prints `overlay checks skipped: no overlay manifest at <path>` and exits 0 | `pre-commit.test.cjs`: the visible skip, the refusal and lookup success |\n| No test covered that branch | New `overlays/root/opencode/scripts/git-hooks/tests/pre-commit.test.cjs`, adopted into the manifest | 6 of 6 |\n| The edit guard core, the commit gate and the git-write gate each hard-coded `overlays` beside the tree | Each reads `overlayDir` from `skilled/.skilled-overlays.json`, with `../overlays` as the fallback, and keeps its fail-open or fail-closed posture | One `\"../ovl\"` case in each hook's tests |\n| The plugin tests used only a stub bridge | One case imports the applied plugin beside the real vendored `v2-bridge.js` | Fails when `definePlugin` is renamed in the live bridge, which was then restored byte for byte |\n| `overlays/relayout-runs/` was not ignored | `.gitignore` and `overlays/README.md` name it beside `repin-runs/` | Diff |\n| A temp fixture folder was still named `barter-overlays` | Renamed to `overlays` | `compiled-routing-byte-parity.test.cjs` 5 of 5 |\n| The overlay-first rule quoted `overlays/...` where the guard prints `../overlays/...` | The rule's guard and status examples quote `../overlays/...` | Matches `--guard` output from `skilled/` |\n\n## Known Limitations\n\n1. **`/doctor:update record-base` did not record.** The engine resolves the pin against ai-speckit, whose framework sits under `skilled/`; `base.json` is unchanged.\n2. **`npm ci` in `.opencode` is still to run.** Upstream changed its lockfile, and an install waits for the operator.\n3. **Eleven overlay tests fail as before this phase.** They import modules that exist only at the destination.\n4. **Engine gaps.** The relayout cannot move nested sources in one run, and it leaves a folder only a layout link reaches.\n5. **Doc wording, fixed by the review remediation.** The rule file now quotes `../overlays/framework/...`, the path the guard prints from `skilled/`.\n6. **One old-name hit stays.** The vendored upstream test `overlay-engine-fixes.test.cjs` uses `barter-overlays` on purpose, as a custom setting value. It is an upstream engine file, so ai-speckit does not change it.\n7. **Left open by the re-pin onto `b5a630c`.**\n   - Upstream's root `.gitignore` line `!specs/**/orchestration-status.log` was not carried, because it would change what every developer track tracks.\n   - The vibe mirrors miss 14 Barter skill links and 1 prompt. That gap predates this re-pin, because the runbook does not run the vibe syncs.\n   - One `executor-config.vitest.ts` case fails on Barter's Pi default with inputs identical to `HEAD`.\n   - The `git-setup-check` `hooks` row fails by design, against Barter's own `core.hooksPath`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:limitations -->\n\n---","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017nyoSkUPsCKcmA9T2wJddK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
