{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChEY4iPSxxSuXi2q3rwzV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NUShuVcR9zkfF2SJZS7G5Z","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled; L=specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/opus-medium; R=barter/ai-speckit/specs/skilled-barter-overlays/002-spec-tracks-restructure/039-overlays-framework-root-layout/implementation-summary.md; B=barter/ai-speckit/overlays; H=$B/root/opencode/scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit; G=$B/framework/hooks/barter-overlay-guard/lib/barter-overlay-guard-core.cjs; W=$B/framework/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/barter-git-write-gate.mjs; cat > $L/iterations/iteration-011.md <<EOF\n# Iteration 011 - Frontier node F-1-005: traceability and maintainability\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Lineage: opus-medium, session fanout-opus-medium-1795192401900-xpt66n\n- Node: F-1-005 (Barter, read-only nested repo), dimensions traceability (registry next) and maintainability, each with its own pass.\n- Review focus addressed: checked ai-speckit's own record of the remediation (039 implementation-summary, recorded in e63bd038a5d) row by row against commit 5dd004f3faa and the tests it names, and judged the cost of the three hooks' duplicated lookup.\n- Sources: steer.md absent; strategy; registry frontier (F-1-005 next traceability).\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- \\`$R:76-89\\` (remediation table), \\`$R:90-100\\` (re-pin follow-up), \\`$R:154-175\\` (Known Limitations)\n- \\`git show --stat e63bd038a5d\\` (5 record files) and \\`git show --stat 5dd004f3faa\\` (26 files)\n- \\`$H:83-110\\`, \\`$G:53-75\\`, \\`$W:177-189\\` (three copies of the overlayDir lookup)\n\n## Findings by Severity\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. R5-P1-001 (Skilled engine) stays active; the 039 record does not mention commits from a linked worktree, which is consistent with it not knowing of the gap.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n## Traceability Pass\n\n| 039 row | Code or test | Result |\n|---------|--------------|--------|\n| Commit gate fails closed without a manifest | \\`$H:120-146\\`; pre-commit.test.cjs \"refuses a staged vendored change when no manifest exists\" (6 of 6, iteration 4) | pass |\n| New pre-commit test adopted into the manifest | 5dd004f3faa touches overlay-manifest.json (+7) and adds pre-commit.test.cjs | pass |\n| Three hooks read overlayDir, one \"../ovl\" case each | \\`$H:93-107\\`, \\`$G:60-71\\`, \\`$W:177-187\\`; guard-core test +10, gate test +14, pre-commit \"honours a different overlayDir setting\" | pass |\n| Plugin case on the real bridge | barter-overlay-guard.test.cjs real-bridge case (3 of 3, iteration 7) | pass |\n| relayout-runs ignored and documented | .gitignore:69, README.md:459 | pass |\n| Fixture renamed | compiled-routing-byte-parity.test.cjs fixture now \\`overlays\\` | pass |\n| Rule quotes ../overlays | barter-overlay-first.md:48, 52 | pass |\n| Re-pin onto b5a630c, numbers equal baseline | live rerun at iteration 8: in-sync=488, 136/136, RESULT: PASSED, allow | pass |\n\n- Known Limitation 6 records the vendored \\`barter-overlays\\` test value as deliberate; R3-P2-001 therefore disputes a recorded decision rather than reporting an oversight.\n\n## Maintainability Pass\n\n- The overlayDir lookup exists three times (bash with inline node, CommonJS, ESM). Each is about ten lines, each falls back to \\`../overlays\\` on an absent or unparsable setting, and the engine stays the validator. Phase 007 records the reason (no shared module across the three runtimes). The copies agree today; the cost of a fourth runtime is one more copy. Not raised.\n- The commit hook's inline node block (\\`$H:93-107\\`) is the least testable copy, and pre-commit.test.cjs covers it end to end, including the unparsable-setting fallback.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- spec_code: pass, every 039 remediation row traced to code or a rerun test.\n- checklist_evidence: pass for the 039 verification rows this lineage reran.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The hooks fall back to \\`../overlays\\` while the engine falls back to \\`skilled-overlays\\` with no setting file (iteration 3). Barter always ships the setting, and the commit gate fails closed either way.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- 039 remediation table, re-pin numbers, limitations list.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A 039 claim with no evidence behind it: none found.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: security\n- Focus area: frontier node F-1-007 (records), with maintainability in the same pass\n- Reason: last node with uncovered dimensions\n- Rotation status: F-1-001, F-1-003, F-1-005 all dimensions done\n- Required evidence: whether the records expose secrets or credentials (008 push credential override), and record maintainability\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\nEOF\ncat > $L/prompts/spec-011.json <<EOF\n{\"iteration\":11,\"node\":\"F-1-005\",\"dimension\":\"traceability\",\"dimensionsOverride\":[\"traceability\",\"maintainability\"],\"scope\":[\"$R\",\"$H\",\"$G\",\"$W\"],\"priorWeighted\":17,\n\"filesReviewed\":[\"$R:80\",\"$R:160\",\"$H:93\",\"$G:60\",\"$W:177\"],\n\"findings\":[],\n\"traceability\":[{\"protocolId\":\"spec_code\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"gateClass\":\"hard\",\"applicable\":true,\"evidence\":[\"$R:80\",\"$H:120\"],\"summary\":\"every 039 remediation row traces to code or a rerun test\"},{\"protocolId\":\"checklist_evidence\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"gateClass\":\"hard\",\"applicable\":true,\"evidence\":[\"$R:147\"],\"summary\":\"039 verification rows reproduce\"}],\n\"novelty\":\"No new findings; 039 record fully traceable; hook lookup duplication judged acceptable and documented.\",\n\"ledger\":[{\"bugClass\":\"record_contradiction\",\"targetRefs\":[\"$R\"],\"hypothesis\":\"039 claims a fix the code lacks\",\"result\":\"all eight rows trace\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"$R:80\"],\"disposition\":\"ruled_out\"},\n{\"bugClass\":\"duplication\",\"targetRefs\":[\"$H\",\"$G\",\"$W\"],\"hypothesis\":\"triplicated lookup has drifted\",\"result\":\"three copies agree; reason recorded\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"$G:60\",\"$W:177\"],\"disposition\":\"ruled_out\"}],\n\"ruledOut\":[{\"direction\":\"039 record claims without evidence\",\"reason\":\"each row traced\"}]}\nEOF\nnode $L/prompts/emit.cjs $L/prompts/spec-011.json $L 2026-11-20T17:18:00Z 2>&1 | cut -c1-60; node $L/prompts/graph.cjs $L 11 | cut -c1-60; node $L/prompts/conv.cjs $L 11 3 3","description":"Write, record, graph and converge iteration 11"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1498,"cache_read_input_tokens":316237,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1498},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"faa6b93c-ce84-436d-8875-372fa8efb878","uuid":"0e71e7ef-2fe7-497d-8253-aa104b31d69d","timestamp":"2026-11-20T16:59:55.742Z","request_id":"req_011ChEY4i7bB5keNpqaKEViL","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01NUShuVcR9zkfF2SJZS7G5Z":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled; L=specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/opus-medium; R=barter/ai-speckit/specs/skilled-barter-overlays/002-spec-tracks-restructure/039-overlays-framework-root-layout/implementation-summary.md; B=barter/ai-speckit/overlays; H=$B/root/opencode/scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit; G=$B/framework/hooks/barter-overlay-guard/lib/barter-overlay-guard-core.cjs; W=$B/framework/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/barter-git-write-gate.mjs; cat > $L/iterations/iteration-011.md <<EOF\n# Iteration 011 - Frontier node F-1-005: traceability and maintainability\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Lineage: opus-medium, session fanout-opus-medium-1795192401900-xpt66n\n- Node: F-1-005 (Barter, read-only nested repo), dimensions traceability (registry next) and maintainability, each with its own pass.\n- Review focus addressed: checked ai-speckit's own record of the remediation (039 implementation-summary, recorded in e63bd038a5d) row by row against commit 5dd004f3faa and the tests it names, and judged the cost of the three hooks' duplicated lookup.\n- Sources: steer.md absent; strategy; registry frontier (F-1-005 next traceability).\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- \\`$R:76-89\\` (remediation table), \\`$R:90-100\\` (re-pin follow-up), \\`$R:154-175\\` (Known Limitations)\n- \\`git show --stat e63bd038a5d\\` (5 record files) and \\`git show --stat 5dd004f3faa\\` (26 files)\n- \\`$H:83-110\\`, \\`$G:53-75\\`, \\`$W:177-189\\` (three copies of the overlayDir lookup)\n\n## Findings by Severity\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. R5-P1-001 (Skilled engine) stays active; the 039 record does not mention commits from a linked worktree, which is consistent with it not knowing of the gap.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n## Traceability Pass\n\n| 039 row | Code or test | Result |\n|---------|--------------|--------|\n| Commit gate fails closed without a manifest | \\`$H:120-146\\`; pre-commit.test.cjs \"refuses a staged vendored change when no manifest exists\" (6 of 6, iteration 4) | pass |\n| New pre-commit test adopted into the manifest | 5dd004f3faa touches overlay-manifest.json (+7) and adds pre-commit.test.cjs | pass |\n| Three hooks read overlayDir, one \"../ovl\" case each | \\`$H:93-107\\`, \\`$G:60-71\\`, \\`$W:177-187\\`; guard-core test +10, gate test +14, pre-commit \"honours a different overlayDir setting\" | pass |\n| Plugin case on the real bridge | barter-overlay-guard.test.cjs real-bridge case (3 of 3, iteration 7) | pass |\n| relayout-runs ignored and documented | .gitignore:69, README.md:459 | pass |\n| Fixture renamed | compiled-routing-byte-parity.test.cjs fixture now \\`overlays\\` | pass |\n| Rule quotes ../overlays | barter-overlay-first.md:48, 52 | pass |\n| Re-pin onto b5a630c, numbers equal baseline | live rerun at iteration 8: in-sync=488, 136/136, RESULT: PASSED, allow | pass |\n\n- Known Limitation 6 records the vendored \\`barter-overlays\\` test value as deliberate; R3-P2-001 therefore disputes a recorded decision rather than reporting an oversight.\n\n## Maintainability Pass\n\n- The overlayDir lookup exists three times (bash with inline node, CommonJS, ESM). Each is about ten lines, each falls back to \\`../overlays\\` on an absent or unparsable setting, and the engine stays the validator. Phase 007 records the reason (no shared module across the three runtimes). The copies agree today; the cost of a fourth runtime is one more copy. Not raised.\n- The commit hook's inline node block (\\`$H:93-107\\`) is the least testable copy, and pre-commit.test.cjs covers it end to end, including the unparsable-setting fallback.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- spec_code: pass, every 039 remediation row traced to code or a rerun test.\n- checklist_evidence: pass for the 039 verification rows this lineage reran.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The hooks fall back to \\`../overlays\\` while the engine falls back to \\`skilled-overlays\\` with no setting file (iteration 3). Barter always ships the setting, and the commit gate fails closed either way.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- 039 remediation table, re-pin numbers, limitations list.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A 039 claim with no evidence behind it: none found.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: security\n- Focus area: frontier node F-1-007 (records), with maintainability in the same pass\n- Reason: last node with uncovered dimensions\n- Rotation status: F-1-001, F-1-003, F-1-005 all dimensions done\n- Required evidence: whether the records expose secrets or credentials (008 push credential override), and record maintainability\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\nEOF\ncat > $L/prompts/spec-011.json <<EOF\n{\"iteration\":11,\"node\":\"F-1-005\",\"dimension\":\"traceability\",\"dimensionsOverride\":[\"traceability\",\"maintainability\"],\"scope\":[\"$R\",\"$H\",\"$G\",\"$W\"],\"priorWeighted\":17,\n\"filesReviewed\":[\"$R:80\",\"$R:160\",\"$H:93\",\"$G:60\",\"$W:177\"],\n\"findings\":[],\n\"traceability\":[{\"protocolId\":\"spec_code\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"gateClass\":\"hard\",\"applicable\":true,\"evidence\":[\"$R:80\",\"$H:120\"],\"summary\":\"every 039 remediation row traces to code or a rerun test\"},{\"protocolId\":\"checklist_evidence\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"gateClass\":\"hard\",\"applicable\":true,\"evidence\":[\"$R:147\"],\"summary\":\"039 verification rows reproduce\"}],\n\"novelty\":\"No new findings; 039 record fully traceable; hook lookup duplication judged acceptable and documented.\",\n\"ledger\":[{\"bugClass\":\"record_contradiction\",\"targetRefs\":[\"$R\"],\"hypothesis\":\"039 claims a fix the code lacks\",\"result\":\"all eight rows trace\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"$R:80\"],\"disposition\":\"ruled_out\"},\n{\"bugClass\":\"duplication\",\"targetRefs\":[\"$H\",\"$G\",\"$W\"],\"hypothesis\":\"triplicated lookup has drifted\",\"result\":\"three copies agree; reason recorded\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"$G:60\",\"$W:177\"],\"disposition\":\"ruled_out\"}],\n\"ruledOut\":[{\"direction\":\"039 record claims without evidence\",\"reason\":\"each row traced\"}]}\nEOF\nnode $L/prompts/emit.cjs $L/prompts/spec-011.json $L 2026-11-20T17:18:00Z 2>&1 | cut -c1-60; node $L/prompts/graph.cjs $L 11 | cut -c1-60; node $L/prompts/conv.cjs $L 11 3 3","description":"Write, record, graph and converge iteration 11"}}}
