{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChEYN23ZXfnzkP5BNeBxp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019TtDQPHkdgccDccUMJzRJU","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled; L=specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/opus-medium; E=.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs; A=.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-overlay-apply.yaml; cat > $L/iterations/iteration-014.md <<EOF\n# Iteration 014 - Recovery: severity escalation and function-level pass (maintainability, correctness)\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Lineage: opus-medium, session fanout-opus-medium-1795192401900-xpt66n\n- Trigger: STUCK_RECOVERY after iteration 13 (stuck=3). A deep_review.recovery_started event was recorded through the gateway before this iteration (strategy escalate-severity-review, target dimension maintainability, the least-passed dimension tied with security and traceability).\n- Recovery strategies used: (1) escalate severity review, re-reading every active P2 for a P1 case; (2) change granularity, function by function through relayoutUnderLock's code outside its guarded block.\n- Review focus addressed: rollback correctness and error contract at the edges of the relayout run.\n- Sources: steer.md absent; strategy; conv-013 stop decision.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- \\`$E:6490-6508\\` (backup copy before the guarded block), \\`$E:6552-6558\\` (prune after it), \\`$E:4705-4710\\` (pruneEmptyParents)\n- \\`$E:6636-6667\\` (main: a thrown error prints \"[overlay-engine] <message>\" and returns exit 2)\n- \\`$A:111-117\\` (relayout exit handling)\n- Every active P2 in the registry (escalation pass)\n\n## Findings by Severity\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. Escalation pass: no active P2 has a case that reaches a P1 impact. R1-P2-001 needs an operator to delete the moved folder after a double failure; R5-P2-001 needs the operator to plant the link; the record and doc findings misinform but break nothing. All stay P2.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **A relayout that fails outside its guarded block exits 2 with a raw engine error the apply workflow has no rule for, and the prune case reports failure for a relayout that completed** -- $E:6554 -- The guarded block covers the moves, the manifest write and the relinks (\\`$E:6514-6550\\`). The backup copies run before it (\\`$E:6501-6504\\`) and the empty-folder prune runs after it (\\`$E:6554\\`); the comment says pruning happens \"once nothing can fail\", but pruneEmptyParents calls rmdirSync (\\`$E:4708\\`), which can throw. Either throw reaches main's catch and prints \"[overlay-engine] <message>\" with exit 2 (\\`$E:6661-6665\\`). After a prune failure every copy has moved and the manifest names the new paths, yet the run never prints its moved count or \"run ... apply\", and exits as a failure. A backup-copy failure leaves a partial relayout-runs/<stamp> folder behind. The apply workflow's exit-2 rules (\\`$A:114-116\\`) cover refuse lines and \"error: relayout failed while\" lines only, so it has no reading for either case, and it does not run the apply that rewrites destinations.\n   - Finding class: error-contract-gap\n   - Scope proof: the two unguarded write steps of relayoutUnderLock; every other write is inside the try.\n   - Affected surface hints: relayoutUnderLock prune and backup steps; doctor-overlay-apply.yaml relayout exit-2 rules; references/overlays.md relayout failure paragraph.\n   - Case: relayout moves custom/place.md, writes the manifest, then rmdirSync on the emptied custom/ folder fails with EACCES; the engine prints \"[overlay-engine] EACCES ...\" and exits 2 although the move and manifest write are done.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- spec_code: partial. Phase 006 REQ-001 covers failures of a move, the manifest write or a relink; the two unguarded steps are outside its words but inside its intent (\"leave no half-moved overlay folder\").\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Process slip: the recovery_started event belonged after iteration 12's STUCK_RECOVERY decision and was recorded only after iteration 13's. Iteration 13 therefore ran as a recovery iteration without its event. The ledger now carries the event, and this iteration is the first after it.\n- A prune failure leaves a consistent tree: destinations still match their old copies' bytes, so status stays in sync; the harm is the wrong exit and the missing next step, not data loss.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- pruneEmptyParents stops at the overlay root (\\`$E:4706\\`), so it never removes the folder itself.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- P2-to-P1 escalation for any active P2: no case reaches a broken tree or a bypassed gate.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: none\n- Focus area: synthesis if the stop decision allows it\n- Reason: recovery produced one new finding; all nodes answered\n- Rotation status: complete\n- Required evidence: stop decision after this iteration\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\nEOF\ncat > $L/prompts/spec-014.json <<EOF\n{\"iteration\":14,\"node\":null,\"focusOverride\":\"Recovery: severity escalation and function-level pass on relayoutUnderLock\",\"dimension\":\"maintainability\",\"dimensionsOverride\":[\"maintainability\",\"correctness\"],\"scope\":[\"$E\",\"$A\"],\"priorWeighted\":17,\n\"filesReviewed\":[\"$E:6554\",\"$E:6501\",\"$E:4708\",\"$E:6661\",\"$A:114\"],\n\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"R14-P2-001\",\"severity\":\"P2\",\"title\":\"A relayout that fails outside its guarded block exits 2 with a raw engine error the apply workflow has no rule for\",\"file\":\"$E:6554\",\"findingClass\":\"error-contract-gap\"}],\n\"traceability\":[{\"protocolId\":\"spec_code\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"gateClass\":\"hard\",\"applicable\":true,\"evidence\":[\"$E:6554\",\"$A:116\"],\"summary\":\"two unguarded relayout steps sit outside REQ-001's words\"}],\n\"novelty\":\"Recovery iteration: one new P2 from a function-level pass; escalation found no P2 that reaches P1.\",\n\"ledger\":[{\"bugClass\":\"error_contract\",\"targetRefs\":[\"$E\"],\"hypothesis\":\"a step outside the guarded block can fail with an unhandled error\",\"result\":\"backup copy and prune throw to main's catch\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"$E:6554\",\"$E:6661\"],\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"linkedFindingId\":\"R14-P2-001\"},\n{\"bugClass\":\"severity_escalation\",\"targetRefs\":[\"$E\"],\"hypothesis\":\"an active P2 has a P1 case\",\"result\":\"none reaches a broken tree or bypassed gate\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"$E:6534\"],\"disposition\":\"ruled_out\"}],\n\"ruledOut\":[{\"direction\":\"P2 to P1 escalation\",\"reason\":\"no active P2 reaches a P1 impact\"}]}\nEOF\nnode $L/prompts/emit.cjs $L/prompts/spec-014.json $L 2026-11-20T17:30:00Z 2>&1 | cut -c1-60; node $L/prompts/graph.cjs $L 14 | cut -c1-60; node $L/prompts/conv.cjs $L 14 3 3","description":"Write, record, graph and converge iteration 14"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":335,"cache_read_input_tokens":347150,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":335},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"faa6b93c-ce84-436d-8875-372fa8efb878","uuid":"eb15c1f2-0a3d-4e49-8fc1-8443a0a63b39","timestamp":"2026-11-20T17:03:50.668Z","request_id":"req_011ChEYN1nBvLgSgp1grfPFW","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_019TtDQPHkdgccDccUMJzRJU":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled; L=specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/opus-medium; E=.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs; A=.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-overlay-apply.yaml; cat > $L/iterations/iteration-014.md <<EOF\n# Iteration 014 - Recovery: severity 