{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChEYUh2m1otkkpEaxmg3m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019H1Un1WvoEUXPWL5HzARpr","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled; L=specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/opus-medium; E=.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/overlay-engine.cjs; H=barter/ai-speckit/overlays/root/opencode/scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit; TS=.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/overlay-engine-strict-writes.test.cjs; P=.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-overlay-presentation.txt; SY=.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-overlay-status.yaml; O=.skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/references/overlays.md; S=specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout; cat > $L/iterations/iteration-015.md <<EOF\n# Iteration 015 - Recovery: traceability protocol replay and registry repair (traceability)\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Lineage: opus-medium, session fanout-opus-medium-1795192401900-xpt66n\n- Trigger: the stop check after iteration 14 returned BLOCKED on dimensionCoverageGate because core protocol spec_code was last recorded as partial, which the gate reads as unfinished. Recovery strategy \"Traceability protocol replay: re-run unresolved core checks\" applies.\n- Second trigger, found while preparing this replay: the reducer folds a refinement into its target and takes the refinement's severity and title. Iteration 9's R9-P2-001 (a P2 test gap with refines R5-P1-001) therefore lowered R5-P1-001 to P2 in the registry and replaced its title. Iteration 10's R10-P2-001 and iteration 2's R2-P2-002 likewise replaced the titles of R2-P2-001 and R1-P2-001. Nothing in the evidence changed; the severity drop is a recording error by this lineage.\n- Review focus addressed: consolidate the two core protocols over the whole packet and restore the registry to the evidence.\n- Sources: steer.md absent; strategy; registry; conv-014 stop decision.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- Registry open findings (11 entries) against iterations 1-14\n- \\`$E:5864\\`, \\`$H:164\\`, \\`$TS:858-872\\` (re-read for the P1 restatement)\n- \\`$P:563, 595\\`, \\`$SY:58\\`, \\`$E:6534\\`, \\`$O:96\\` (re-read for the two P2 restatements)\n\n## Findings by Severity\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\n1. **The engine's commit check allows every unowned vendored change when git runs it from a hook in a linked worktree, and no test runs pre-commit under that environment** -- $E:5864 -- Restates R5-P1-001 at its adjudicated severity, folding in R9-P2-001's test gap. stagedUnownedChanges probes the top level with the hook's GIT_DIR (\\`$E:5864\\` through runGit), which in a linked worktree reports the tree subfolder as the top level, so no staged name matches a vendored key and the check prints allow. Reproduced at iteration 5 (exit 1 refuse without GIT_DIR, exit 0 allow with it), status also passes under it (iteration 6), and worktrees are a documented ai-speckit workspace with a shared core.hooksPath (iteration 13). The only hook-environment test runs status, never pre-commit (\\`$TS:858-872\\`).\n   - Finding class: fail-open-gate (refines R5-P1-001; restores its severity)\n   - Scope proof: stagedUnownedChanges is the commit path's only hook-environment top-level probe; trackedTreeKeys shares the pattern on the status path.\n   - Affected surface hints: overlay-engine.cjs stagedUnownedChanges and trackedTreeKeys; Barter pre-commit hook; strict-writes hook-environment test; 006 Known Limitation 1.\n   - Case: in a linked worktree of ai-speckit, stage an edit to skilled/.skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md that no overlay owns and run git commit; the hook prints allow and the commit lands.\n\n\\`\\`\\`json\n{\"type\":\"fail-open-gate\",\"claim\":\"Under a hook-exported GIT_DIR, overlay-engine pre-commit returns allow for a staged unowned vendored change in a tree below the git top level, and no