paragraph; apply YAML line 116.\n   - Case: a moved folder holding assets/api-token.js, a failed relink and a failed restore; the operator restores from a backup without the token file.\n\n## Traceability Protocol Replay\n\n- spec_code: fail (terminal). Run across all four nodes (iterations 1-14). Engine behavior matches phase 006 REQ-001..REQ-008 and the 007 and 039 records, and the docs quote the engine's lines exactly, but four doc-code mismatches stay active: R2-P2-001 (\\`$P:563\\`, \\`$SY:58\\`), R6-P2-001 (\\`$P:560\\`), R1-P2-001 (\\`$O:96\\`) and R14-P2-001 (\\`$E:6554\\` against the apply workflow).\n- checklist_evidence: fail (terminal). Test counts, push, pin and status numbers all reproduce (iterations 4, 8), but two record lines contradict git or each other: R4-P2-001 (\\`$S/008-push-and-repin/implementation-summary.md:115\\`) and R4-P2-002 (\\`$S/007-barter-review-fixes/implementation-summary.md:91\\`).\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- spec_code: fail, as above.\n- checklist_evidence: fail, as above.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Recording lesson for the synthesis: a refines row must carry the target's severity, or it rewrites the target's severity in the registry.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- None new.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A real change in R5-P1-001's evidence between iterations 5 and 9: none; the drop was a recording artifact.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: none\n- Focus area: synthesis if the stop decision allows it\n- Reason: core protocols terminal, registry repaired, frontier answered\n- Rotation status: complete\n- Required evidence: stop decision after this iteration\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\nEOF\npython3 - $L/prompts/spec-015.json \"$E\" \"$H\" \"$TS\" \"$P\" \"$SY\" \"$O\" \"$S\" <<'PY'\nimport json,sys\np,E,H,TS,P,SY,O,S=sys.argv[1:]\nclaim={\"type\":\"fail-open-gate\",\"claim\":\"Under a hook-exported GIT_DIR, overlay-engine pre-commit returns allow for a staged unowned vendored change in a tree below the git top level, and no test co