 \"injected rename failure\", \"injected link failure\"), because the pre-fix engine has no rollback\n- Same three tests against the current engine: pass (iteration 1, 19 of 19 relayout tests)\n- \\`$E:5864\\`, \\`$H:164\\`, \\`$TS:858-872\\` (unchanged since iteration 15)\n\n## Findings by Severity\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\n1. **The engine's commit check allows every unowned vendored change when git runs it from a hook in a linked worktree, and no test runs pre-commit under that environment** -- $E:5864 -- Re-records iteration 15's restatement of R5-P1-001 at its adjudicated P1, now in a delta row the reducer reads. Evidence unchanged: reproduced allow under GIT_DIR (iteration 5), status passes under it (iteration 6), worktrees are a documented ai-speckit workspace with a shared core.hooksPath (iteration 13), and the only hook-environment test runs status, not pre-commit (\\`$TS:858-872\\`).\n   - Finding class: fail-open-gate (refines R5-P1-001; restores its severity)\n   - Scope proof: stagedUnownedChanges is the commit path's only hook-environment top-level probe.\n   - Affected surface hints: overlay-engine.cjs stagedUnownedChanges and trackedTreeKeys; Barter pre-commit hook; strict-writes hook-environment test.\n   - Case: in a linked worktree of ai-speckit, stage an unowned edit under skilled/.skilled/ and run git commit; the hook prints allow and the commit lands.\n\n\\`\\`\\`json\n{\"type\":\"fail-open-gate\",\"claim\":\"Under a hook-exported GIT_DIR, overlay-engine pre-commit returns allow for a staged unowned vendored change in a tree below the git top level, and no test covers that environment for pre-commit\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"$E:5864\",\"$H:164\",\"$TS:868\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"Barter hook does not clear GIT_DIR; status also exits 0 under it; main checkout unaffected; worktrees documented in ai-speckit AGENTS.md:222\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"Unreachable only if ai-speckit never commits from a linked worktree, which its own workspace rule contradicts\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P1\",\"confidence\":0.85,\"downgradeTrigger\":\"The hook or engine clears GIT_DIR before the probe, or ai-speckit forbids commits from linked worktrees\"}\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone new.\n\n## Test-Strength Verdict\n\n- The three rollback tests added by the remediation fail on the engine before 3aab896957e and pass after it. The pre-fix failure is the injected error escaping with the first copy left moved, which is the half-move R1-P1-001 described. The tests guard the fix.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- checklist_evidence: fail (unchanged terminal result from iteration 15; this iteration adds test-strength evidence, not a new check result for the record findings).\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The pre-fix copies live in this lineage's prompts/prefix-engine/ and were run from there; node:test's fixture cleanup removed its temporary workspaces.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- Rollback tests' sensitivity to the fix.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Rollback tests that would pass without the fix.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: none\n- Focus area: synthesis if the stop decision allows it\n- Reason: every node answered, core protocols terminal, registry repaired\n- Rotation status: complete\n- Required evidence: stop decision after this iteration\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\nEOF\npython3 - $L/prompts/spec-016.json \"$E\" \"$H\" \"$TS\" \"$TF\" <<'PY'\nimport json,sys\np,E,H,TS,TF=sys.argv[1:]\nclaim={\"claimType\":\"fail-open-gate\",\"claim\":\"Under a hook-exported GIT_DIR, overlay-engine pre-commit returns allow for a staged unowned vendored change in a tree below the git top level, and no test covers that environment for pre-commit\",\"evidenceRefs\":[E+\":5864\",H+\":164\",TS+\":868\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"Barter hook does not clear GIT_DIR; status also exits 0 under it; main checkout unaffected; worktrees documented in ai-speckit AGENTS.md:222\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"Unreachable only if ai-spe