{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChEZ8Apt3xiH83zEMU37K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Xrk6SxUJLhJVU7kaR7pd5V","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled; L=specs/system-skilled-doctor/007-overlay-framework-root-layout/review/lineages/opus-medium; python3 - $L/review-report.md $L/deep-review-strategy.md <<'PY'\nimport sys\nrp,sp=sys.argv[1:]\nr=open(rp).read()\nold=\"- Stop: legal convergence after 17 iterations (`STOP`, `composite_converged`). All nine legal-stop gates passed, the graph decision was STOP_ALLOWED, and the terminal gates (evidence, scope, coverage) passed.\"\nassert old in r\nr=r.replace(old,old+\"\\n  - dimensionCoverageGate passed only after iteration 17 re-ran both core protocols (spec_code and checklist_evidence) against their own objects. That moved them from iteration 15's fail to pass with file:line evidence. The findings behind the earlier fail stay active. See section 7.\")\nold2=\"- The coverage graph and graph-convergence events started at iteration 5 (iterations 1-4 backfilled). Before that, convergence ran only after iteration 1.\"\nassert old2 in r\nr=r.replace(old2,old2+\"\"\"\n- `durationMs` is wrong for iterations 3-17. Each record's start time was typed by hand and ran ahead of the real clock, so those records carry negative durations (from -85870 down to -2025635). The real wall time from init (16:35Z) to synthesis (about 17:13Z) was about 38 minutes. The records are durable and were not rewritten.\n- Writes outside the lineage: none in the repository. The root `review/` files that changed during the run (`fanout-run.log`, `observability-events.jsonl`, `orchestration-status.log`) carry `producer: fanout-run`, which is the runner's heartbeat. The packet's `spec.md` and `graph-metadata.json` were changed at 17:56 local by a concurrent session (see Deferred Items). Scratch captures went to `/tmp`, where `rm` is banned for this lineage, so they are left there:\n  - `/tmp/opusmed-{barter-status,contract,engine-all,plugin,precommit,relayout}.txt`\n  - `/tmp/opusmed-engine-f2a.cjs`\n  - the hook-env repository `/tmp/opusmed-hookenv.Z1DF`\n  - `/tmp/opusmed-gitdir.1QPv`. node:test removed its own fixture workspaces.\"\"\")\nopen(rp,\"w\").write(r)\ns=open(sp).read()\ns=s.replace(\"- Rerunning the cited test suites and checking git ancestry turned record claims into evidence (iteration 4)\",\"\"\"- Rerunning the cited test suites and checking git ancestry turned record claims into evidence (iteration 4)\n- A temp git repository with an env-printing hook, then the strict-writes fixture run with and without GIT_DIR, reproduced R5-P1-001 end to end (iterations 5-6)\n- A posture map per hook (fail open vs fail closed) separated design choices from defects (iteration 7)\n- Running the new rollback tests against the engine before 3aab896957e proved they guard the fix: 3 of 3 fail (iteration 16)\n- Function-level reading of the code outside relayoutUnderLock's try block found R14-P2-001 during stuck recovery (iteration 14)\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"- Hook vs engine fallback mismatch looked like a fail-open but the engine call fails closed behind it (iteration 3)\",\"\"\"- Hook vs engine fallback mismatch looked like a fail-open but the engine call fails closed behind it (iteration 3)\n- A refines row whose severity differs from its target rewrites the target's severity: R9-P2-001 lowered R5-P1-001 to P2 (iteration 9, repaired at 16)\n- A claim packet merged into a delta row with a `type` key overwrote the row's `type:\"finding\"`, and the reducer skipped it (iteration 15, repaired at 16)\n- Recording core protocols as fail for doc-to-code drift blocked the stop on a gate that measures spec-to-code alignment (iteration 15, re-adjudicated at 17)\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"- Push claimed without evidence: b5a630c6efa is on origin/main (iteration 4)\",\"\"\"- Push claimed without evidence: b5a